{"abstract":"Purpose: To assess the risk of self-fulfilling prophecy from withdrawal of life-sustaining therapy (WLST) in comatose cardiac arrest patients undergoing neuroprognostication. Methods: Post-hoc multicentre study matching adults resuscitated from out-of-hospital cardiac arrests, in WLST-permitting cohorts (TTM and TTM2), and non-WLST-permitting cohorts (KORHN and ProNeCA). We matched patients in a 1:1 ratio based on a propensity score, assessing the risk of WLST due to a presumed poor neurological prognosis and criteria predictive of poor neurological outcome, as outlined in the 2021 European Resuscitation Council/European Society of Intensive Care Medicine (ERC/ESICM) guidelines. Functional outcome was compared at six months. Results: We included 1717 patients, of whom 497 (29 %) had WLST due to neurological criteria at a median of 143 h (IQR 108–177). 303 (61 %) patients with WLST retrospectively fulfilled ≥ 2 ERC/ESICM criteria predictive of poor outcome. No patients with ≥ 2 ERC/ESICM criteria had good functional outcome at six months, neither in the WLST cohort nor among the matched controls. One patient (0.3 %) with an indeterminate prognosis (≤1 ERC/ESICM criteria) had a good functional outcome in the WLST cohort versus 18–26 % of the matched controls. In exploratory weighted estimates, up to 18 % of patients with indeterminate prognosis may have survived with a good functional outcome, if WLST had not occurred. Conclusion: In patients with at least 2 ERC/ESICM criteria predictive of poor outcome, the risk of self-fulfilling prophecy from WLST was negligible. However, in patients with an indeterminate prognosis, the practice of WLST was associated with a lower likelihood of good functional outcome.","author_count":44,"contributors":["Lagebrant, Alice","Lee, Byung Kook","Youn, Chun Song","Sandroni, Claudio","Bělohlávek, Jan","Cariou, Alain","Carrai, Riccardo","Dankiewicz, Josef","Friberg, Hans","Grejs, Anders Morten","Grippo, Antonello","Hassager, Christian","Horn, Janneke","Haenggi, Matthias","Jakobsen, Janus C.","Keeble, Thomas R.","Kirkegaard, Hans","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Kuiper, Michael A.","Lee, Dong Hun","Levin, Helena","Lilja, Gisela","Lundin, Andreas","Nielsen, Niklas","Oddo, Mauro","Oh, Sang Hoon","Park, Kyu Nam","Pellis, Tommaso","Robba, Chiara","Rylander, Christian","Ryu, Seok Jin","Saxena, Manoxj","Scarpino, Maenia","Schrag, Claudia","Stammet, Pascal","Storm, Christian","Taccone, Fabio Silvio","Thomas, Matthew","Ullén, Susann","Westhall, Erik","Wise, Matt P.","Young, Paul","Cronberg, Tobias","Moseby-Knappe, Marion"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-824896"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Lagebrant, Alice"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Czechia","France","Germany","Italy","Luxembourg","Netherlands","New Zealand","Poland","Slovakia","South Korea","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["AP-HP Assistance Publique - Hopitaux de Paris","All Global Affiliations","Azienda Ospedaliera Careggi","Capital & Coast District Health Board","Cardiff University","Catholic University in Ruzomberok","Center Hospitalier de Luxembourg","Charité-Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Charles University","Chonnam National University","ETH Zürich","Fondazione Policlinico Universitario Agostino Gemelli IRCCS","Helsingborg Hospital","Kantonsspital St. Gallen, St. Gallen, Switzerland.","Lund University","Medical Centre Leeuwarden","Medical Research Institute of New Zealand","Mid and South Essex NHS Foundation Trust","Monash University","San Martino Hospital Genoa","St. George Hospital","The Catholic University of Korea Seoul St. Mary's Hospital","The George Institute for Global Health","University Hospitals Bristol and Weston NHS Foundation Trust","University Hospitals Brussels (UZB)","University of Amsterdam","University of Genoa","University of Gothenb