{"abstract":"Purpose: To explore modifications of the 2021 European Resuscitation Council/European Society of Intensive Care Medicine (ERC/ESICM) guideline algorithm for neuroprognostication after cardiac arrest to improve its prognostic accuracy. Methods: Post-hoc analysis of four prospective multicentre studies (TTM, TTM2, KORHN and ProNeCA). We raised the Glasgow Coma Scale motor (GCS-M) inclusion threshold at 72 h after cardiac arrest from the current GCS-M < 4 to GCS-M < 6 (all unconscious patients). Secondly, we included good outcome predictors (GCS-M 4–5, neuron-specific enolase < 17 µg/L, benign electroencephalography patterns ≤ 72 h post-arrest and normal magnetic resonance imaging at 72–168 h post-arrest) in the algorithm. Functional outcome was assessed dichotomously at six months, including modified Rankin Scale 0–3, Cerebral Performance Category 1–2 or Glasgow Outcome Scale 4–5 (no symptoms to moderate disability) as good outcome. Results: We analysed 3,388 patients, of whom 2,079 had GCS-M < 4 at ≥ 72 h. Of the 874 patients identified by the 2021 ERC/ESICM poor outcome criteria, 870 had poor functional outcome (specificity: 99.6% [95%CI 99.0–99.9]). Using the GCS-M < 6 threshold, 366 more patients entered the algorithm (N = 2,445). Seven more patients with poor outcomes were identified, with close to identical specificity. Good outcome predictors thereafter identified 673 patients with potential recovery, of whom 411 (61%) had a good functional outcome at six months. With the updated algorithm, the number of prognosticated patients with an indeterminate prognosis decreased from 1,205/2,079 (58%) to 891/2,445 (36%). Conclusion: Raising the GCS-M inclusion threshold and adding favourable predictors to the 2021 ERC/ESICM prognostication algorithm reduced prognostic uncertainty without increasing falsely pessimistic predictions.","author_count":42,"contributors":["Lagebrant, Alice","Sandroni, Claudio","Nolan, Jerry P.","Bělohlávek, Jan","Cariou, Alain","Carrai, Riccardo","Dankiewicz, Josef","Grejs, Anders Morten","Grippo, Antonello","Hassager, Christian","Horn, Janneke","Haenggi, Matthias","Jakobsen, Janus C.","Keeble, Thomas R.","Kirkegaard, Hans","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Kuiper, Michael A.","Lee, Byung Kook","Lee, Dong Hun","Levin, Helena","Lilja, Gisela","Lundin, Andreas","Nielsen, Niklas","Oh, Sang Hoon","Park, Kyu Nam","Pellis, Tommaso","Robba, Chiara","Rylander, Christian","Ryu, Seok Jin","Saxena, Manoxj","Scarpino, Maenia","Schrag, Claudia","Stammet, Pascal","Storm, Christian","Taccone, Fabio Silvio","Thomas, Matthew","Westhall, Erik","Wise, Matt P.","Youn, Chun Song","Young, Paul","Cronberg, Tobias","Moseby-Knappe, Marion"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-813800"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, Central","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Lagebrant, Alice"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Cuba","Czechia","France","Germany","Italy","Luxembourg","Netherlands","New Zealand","Poland","Slovakia","South Korea","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["AP-HP Assistance Publique - Hopitaux de Paris","ARU School of Medicine & MTRC","All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC","Anglia Ruskin University","Azienda Ospedaliera Careggi","Cantonal Hospital St. Gallen","Capital & Coast District Health Board","Cardiff University","Careggi University Hospital","Catholic University in Ruzomberok","Catholic University of Korea","Catholic University of the Sacred Heart","Center Hospitalier de Luxembourg","Centre Hospitalier de Luxembourg","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","Charité-Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Charles University","Chonnam National University","Chonnam National University Hospital","Chonnam National University Medical School","ETH Zürich","Fondazione Policlinico Universitario Agostino Gemelli IRCCS","Fondazione Policlinico Universitario Gemelli","Free University of Brussels","General Teaching Hospital","Graduate School of Health Economics and Management","Helsingborg Hospital","Hospital Cochin","Hôpital Universitaire de Bruxelles","Hôpital Universitaire de Bruxelles (HUB)","IRCCS Azienda Ospedaliera Universitaria San Martino IST","IRCCS Ospedale Policlinico San Martino","Kantonsspital St. Gallen","Kantonsspital St. Gallen, St. Gallen, Switzerland.","Lund University","MSE Trust","Medical Centre Leeuwarden","Medical Research Institute of New Zealand","Mid and South Essex NHS Foundation Trust","Monash University","Ospedale Santa Maria degli Angeli Pordenone","Paris-Cité University","Policlinico Universitario Agostino Gemelli","Pordenone Hospital","Royal United Hospital Bath NHS Trust","Royal United Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Royal United Hospitals Bath NHS Foundation Trust","San Martino Hospital Genoa","Skåne University Hospital","St. George Hospital","The Catholic University of Korea Seoul St. Mary's Hospital","The George Institute for Global Health","The St George Hospital","University Hospital Wales","University Hospital Zurich","University Hospital Zürich","University Hospital of Wales","University Hospitals Bristol and Weston NHS Foundation Trust","University Hospitals Brussels (UZB)","University of Amsterdam","University of Genoa","University of Gothenburg","University of Luxembourg","University of Melbourne","University of Warwick","Université Libre de Bruxelles","Uppsala University","Wellington Hospital","Wroclaw Medical University","Wrocław Medical University"],"keyword":["Cardiac arrest","Functional outcome","Good Outcome Prediction","Indeterminate Prognosis","Neurological Prognostication"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"p