{"abstract":"Multisystem inflammatory syndrome in children (MIS-C) is a severe disease that emerged during the COVID-19 pandemic. Although recognized as an immune-mediated condition, the pathogenesis remains unresolved. Furthermore, the absence of a diagnostic test can lead to delayed immunotherapy. Using state-of-the-art mass-spectrometry proteomics, assisted by artificial intelligence (AI), we aimed to identify a diagnostic signature for MIS-C and to gain insights into disease mechanisms. We identified a highly specific 4-protein diagnostic signature in children with MIS-C. Furthermore, we identified seven clusters that differed between MIS-C and controls, indicating an interplay between apolipoproteins, immune response proteins, coagulation factors, platelet function, and the complement cascade. These intricate protein patterns indicated MIS-C as an immunometabolic condition with global hypercoagulability. Our findings emphasize the potential of AI-assisted proteomics as a powerful and unbiased tool for assessing disease pathogenesis and suggesting avenues for future interventions and impact on pediatric disease trajectories through early diagnosis.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Nygaard, Ulrikka","Nielsen, Annelaura Bach","Dungu, Kia Hee Schultz","Drici, Lylia","Holm, Mette","Ottenheijm, Maud Eline","Nielsen, Allan Bybeck","Glenthøj, Jonathan Peter","Schmidt, Lisbeth Samsø","Cortes, Dina","Jørgensen, Inger Merete","Mogensen, Trine H","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Mann, Matthias","Vissing, Nadja Hawwa","Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-742128"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nygaard, Ulrikka"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proteomic profiling reveals diagnostic signatures and pathogenic insights in multisystem inflammatory syndrome in children","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-024-06370-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-742128","identifier":[{"id":"38839859","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11153518","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85195332433","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f94482a9-5e35-4b14-8ada-45e3e1408bb3","ku-959d4415-4fd0-45ed-b500-caee3a6adc5b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-81A5A0A85B889CE2BAE119F315444A29"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/395085283/s42003_024_06370_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-024-06370-8","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ulrikka","key":"nygaardulrikkapau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"43b2e239-ddc1-4676-a8db-0a0f23906813","name":"Nygaard, Ulrikka","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annelaura Bach","key":"nielsenannelaurabachpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2a42eff8-3176-4b59-8e7c-3857eb418d8b","name":"Nielsen, Annelaura Bach","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Kia Hee Schultz","key":"dungukiaheeschultzpau","last":"Dungu","name":"Dungu, Kia Hee Schultz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lylia","key":"dricilyliapau","last":"Drici","locid":"8a587646-4df0-4392-b736-b67dfa65b563","name":"Drici, Lylia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"holmmettepau","last":"Holm","locid":"78e86e2a-813e-4f86-9a37-75a7cc79173f","name":"Holm, Mette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maud Eline","key":"ottenheijmmaudelinepau","last":"Ottenheijm","locid":"4943980b-1f6c-4ccc-bc68-b7d09a08d926","nam