ai J.","key":"weweralbrechtsennicolaijpau","last":"Wewer Albrechtsen","locid":"0d59b767-fdca-42a0-b879-70fb0ec55651","name":"Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","name_org":"Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J.","orcid":"0000-0003-4230-5753","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38839859"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s42003-024-06370-8","issn":["23993642"],"issue":"1","journal":"Communications Biology","paperid":"688","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Communications Biology","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195332433"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f94482a9-5e35-4b14-8ada-45e3e1408bb3","ku-959d4415-4fd0-45ed-b500-caee3a6adc5b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Proteomic profiling reveals diagnostic signatures and pathogenic insights in multisystem inflammatory syndrome in children","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-742128","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"α-Synuclein (α-syn) accumulates as insoluble amyloid but also forms soluble α-syn oligomers (αSOs), thought to be even more cytotoxic than fibrils. To detect and block the unwanted activities of these αSOs, we have raised 30 monoclonal antibodies (mAbs) against different forms of αSOs, ranging from unmodified αSOs to species stabilized by lipid peroxidation products and polyphenols, αSOs formed by C-terminally truncated α-syn, and multivalent display of α-syn on capsid virus-like particles (cVLPs). While the mAbs generally show a preference for αSOs, they also bind fibrils, but to variable extents. Overall, we observe great diversity in the mAbs' relative affinities for monomers and αSOs, varied requirements for the C-terminal extension of α-syn, and only a modest effect on α-syn fibrillation. Several mAbs show several orders of magnitude preference for αSOs over monomers in in-solution studies, while the commercial antibody MJF14 only bound 10-fold more strongly to αSOs than monomeric α-syn. Gratifyingly, seven mAbs almost completely block αSO permeabilization of membrane vesicles. Five selected mAbs identified α-syn-related pathologies like Lewy bodies (LBs) and Lewy Neurites, as well as Glial Cytoplasmic Inclusions in postmortem brains from people diagnosed for PD, dementia with LBs or multiple system atrophy, although to different extents. Three mAbs were particularly useful for pathological evaluation of postmortem brain human tissue, including early stages of PD. Although there was no straightforward connection between the mAbs' biophysical and immunohistochemical properties, it is encouraging that this comprehensive collection of mAbs able to recognize different aggregated α-syn species in vitro also holds diagnostic potential.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Nielsen, Janni","Lauritsen, Johanne","Pedersen, Jannik Nedergaard","Nowak, Jan Stanislaw","Bendtsen, Malthe Kjær","Kleijwegt, Giulia","Lusser, Kaija","Civit, Laia","Valero Moreno, Julian","Schneider, Matthias M","Krainer, Georg","Goksøyr, Louise","Khalifé, Paul","Kaalund, Sanne Simone","Aznar, Susana","Kjaergaard, Magnus","Sereikaité, Vita","Strømgaard, Kristian","Knowles, Tuomas P J","Nielsen, Morten Agertoug","Sander, Adam F","Romero-Ramos, Marina","Otzen, Daniel E"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-756096"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Otzen, Daniel E","Romero-Ramos, Marina"],"country":["Austria","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cambridge","University of Graz"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"molecular properties and diagnostic potential of monoclonal antibodies targeting cytotoxic α synuclein oligomers","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41531-024-00747-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-756096","identifier":[{"id":"85199976848","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39075088","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11286781","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-ccac1b0b-ba12-405d-9fd3-a0b8f02c7c79","ku-f1e73abb-e982-44ec-b43b-5f39595bb502"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-46E683A5951F7B0EC0C9F4A2AC9573BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41531-024-00747-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/402444732/Molecular_properties.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1",