nternational inception cohort study (PLOT-ICU)","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-722902","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Imputation techniques provide means to replace missing measurements with a value and are used in almost all downstream analysis of mass spectrometry (MS) based proteomics data using label-free quantification (LFQ). Here we demonstrate how collaborative filtering, denoising autoencoders, and variational autoencoders can impute missing values in the context of LFQ at different levels. We applied our method, proteomics imputation modeling mass spectrometry (PIMMS), to an alcohol-related liver disease (ALD) cohort with blood plasma proteomics data available for 358 individuals. Removing 20 percent of the intensities we were able to recover 15 out of 17 significant abundant protein groups using PIMMS-VAE imputations. When analyzing the full dataset we identified 30 additional proteins (+13.2%) that were significantly differentially abundant across disease stages compared to no imputation and found that some of these were predictive of ALD progression in machine learning models. We, therefore, suggest the use of deep learning approaches for imputing missing values in MS-based proteomics on larger datasets and provide workflows for these.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Webel, Henry","Niu, Lili","Nielsen, Annelaura Bach","Locard-Paulet, Marie","Mann, Matthias","Jensen, Lars Juhl","Rasmussen, Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-748479"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","Université Paul Sabatier Toulouse III"],"keyword":["Deep learning","Humans","Male","Mass Spectrometry methods","Proteomics methods","Supervised machine learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"imputation of label free quantitative mass spectrometry based proteomics data using self supervised deep learning","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-48711-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-748479","identifier":[{"id":"38926340","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11208500","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85197132385","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8258110c-7b80-4509-8e1a-65064a675b92"],"keyword":["Deep Learning","Humans","Male","Mass Spectrometry/methods","Proteomics/methods","Supervised Machine Learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7440DBE932BE3957283610D77A282E64"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/396732957/s41467_024_48711_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-48711-5","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Rasmussen Group","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Rasmussen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"université paul sabatier toulouse iii","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université Paul Sabatier Toulouse III","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henry","key":"webelpau","last":"Webel","locid":"3c086234-ec03-49aa-9df7-97fea73c5dfb","name":"Webel, Henry","orcid":"0000-0001-8833-7617","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lili","key":"niupau","last":"Niu","locid":"f74df5eb-9404-4bdb-9d58-289bf2c90efa","name":"Niu, Lili","orcid":"0000-0003-4571-4368","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annelaura Bach","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2a42eff8-3176-4b59-8e7c-3857eb418d8b","name":"Nielsen, Annelaura Bach","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Marie","key":"locardpauletpau","last":"Locard-Paulet","locid":"9e3842e4-c41c-4133-859e-7884a60496fb","name":"Locard-Paulet, Marie","orcid":"0000-0003-2879-9224","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Juhl","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"cae227d4-1222-4c3a-a7b0-34ad91d42e5a","name":"Jensen, Lars Juhl","orcid":"0000-0001-7885-715X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Simon","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"274c7fdf-d0c2-4c4e-8739-9b5e74d5005f","name":"Rasmussen, Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-6323-9041","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38926340"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-48711-5","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"5405","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197132385"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8258110c-7b80-4509-8e1a-65064a675b92"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Imputation of label-free quantitative mass spectrometry-based proteomics data using self-supervised deep learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-748479","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Air pollution has been shown to significantly impact human health including cancer. Gastric and upper aerodigestive tract (UADT) cancers are common and increased risk has been associated with smoking and occupational exposures. However, the association with air pollution remains unclear. We pooled European subcohorts (N = 287,576 participants for gastric and N = 297,406 for UADT analyses) and investigated the association between residential exposure to fine particles (PM2.5), nitrogen dioxide (NO2), black carbon (BC) and ozone in the warm season (O3w) with gastric and UADT cancer. We applied Cox proportional hazards models adjusting for potential confounders at the individual and area-level. During 5,305,133 and 5,434,843 person-years, 872 gastric and 1139 UADT incident cancer cases were observed, respectively. For gastric cancer, we found no association with PM2.5, NO2 and BC while for UADT the hazard ratios (95% confidence interval) were 1.15 (95% CI: 1.00–1.33) per 5 μg/m3 increase in PM2.5, 1.19 (1.08–1.30) per 10 μg/m3 increase in NO2, 1.14 (1.04–1.26) per 0.5 × 10−5 m−1 increase in BC and 0.81 (0.72–0.92) per 10 μg/m3 increase in O3w. We found no association between long-term ambient air pollution exposure and incidence of gastric cancer, while for long-term exposure to PM2.5, NO2 and BC increased incidence of UADT cancer was observed.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Nagel, Gabriele","Chen, Jie","Jaensch, Andrea","Skodda, Lea","Rodopoulou, Sophia","Strak, Maciej","de Hoogh, Kees","Andersen, Zorana Jovanovic","Bellander, Tom","Brandt, Jørgen","Fecht, Daniela","Forastiere, Francesco","Gulliver, John","Hertel, Ole","Hoffmann, Barbara","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Katsouyanni, Klea","Ketzel, Matthias","Leander, Karin","Magnusson, Patrik K.E.","Pershagen, Göran","Rizzuto, Debora","Samoli, Evangelia","Severi, Gianluca","Stafoggia, Massimo","Tjønneland, Anne","Vermeulen, Roel C.H.","Wolf, Kathrin","Zitt, Emanuel","Brunekreef, Bert","Hoek, Gerard","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Weinmayr, Gudrun"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-735314"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nagel, Gabriele"],"country":["Austria","France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Netherlands","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Agency for Preventive and Social Medicine","All Global Affiliations","Department of Epidemiology, Lazio Regional Health Service","Dept Epidemiol Lazio Reg","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Helmholtz Zentrum Munich","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","Imperial College London","Karolinska Institutet","LKH Feldkirch","MRC Centre for Environment and Health","National Institute for Public Health and the Environment (RIVM)","National Institute of Public Health and the Environment","National and Kapodistrian University of Athens","Paris-Saclay University","Stockholm Gerontology Research Center","Stockholm Gerontology Research Centre","Swiss Tropical and Public Health Institute","Ulm University","Universite Paris-Saclay","University of Athens","University of Basel","University of Leicester","University of Surrey","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Air Pollutants adverse effects","Air Pollution adverse effects","Air pollution","Environmental Exposure adverse effects","Gastric cancer","Humans","Incidence","Nitrogen Dioxide adverse effects","Nitrogen dioxide","Ozone","Particulate Matter adverse effects","Stomach Neoplasms epidemiology","UADT","particular matter"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to air pollution and incidence of gastric and the upper aerodigestive tract cancers in a pooled european cohort the elapse project","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.34864","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-735314","identifier":[{"id":"85184861346","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38339851","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c2e0fdb2-8d39-4d5e-9108-6ef0a94b8d6d","ku-4e399958-68bc-4718-8279-94f4a19127f1"],"keyword":["Air Pollutants/adverse effects","Air Pollution/adverse effects","Environmental Exposure/adverse effects","Humans","Incidence","Nitrogen Dioxide/adverse effects","Particulate Matter/adverse effects","Stomach Neoplasms/epidemiology","UADT","air pollution","gastric cancer","nitrogen dioxide","ozone","particular matter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6E5617B9BBA0BF70E7F981E25DECF2AA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/383181485/Intl_Journal_of_Cancer_2024_Nagel_Long_term_exposure_to_air_pollution_and_incidence_of_gastric_and_the_upper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.34864","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ulm university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ulm University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gr","key":"national and kapodistrian university of athens","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National and Kapodistrian University of Athens","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gr","key":"university of athens","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Athens","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"national institute of public health and t