","first":"Gianluca","key":"severipau","last":"Severi","name":"Severi, Gianluca","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10 14 15","first":"Massimo","key":"stafoggiapau","last":"Stafoggia","name":"Stafoggia, Massimo","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9 18","first":"Anne","key":"tjønnelandpau","last":"Tjønneland","locid":"853b23de-35d6-44f7-88fa-edbe4a4f8b6d","name":"Tjønneland, Anne","orcid":"0000-0003-4385-2097","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Roel C.H.","key":"vermeulenpau","last":"Vermeulen","name":"Vermeulen, Roel C.H.","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"24 25","first":"Kathrin","key":"wolfpau","last":"Wolf","name":"Wolf, Kathrin","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"26 27","first":"Emanuel","key":"zittpau","last":"Zitt","name":"Zitt, Emanuel","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bert","key":"brunekreefpau","last":"Brunekreef","name":"Brunekreef, Bert","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gerard","key":"hoekpau","last":"Hoek","name":"Hoek, Gerard","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"18 11","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gudrun","key":"weinmayrpau","last":"Weinmayr","name":"Weinmayr, Gudrun","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38339851"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ijc.34864","issn":["00207136"],"issue":"11","journal":"International Journal of Cancer","pages":"1900-1910","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cancer","volume":"154"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184861346"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c2e0fdb2-8d39-4d5e-9108-6ef0a94b8d6d","ku-4e399958-68bc-4718-8279-94f4a19127f1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long-term exposure to air pollution and incidence of gastric and the upper aerodigestive tract cancers in a pooled European cohort : The ELAPSE project","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-735314","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: The three correlated environmental exposures (air pollution, road traffic noise, and green space) have all been associated with the risk of myocardial infarction (MI). The present study aimed to analyse their independent and cumulative association with MI. METHODS AND RESULTS: In a cohort of all Danes aged 50 or older in the period 2005-17, 5-year time-weighted average exposure to fine particles (PM2.5), ultrafine particles, elemental carbon, nitrogen dioxide (NO2), and road traffic noise at the most and least exposed façades of residence was estimated. Green space around residences was estimated from land use maps. Cox proportional hazard models were used to estimate hazard ratios (HRs) and 95% confidence interval (CI), and cumulative risk indices (CRIs) were calculated. All expressed per interquartile range. Models were adjusted for both individual and neighbourhood-level socio-demographic covariates. The cohort included 1 964 702 persons. During follow-up, 71 285 developed MI. In single-exposure models, all exposures were associated with an increased risk of MI. In multi-pollutant analyses, an independent association with risk of MI was observed for PM2.5 (HR: 1.026; 95% CI: 1.002-1.050), noise at most exposed façade (HR: 1.024; 95% CI: 1.012-1.035), and lack of green space within 150 m of residence (HR: 1.018; 95% CI: 1.010-1.027). All three factors contributed significantly to the CRI (1.089; 95% CI: 1.076-1.101). CONCLUSION: In a nationwide cohort study, air pollution, noise, and lack of green space were all independently associated with an increased risk of MI. The air pollutant PM2.5 was closest associated with MI risk.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Sørensen, Mette","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","Ketzel, Matthias","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Brandt, Jørgen","Frohn, Lise Marie","Massling, Andreas","Khan, Jibran","Münzel, Thomas","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-741948"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","University Medical Center Mainz","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Cohort study","Epidemiology","Green space","Myocardial Infarction","Traffic noise"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"concomitant exposure to air pollution green space and noise and risk of myocardial infarction a cohort study from denmark","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85181263003","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Research described in this article was conducted under contract to the Health Effects Institute (HEI), an organization jointly funded by the United States Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) (Assistance Award No. R-82811201) and certain motor vehicle and engine manufacturers. The contents of this article do not necessarily reflect the views and policies of the EPA or the vehicle and engine manufacturers. The study funder was not involved in the design of the study; the collection, analysis, and interpretation of the data; and writing the paper and did not impose any restrictions regarding the publication of the paper."],"id":"S02-100.00-741948","identifier":[{"id":"37738461","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85181263003","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-95b579f1-7240-4635-b9dc-aa48f0eeb221","ruc-f976f81f-8473-42fe-a770-713dc80ef875"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Cohort study","Epi