blisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Hepatology","volume":"80"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Nordic Bioscience","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Region Zealand","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","dr holm app aps."],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-24c183cd-4ddd-4445-a4d6-89853dd51682"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Identifying patterns of steatotic liver disease severity: a multi-omic analysis of 834 distinct omics features from healthy to end- stage liver disease in 854 individuals","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-750243","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Manufacturing systems are continually challenged by evolving market demands, environmental constraints, and regulatory uncertainties. Manufacturers therefore need to develop and implement the reconfigurability capability to rapidly and cost-effectively adapt to new requirements throughout their life cycles. To this end, reconfigurability enablers —physical or logical factors that facilitate such adjustments— are needed. To support the identification and implementation of necessary reconfigurability enablers in existing factories and manufacturing systems, this study proposes a structured methodology to identify and select reconfigurability enablers and applies it within a case study in a brownfield factory . In the case study, an existing factory was analyzed. The current configuration was investigated, including the characterization of strategic requirements and anticipated trends. The analysis allowed to identify and select reconfigurability enablers for the manufacturer. The preliminary findings from the case study underscore the need to further implement and validate the methodology in industrial cases. The proposed methodology provides a foundation for future research on the systematic design of reconfigurability enablers. This study emphasizes the necessity for systematically designing reconfigurability enablers at various levels of detail, highlighting how enablers at workstation and system levels influence each other.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Napoleone, Alessia","Andersen, Rasmus","Andersen, Ann-Louise","Brunø, Thomas Ditlev","Nielsen, Kjeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-756698"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Napoleone, Alessia"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology"],"keyword":["Resilient Manufacturing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a methodology for identification of reconfigurability enablers and application in a manufacturing system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85204621070&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-756698","identifier":[{"id":"85204621070","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4d172dad-1de7-4f4b-9dd8-2e475892ca0d"],"keyword":["Reconfigurability Enablers","Reconfigurability Strategy","Reconfigurable Manufacturing System (RMS)","Resilient Manufacturing","System Life Cycle"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DEF371D4D3EC81F4989E73762833C8F8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Sustainable Manufacturing Systems research group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessia","key":"napoleonealessiapau","last":"Napoleone","name":"Napoleone, Alessia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"