{"abstract":"Aims: To describe the level of physical activity 6 months after an out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) and to explore potential risk factors of a low level of physical activity. Methods: Post-hoc analyses of the international multicentre Targeted Hypothermia versus Targeted Normothermia after Out-of-Hospital Cardiac arrest (TTM2) trial. At 6 months, survivors at 61 sites in Europe, Australia and New Zeeland were invited to a follow-up. The participants answered two questions on self-reported physical activity. Answers were categorized as a low, moderate, or high level of physical activity and further dichotomized into a low versus moderate/high level of physical activity. Potential risk factors for a low level of physical activity were collected and investigated by univariable and multivariable logistic regression. Results: At 6 months, 807 of 939 (86%) OHCA survivors answered the two questions of physical activity; 34% reported a low, 44% moderate and 22% high level of physical activity. Obesity (OR = 1.75, 95% CI 1.10–2.77, p = 0.018), mobility problems by EuroQol 5 dimensions 5 levels (OR = 1.73, 95% CI 1.06–2.84, p = 0.029), and cognitive impairment by Symbol Digit Modalities Test (OR = 1.78, 95% CI 1.13–2.82, p = 0.013) were significantly associated with a low level of physical activity in the multivariable analysis. Conclusion: One third of the OHCA survivors reported a low level of physical activity. Obesity, mobility problems, and cognitive impairment were associated with a low level of physical activity. ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT02908308.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Heimburg, Katarina","Blennow Nordström, Erik","Dankiewicz, Josef","Friberg, Hans","Grejs, Anders Morten","Hänggi, Matthias","Keeble, Thomas R.","Kirkegaard, Hans","Nielsen, Niklas","Rylander, Christian","Tornberg, Åsa B.","Ullén, Susann","Wise, Matthew P.","Cronberg, Tobias","Lilja, Gisela"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-772712"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Heimburg, Katarina"],"country":["Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anglia Ruskin University","Cardiff University","Lund University","Mid and South Essex NHS Foundation Trust","University of Bern","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Cardiac arrest","Cardiovascular risk factors","Cognitive function","Patient reported outcome","Physical activity","Physical function"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low physical activity level in out of hospital cardiac arrest survivors with obesity mobility problems and cognitive impairment results from the ttm000000000002 trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2024.110407","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-772712","identifier":[{"id":"85206144627","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39368797","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-71775be6-3871-4422-bf70-138b383a51b5"],"keyword":["Cardiac arrest","Cardiovascular risk factors","Cognitive function","Patient-reported outcome","Physical activity","Physical function"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C0A780AC60F3E1CCA53809917DA75584"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2024.110407","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"A