","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"26","first":"Elom K.","key":"aglagopau","last":"Aglago","name":"Aglago, Elom K.","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"27","first":"John","key":"daneshpau","last":"Danesh","name":"Danesh, John","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"26","first":"Elio","key":"ribolipau","last":"Riboli","name":"Riboli, Elio","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marc J.","key":"gunterpau","last":"Gunter","name":"Gunter, Marc J.","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathilde","key":"touvierpau","last":"Touvier","name":"Touvier, Mathilde","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39529812"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.lanepe.2024.101006","issn":["26667762"],"journal":"The Lancet Regional Health - Europe","paperid":"101006","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Regional Health - Europe","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204691430"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cb9d6394-e223-48d5-b9ca-bf3f4022e4b8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nutritional quality of diet characterized by the Nutri-Score profiling system and cardiovascular disease risk : a prospective study in 7 European countries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-779077","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: The aim of this study was to assess whether hypothermia increased survival and improved functional outcome when compared with normothermia in out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) patients with similar characteristics than in previous randomized studies showing benefits for hypothermia. Methods: Post hoc analysis of a pragmatic, multicenter, randomized clinical trial (TTM-2, NCT02908308). In this analysis, the subset of patients included in the trial who had similar characteristics to patients included in one previous randomized trial and randomized to hypothermia at 33 °C or normothermia (i.e. target < 37.8 °C) were considered. The primary outcome was survival at 6 months; secondary outcomes included favorable functional outcome at 6 months, defined as a modified Rankin scale of 0–3. Time-to-death and the occurrence of adverse events were also reported. Results: From a total of 1891 included in the TTM-2 study, 600 (31.7%) were included in the analysis, 294 in the hypothermia and 306 in the normothermia group. At 6 months, 207 of the 294 patients (70.4%) in the hypothermia group and 220 of the 306 patients (71.8%) in the normothermia group had survived (relative risk with hypothermia, 0.96; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.81 to 1.15; P = 0.71). Also, 198 of the 294 (67.3%) in the hypothermia group and 202 of the 306 (66.0%) in the normothermia group had a favorable functional outcome (relative risk with hypothermia, 1.03; 95% CI, 0.87 to 1.23; P = 0.79). There was a significant increase in the occurrence of arrythmias in the hypothermia group (62/294, 21.2%) when compared to the normothermia group (43/306, 14.1%—OR 1.49, 95% CI 1.05–2.14; p = 0.026). Conclusions: In this study, hypothermia at 33˚C did not improve survival or functional outcome in a subset of patients with similar cardiac arrest characteristics to patients in whom benefit from hypothermia was shown in prior studies.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Taccone, Fabio Silvio","Cariou, Alain","Zorzi, Stefano","Friberg, Hans","Jakobsen, Janus C.","Nordberg, Per","Robba, Chiara","Belohlavek, Jan","Hovdenes, Jan","Haenggi, Matthias","Åneman, Anders","Grejs, Anders Morten","Keeble, Thomas R.","Annoni, Filippo","Young, Paul J.","Wise, Matt P.","Cronberg, Tobias","Lilja, Gisela","Nielsen, Niklas","Dankiewicz, Josef"],"cuid":["S02-089.47-767773"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Taccone, Fabio Silvio"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Czechia","France","Italy","New Zealand","Norway","Poland","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["AP-HP Assistance Publique - Hopitaux de Paris","After ROSC Network","All Global Affiliations","Anglia Ruskin School of Medicine","Anglia Ruskin University","Capital & Coast District Health Board","Cardiff University","Charles University","ETH Zürich","General Teaching Hospital","Hospital Cochin","Hôpital Universitaire de Bruxelles (HUB)","IRCCS Azienda Ospedaliera Universitaria San Martino IST","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Liverpool Hospital","Liverpool Hospital, Australia","Lund University","MSE Trust","Medical Research Institute of New Zealand","Mid and South Essex NHS Foundation Trust","Monash University","Oslo University Hospital","San Martino Hospital Genoa","University Hospital Wales","University Hospital Zurich","University Hospitals Brussels (UZB)","University of Genoa","University of Melbourne","Université Libre de Bruxelles","Wellington Hospital","Wroclaw Medical University","Wrocław Medical University"],"keyword":["Aged","Cardiac arrest","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation methods","Female","Humans","Hypothermia","Hypothermia Induced methods","Male","Middle Aged","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest therapy","Outcome","Shockable rhythm","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","