"name":"Young, Paul J.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 34 35","corresponding":null,"first":"Matt P.","key":"wisepau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Matt P.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Gisela","key":"liljapau","last":"Lilja","name":"Lilja, Gisela","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Josef","key":"dankiewiczpau","last":"Dankiewicz","name":"Dankiewicz, Josef","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39407230"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13054-024-05119-3","issn":["1466609X"],"issn_org":["13648535"],"issue":"1","journal":"Critical Care","paperid":"335","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","publisher_org":"BioMed Central Ltd","status":"p","title":"Critical Care","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206470958"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-af57bbf4-a7a7-4267-95d2-ea54c785b2ba","sdu-84b2bdd5-eae6-4bbb-92ba-f822eb8f57a8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Hypothermia versus normothermia in patients with cardiac arrest and shockable rhythm : a secondary analysis of the TTM-2 study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.47-767773","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"It is unclear whether cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract (UADT) and gastric cancer are related to air pollution, due to few studies with inconsistent results. The effects of particulate matter (PM) may vary across locations due to different source contributions and related PM compositions, and it is not clear which PM constituents/sources are most relevant from a consideration of overall mass concentration alone. We therefore investigated the association of UADT and gastric cancers with PM2.5 elemental constituents and sources components indicative of different sources within a large multicentre population based epidemiological study. Cohorts with at least 10 cases per cohort led to ten and eight cohorts from five countries contributing to UADT- and gastric cancer analysis, respectively. Outcome ascertainment was based on cancer registry data or data of comparable quality. We assigned home address exposure to eight elemental constituents (Cu, Fe, K, Ni, S, Si, V and Zn) estimated from Europe-wide exposure models, and five source components identified by absolute principal component analysis (APCA). Cox regression models were run with age as time scale, stratified for sex and cohort and adjusted for relevant individual and neighbourhood level confounders. We observed 1139 UADT and 872 gastric cancer cases during a mean follow-up of 18.3 and 18.5 years, respectively. UADT cancer incidence was associated with all constituents except K in single element analyses. After adjustment for NO2, only Ni and V remained associated with UADT. Residual oil combustion and traffic source components were associated with UADT cancer persisting in the multiple source model. No associations were found for any of the elements or source components and gastric cancer incidence. Our results indicate an association of several PM constituents indicative of different sources with UADT but not gastric cancer incidence with the most robust evidence for traffic and residual oil combustion.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Weinmayr, Gudrun","Chen, Jie","Jaensch, Andrea","Skodda, Lea","Rodopoulou, Sophia","Strak, Maciej","de Hoogh, Kees","Andersen, Zorana Jovanovic","Bellander, Tom","Brandt, Jørgen","Fecht, Daniela","Forastiere, Francesco","Gulliver, John","Hertel, Ole","Hoffmann, Barbara","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Katsouyanni, Klea","Ketzel, Matthias","Leander, Karin","Magnusson, Patrik K.E.","Pershagen, Göran","Rizzuto, Debora","Samoli, Evangelia","Severi, Gianluca","Stafoggia, Massimo","Tjønneland, Anne","Vermeulen, Roel","Wolf, Kathrin","Zitt, Emanuel","Brunekreef, Bert","Thurston, George","Hoek, Gerard","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Nagel, Gabriele"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-724936"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Netherlands","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Agency for Preventive and Social Medicine","All Global Affiliations","Department of Epidemiology, Lazio Regional Health Service","Dept Epidemiol Lazio Reg","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","Imperial College London","Karolinska Institutet","LKH Feldkirch","MRC Centre for Environment and Health","National Institute of Public Health and the Environment","National and Kapodistrian University of Athens","New York University","Paris-Saclay University","Stockholm Gerontology Research Center","Swiss Tropical and Public Health Institute","Ulm University","Umeå University","Universite Paris-Saclay","University of Athens","University of Basel","University of Leicester","University of Surrey","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Gastric cancer","Long term exposure","PM composition","PM sources","Particulate matter PM","Upper aerodigestive tract cancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to several constituents and sources of pm sub 000000000002 000000000005 sub is associated with incidence of upper aerodigestive tract cancers but not gastric cancer results from the large pooled european cohort of the elapse project","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85178634685","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-724936","identifier":[{"id":"85178634685","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37996018","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f267660e-1d43-4fce-99de-0dc8d3d89aa7","ku-77247400-3537-4814-bd82-389547559ef4"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Gastric cancer","Long-term exposure","PM composition","PM sources","Particulate matter (PM)","Upper aerodigestive tract cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1CC08D83F0E1F3ADA3FC36684E2184E4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ulm university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ulm University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gr","key":"national and kapodistrian university of athens","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National and Kapodistrian University of Athens","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gr","key":"university of athens","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Athens","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"national institute of public health and the environment","lo