{"abstract":"Lithium is an element that is common in trace amounts, whereas larger quantities are often used as a mood-stabilizing medication for bipolar disorders. The mechanism of action of lithium in the brain is unknown, but there are many theories; one postulated mechanism of action of lithium overlaps with neurodevelopment and autism.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Liew, Zeyan","Meng, Qi","Yan, Qi","Schullehner, Jörg","Hansen, Birgitte","Kristiansen, Søren Munch","Voutchkova, Denitza D.","Olsen, Jørn","Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","Ketzel, Matthias","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Ritz, Beate R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-801680"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Liew, Zeyan","Ritz, Beate R."],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Southern California","University of Surrey","Yale University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-HO-CDR","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between estimated geocoded residential maternal exposure to lithium in drinking water and risk for autism spectrum disorder in offspring in denmark","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-801680","ids":["sdu-13c3250b-ba88-4b14-a41b-3e738ab9c029"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D35F85529FDC2A3659AC43DC0799F8E0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"yale university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Yale University","used":1},{"affno":"2","