","name":"Zirek, Fazilcan","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"47 22","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"bushpau","last":"Bush","name":"Bush, Andrew","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"48 49","corresponding":null,"first":"Annick","key":"clementpau","last":"Clement","name":"Clement, Annick","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 50","first":"Matthias","key":"griesepau","last":"Griese","name":"Griese, Matthias","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik Fouirnaies","key":"buchvaldpau","last":"Buchvald","name":"Buchvald, Frederik Fouirnaies","rank":39,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"48 49","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadia","key":"nathanpau","last":"Nathan","name":"Nathan, Nadia","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Kim Gjerum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"eabd2b94-b01a-4243-bb5a-b6dd696edd6a","name":"Nielsen, Kim G.","name_org":"Nielsen, Kim Gjerum","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37101741"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1183/23120541.00733-2022","issn":["23120541"],"issue":"2","journal":"ERJ Open Research","paperid":"00733-2022","publisher":"European Respiratory Society","status":"p","title":"ERJ Open Research","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159188757"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-14920bd4-b392-4ad1-8cad-c50f43055fc3","ku-a48853dd-95fd-4efb-b8ed-ee6018389b10"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diffuse alveolar haemorrhage in children : an international multicentre study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.94-685851","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Bimetallic nanoparticles have been extensively studied as electrocatalysts due to their superior catalytic activity and selectivity compared to their monometallic counterparts. The properties of bimetallic materials depend on the ordering of the metals in the structure, and to tailor-make materials for specific applications, it is important to be able to control the atomic structure of the materials during synthesis. Here, we study the formation of bimetallic palladium indium nanoparticles to understand how the synthesis parameters and additives used influence the atomic structure of the obtained product. Specifically, we investigate a colloidal synthesis, where oleylamine was used as the main solvent while the effect of two surfactants, oleic acid (OA) and trioctylphosphine (TOP) was studied. We found that without TOP included in the synthesis, a Pd-rich intermetallic phase with the Pd3In structure initially formed, which transformed into large NPs of the CsCl-structured PdIn phase. When TOP was included, the syntheses yielded both In2O3 and Pd3In. In situ X-ray total scattering with Pair Distribution Function analysis was used to study the formation process of PdIn bimetallic NPs. Our results highlight how seemingly subtle changes to material synthesis methods can have a large influence on the product atomic structure.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Wang, Baiyu","Mathiesen, Jette K.","Kirsch, Andrea","Schlegel, Nicolas","Anker, Andy S.","Johansen, Frederik L.","Kjær, Emil T.S.","Aalling-Frederiksen, Olivia","Nielsen, Tobias M.","Thomsen, Maria S.","Jakobsen, Rasmus K.","Arenz, Matthias","Jensen, Kirsten M.Ø."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-716192"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Kirsten M.Ø."],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bern"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formation of intermetallic pdin nanoparticles influence of surfactants on nanoparticle atomic structure","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/d3na00582h","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-716192","identifier":[{"id":"38059038","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85176259041","type":"scopus"},{"id":"001094725500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC10697006","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-03c293e0-37e3-47ff-8c4a-d058863a29c1","ku-edee4997-facd-48df-9f3e-03f225810adb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F6916C2363FC266AC0D371ECD3E0F658"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/d3na00582h","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/376291987/d3na00582h.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/345591097/d3na00582h.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Surface Physics and Catalysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"university of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bern","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Baiyu","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"42e70a6c-bea1-4ceb-9811-a02429a6f6b5","name":"Wang, Baiyu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette K.","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"9040601f-a87a-4784-9d58-e26f0c24e1de","name":"Mathiesen, Jette K.","orcid":"0000-0001-6252-4131","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andrea","key":"kirschpau","last":"Kirsch","locid":"db2d036a-9323-4ebb-8e70-3f2eac25626e","name":"Kirsch, Andrea","orcid":"0000-0003-2602-7415","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolas","key":"schlegelpau","last":"Schlegel","name":"Schlegel, Nicolas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andy S.","key":"ankerpau","last":"Anker","locid":"bfa4e883-f043-4bab-8f3a-be6b10a06907","name":"Anker, Andy S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Frederik L.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Frederik L.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emil T.S.","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","name":"Kjær, Emil T.S.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olivia","key":"aallingfrederiksenpau","last":"Aalling-Frederiksen","locid":"ae253671-5a98-444a-941d-ff56cc11bd2d","name":"Aalling-Frederiksen, Olivia","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias M.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"25600acf-cbd9-42bd-85b7-46efed7ff0d4","name":"Nielsen, Tobias M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria S.","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"e82ae539-e189-4db9-90e2-3f6fc963974f","name":"Thomsen, Maria S.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus K.","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"178960fd-0c18-4ca8-9475-d5c65d1c99ac","name":"Jakobsen, Rasmus K.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"arenzpau","last":"Arenz","name":"Arenz, Matthias","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten M.Ø.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"057e5b4d-da43-4523-b326-379b0c747d06","name":"Jensen, Kirsten M.Ø.","orcid":"0000-0003-0291-217X","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38059038"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/d3na00582h","issn":["25160230"],"issue":"24","journal":"Nanoscale Advances","paperid":"6913","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Nanoscale Advances","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85176259041"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-03c293e0-37e3-47ff-8c4a-d058863a29c1","ku-edee4997-facd-48df-9f3e-03f225810adb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Formation of intermetallic PdIn nanoparticles: influence of surfactants on nanoparticle atomic structure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-716192","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Ocrelizumab, a humanized monoclonal antibody targeted against CD20+ B cells, reduces the frequency of relapses by 46% and disability worsening by 40% compared with interferon beta 1a in relapsing-remitting multiple sclerosis (MS). Rituximab, a chimeric monoclonal anti-CD20 agent, is often prescribed as an off-label alternative to ocrelizumab. Objective: To evaluate whether the effectiveness of rituximab is noninferior to ocrelizumab in relapsing-remitting MS. Design, Setting, and Participants: This was an observational cohort study conducted between January 2015 and March 2021. Patients were included in the treatment group for the duration of study therapy and were recruited from the MSBase registry and Danish MS Registry (DMSR). Included patients had a history of relapsing-remitting MS treated with ocrelizumab or rituximab, a minimum 6 months of follow-up, and sufficient data to calculate the propensity score. Patients with comparable baseline characteristics were 1:6 matched with propensity score on age, sex, MS duration, disability (Expanded Disability Status Scale), prior relapse rate, prior therapy, disease activity (relapses, disability accumulation, or both), magnetic resonance imaging lesion burden (missing values imputed), and country. Exposure: Treatment with ocrelizumab or rituximab after 2015. Main outcomes and Measures: Noninferiority comparison of annualized rate of relapses (ARRs), with a prespecified noninferiority margin of 1.63 rate ratio. Secondary end points were relapse and 6-month confirmed disability accumulation in pairwise-censored groups. Results: Of the 6027 patients with MS who were treated with ocrelizumab or rituximab, a total of 1613 (mean [SD] age; 42.0 [10.8] years; 1089 female [68%]) fulfilled the inclusion criteria and were included in the analysis (898 MSBase, 715 DMSR). A total of 710 patients treated with ocrelizumab (414 MSBase, 296 DMSR) were matched with 186 patients treated with rituximab (110 MSBase, 76 DMSR). Over a pairwise censored mean (SD) follow-up of 1.4 (0.7) years, the ARR ratio was higher in patients treated with rituximab than in those treated with ocrelizumab (rate ratio, 1.8; 95% CI, 1.4-2.4; ARR, 0.20 vs 0.09; P < .001). The cumulative hazard of relapses was higher among patients treated with rituximab than those treated with ocrelizumab (hazard ratio, 2.1; 95% CI, 1.5-3.0). No difference in the risk of disability accumulation was observed between groups. Results were confirmed in sensitivity analyses. Conclusion: In this noninferiority comparative effectiveness observational cohort study, results did not show noninferiority of treatment with rituximab compared with ocrelizumab. As administered in everyday practice, rituximab was associated with a higher risk of relapses than ocrelizumab. The efficacy of rituximab and ocrelizumab administered at uniform doses and intervals is being further evaluated in randomized noninferiority clinical trials.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Roos, Izanne","Hughes, Stella","McDonnell, Gavin","Malpas, Charles B.","Sharmin, Sifat","Boz, Cavit","Alroughani, Raed","Ozakbas, Serkan","Buzzard, Katherine","Skibina, Olga","van der Walt, Anneke","Butzkueven, Helmut","Lechner-Scott, Jeannette","Kuhle, Jens","Terzi, Murat","Laureys, Guy","Van Hijfte, Liesbeth","John, Nevin","Grammond, Pierre","Grand'Maison, Francois","Soysal, Aysun","Jensen, Ana Voldsgaard","Rasmussen, Peter Vestergaard","Svendsen, Kristina Bacher","Barzinji, Ismael","Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted","Sejbæk, Tobias","Prakash, Sivagini","Stilund, Morten Leif Munding","Weglewski, Arkadiusz","Issa, Nadia Mubder","Kant, Matthias","Sellebjerg, Finn","Gray, Orla","Magyari, Melinda","Kalincik, Tomas"],"cuid":["S04-091.88-685791"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["MSBase S