DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d8325f63-ee8e-4519-9b40-83907d3b7d97","ku-cea385a6-4bea-4a08-bb75-68963d14e983"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multiple myeloma risk in relation to long-term air pollution exposure - A pooled analysis of four European cohorts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-716121","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: Air pollution increases the risk of stroke, but the literature on identifying susceptible subgroups of populations is scarce and inconsistent. The aim of this study was to investigate if the association between air pollution and risk of stroke differed by sociodemographic factors, financial stress, comorbid conditions, and residential road traffic noise, population density and green space. Methods: We assessed long-term exposure to air pollution with ultrafine particles, PM2.5, elemental carbon and NO2 for a cohort of 1,971,246 Danes aged 50-85 years. During follow-up from 2005 to 2017, we identified 83,211 incident stroke cases. We used Cox proportional hazards model (relative risk) and Aalen additive hazards models (absolute risk) to estimate associations and confidence intervals (CI) between 5-year running means of air pollution at the residence and risk of stroke in population strata.Results: All four pollutants were associated with higher risk of stroke. The association between air pollution and stroke was strongest among individuals with comorbidities, with shorter education, lower income and being retired. The results also indicated stronger associations among individuals living in less populated areas, and with low noise levels and more green space around the residence. Estimates of absolute risk seemed better suited to detect such interactions than estimates of relative risk. For example for PM2.5 the hazard ratio for stroke was 1.28 (95%CI: 1.22-1.34) and 1.26 (95%CI: 1.16-1.37) among those with mandatory and medium/long educa-tion respectively. The corresponding rate difference estimates per 100,000 person years were 568 (95%CI: 543-594) and 423(95%CI: 390-456)Conclusion: The associations between air pollution and risk of stroke was stronger among individuals of lower socioeconomic status or with pre-existing comorbid conditions. Absolute risk estimates were better suited to identify such effect modification.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Sorensen, Mette","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Ketzel, Matthias","Christensen, Jesper H.","Brandt, Jorgen","Frohn, Lise Marie","Khan, Jibran","Jensen, Steen Solvang","Lund, Thomas","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S03-099.28-685995"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Cardiovascular disease","Cohort study","Epidemiology","European cohorts","Green area","Long term exposure","Mortality","Noise","Quality","Risk","Stroke","Validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"air pollution and stroke effect modification by sociodemographic and environmental factors a cohort study from denmark","src":["au","ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85153794980","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-099.28-685995","identifier":[{"id":"85153794980","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000990942000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"37121155","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-954efbae-c6d9-4fa3-9133-6699d6d3964a","ku-8ead493b-8294-4ed1-85f2-7f50a48aa166","ruc-d945941d-bda1-4662-8ce3-c0f22afa3261"],"keyword":["Air pollution","CARDIOVASCULAR-DISEASE","Cohort study","EUROPEAN COHORTS","Epidemiology","Green-area","LONG-TERM EXPOSURE","MORTALITY","Noise","QUALITY","RISK","Stroke","VALIDATION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-7D9ECE4C96FDAC5A2408F3C168166513"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Molecular and Medical Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ulla Arthur","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper H.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","name_org":"Christensen, Jesper H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Marie","key":"frohnpau","last":"Frohn","locid":"1db55612-df02-4189-ab0d-5c62193e1afc","name":"Frohn, Lise Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4236-5708","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Solvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"0d52f91a-4eaa-46f9-ab5f-d7fd3c31440d","name":"Jensen, Steen Solvang","orcid":"0000-0001-5923-8441","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","first":"Thomas","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"f7a9e1bb-9051-45d6-90f4-edac932486b4","name":"Lund, Thomas","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37121155"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijheh.2023.114165","issn":["14384639","1618131X"],"issn_org":["14384639"],"journal":"International Journal of Hygiene and Environmental Health","paperid":"114165","publisher":"Elsevier GmbH","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hygiene and Environmental Health","volume":"251"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153794980"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-954efbae-c6d9-4fa3-9133-6699d6d3964a","ku-8ead493b-8294-4ed1-85f2-7f50a48aa166","ruc-d945941d-bda1-4662-8ce3-c0f22afa3261"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Air pollution and stroke; effect modification by sociodemographic and environmental factors. A cohort study from Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.28-685995","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Adherence is a prerequisite for the efficacy of any drug, and previous studies have shown that non-adherence is associated with disease activity and increased health care cost in multiple sclerosis (MS). The aim of this study was to investigate rates and reasons for discontinuation of dimethyl fumarate (DMF) among people with MS on a national level and differences between clinics in Denmark. Methods: This was a nationwide, registry and population study of patients treated with DMF. We calculated standard residuals (SR) demonstrate differences between clinics. For survival analysis regarding discontinuation rates and discontinuation due to specific AEs we used log-rank test Cox-proportional hazards and plotted Kaplan-Meier graphics. Results: We included 2,448 people with MS, treated with DMF from 2013 to 2020. Average treatment duration was 26 months (5,382 treatment years). 49.2 % of patients who initiated treatment with DMF (n = 1205) were continuously treated. Reasons for discontinuation were adverse events (54.5 %, n = 656), active disease (26.1 %, n = 315), pregnancy (9.4 %, n = 113) or other reasons (13.2 %, n = 159). We compared SR to the mean regarding reasons for discontinuation and found significant differences between sites regarding gastrointestinal adverse events, flushing and lymphopenia. Discontinuation due to all adverse events, flushing and lymphopenia were more frequent in female than male patients. Conclusion: In this population-based study, we found major differences between the MS clinics in rates and reason for discontinuation of DMF. Our results suggest that management strategies during DMF treatment can reduce discontinuation rates.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Roar, Malte","Nielsen, Amalie Rhode Høgh","Berg, Jonas Munksgaard","Sirakov, Georgi","Stilund, Morten","Schäfer, Jakob","Ratzer, Rikke","Frederiksen, Jette","Asgari, Nasrin","Ashna, Said Nasim","Jensen, Henrik Boye","Kant, Matthias","Theódorsdóttir, Ásta","Illes, Zsolt","Sellebjerg, Finn","Magyari, Melinda","Schlosser, Louise Mose","Nordborg, Hilde","Wergeland, Stig","Sejbaek, Tobias"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-715745"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sejbaek, Tobias"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Haukeland University Hospital","University of Bergen"],"keyword":["Adherence","Adverse events","Dimethyl Fumarate adverse effects","Dimethyl fumarate","Discontinuation","Female","Humans","Immunosuppressive Agents adverse effects","Male","Multiple Sclerosis Relapsing Remitting drug therapy","Multiple Sclerosis drug therapy","Multiple sclerosis","Nationwide registry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discontinuation of dimethyl fumarate in multiple sclerosis a nationwide study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85176426387","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank Claire Gudex, MD, for comments on an earlier version of this paper. Finn Sellebjerg holds a professorship at the Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine, University of Copenhagen, sponsored by the Danish Multiple Sclerosis Society."],"id":"S04-100.00-715745","identifier":[{"id":"85176426387","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37956521","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-a2ec0b1