iversities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d1a98f16-c4a5-4d40-a55f-0413c5ba48af"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A proteomics analysis of 5xFAD mouse brain regions reveals the lysosome-associated protein Arl8b as a candidate biomarker for Alzheimer’s disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-690424","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Studies suggest a link between particulate matter less than or equal to 2.5 μm in diameter (PM2.5) and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS), but to our knowledge critical exposure windows have not been examined. We performed a case-control study in the Danish population spanning the years 1989-2013. Cases were selected from the Danish National Patient Registry based on International Classification of Diseases codes. Five controls were randomly selected from the Danish Civil Registry and matched to a case on vital status, age, and sex. PM2.5 concentration at residential addresses was assigned using monthly predictions from a dispersion model. We used conditional logistic regression to estimate odds ratios (ORs) and 95% confidence intervals (CIs), adjusting for confounding. We evaluated exposure to averaged PM2.5 concentrations 12-24 months, 2-6 years, and 2-11 years pre-ALS diagnosis; annual lagged exposures up to 11 years prediagnosis; and cumulative associations for exposure in lags 1-5 years and 1-10 years prediagnosis, allowing for varying association estimates by year. We identified 3,983 cases and 19,915 controls. Cumulative exposure to PM2.5 in the period 2-6 years prediagnosis was associated with ALS (OR = 1.06, 95% CI: 0.99, 1.13). Exposures in the second, third, and fourth years prediagnosis were individually associated with higher odds of ALS (e.g., for lag 1, OR = 1.04, 95% CI: 1.00, 1.08). Exposure to PM2.5 within 6 years before diagnosis may represent a critical exposure window for ALS.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Nunez, Yanelli","Balalian, Arin","Parks, Robbie M.","He, Mike Z.","Hansen, Johnni","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Ketzel, Matthias","Khan, Jibran","Brandt, Jørge","Vermeulen, Roel","Peters, Susan","Weisskopf, Marc G.","Re, Diane B.","Goldsmith, Jeff","Kioumourtzoglou, Marianthi Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-694128"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nunez, Yanelli"],"country":["Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Columbia University","Harvard University","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","PSE Healthy Energy","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis","Case Control Studies","Environmental Exposure","Fine particulate matter","PM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring relevant time windows in the association between pm sub 000000000002 000000000005 sub exposure and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis a case control study in denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10666968/pdf/kwad099.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-694128","identifier":[{"id":"37092253","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85169503412","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10666968","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-b2bf145b-c9c7-42cb-84c6-f83b0b6bcb45"],"keyword":["PM","air pollution","amyotrophic lateral sclerosis","case-control studies","environmental exposure","exposure windows","fine particulate matter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-FFDC67385B2AEA6BFBCAC1694919431A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10666968/pdf/kwad099.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"columbia university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Columbia University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"pse healthy energy","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"PSE Healthy Energy","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"icahn school of medicine at mount sinai","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanelli","key":"nunezpau","last":"Nunez","name":"Nunez, Yanelli","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Arin","key":"balalianpau","last":"Balalian","name":"Balalian, Arin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robbie M.","key":"parkspau","last":"Parks","name":"Parks, Robbie M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike Z.","key":"hepau","last":"He","name":"He, Mike Z.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Johnni","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Johnni","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørge","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Jørge","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Roel","key":"vermeulenpau","last":"Vermeulen","name":"Vermeulen, Roel","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Susan","key":"peterspau","last":"Peters","name":"Peters, Susan","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc G.","key":"weisskopfpau","last":"Weisskopf","name":"Weisskopf, Marc G.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Diane B.","key":"repau","last":"Re","name":"Re, Diane B.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeff","key":"goldsmithpau","last":"Goldsmith","name":"Goldsmith, Jeff","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianthi Anna","key":"kioumourtzogloupau","last":"Kioumourtzoglou","name":"Kioumourtzoglou, Marianthi Anna","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37092253"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/aje/kwad099","issn":["00029262","14766256"],"issn_org":["00029262"],"issue":"9","journal":"American Journal of Epidemiology","pages":"1499-1508","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Epidemiology","volume":"192"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85169503412"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b2bf145b-c9c7-42cb-84c6-f83b0b6bcb45"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Exploring Relevant Time Windows in the Association Between PM<sub>2.5</sub> Exposure and Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis : A Case-Control Study in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-694128","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Long-Term air pollution is a risk factor for stroke. Which types and sources of air pollution contribute most to stroke in populations is unknown. We investigated whether risk of stroke differed by type and source of air pollution. Methods: We selected all persons aged >50 years and living in Denmark in the period 2005-17. We estimated running 5-year mean residential air-pollution concentrations of particulate matter <2.5 μm (PM2.5), ultrafine particles (UFP), elemental carbon (EC) and nitrogen dioxide (NO2). Pollutants were modelled as total air pollution from all emission sources, as well as apportioned into contributions from non-Traffic and traffic sources. Hazard ratios (HRs) and CIs were estimated by using Cox proportional hazards models, adjusting for area-level and personal demographic and socio-economic covariates. We identified all primary strokes from hospital and mortality registers. Results: The cohort numbered 2 million people and 94-256 cases of stroke. Interquartile ranges (IQR) of air pollution were associated with risk of stroke with HRs of 1.077 (95% CI: 1.061-1.094, IQR: 1.85 μg/m3) for PM2.5, 1.039 (1.026-1.052, IQR: 4248 particles/cm3) for UFP, 1.009 (1.001-1.018, IQR: 0.28 μg/m3) for EC and 1.028 (1.017-1.040, IQR: 7.15 μg/m3) for NO2. Traffic sources contributed little to the total exposure. HRs associated with air pollution from traffic were close to the null, whereas non-Traffic sources tended to be associated with HRs higher than those for total air pollution, e.g. for non-Traffic PM2.5, the HR was 1.091 (1.074-1.108). Conclusions: Air pollution, including UFP, was associated with risk of stroke. The risk appeared attributable mainly to air pollution from non-Traffic sources.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Sørensen, Mette","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Brandt, Jørgen","Frohn, Lise Marie","Ketzel, Matthias","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Im, Ulas","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-716029"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Cohort study","Epidemiology","Stroke","Ultrafine particles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"source specific air pollution and risk of stroke in denmark","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85154618667","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-716029","identifier":[{"id":"36921285","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85154618667","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-87ed83bd-4c9b-48cd-a4fb-76b2a9be1e9e","ruc-dc335edf-4894-4f99-848f-60dd3420c03d"],"keyword":["Air pollution","cohort study","epidemiology","stroke","ultrafine particles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CB10ECDACBE01D4CEAC9B201D7531E7A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Molecular and Medical Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, iCLIMATE Aarhus University Interdisciplinary Centre for Climate Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla Arthur","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Marie","key":"frohnpau","last":"Frohn","locid":"1db55612-df02-4189-ab0d-5c62193e1afc","name":"Frohn, Lise Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4236-5708","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper H.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","name_org":"Christensen, Jesper H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulas","key":"impau","last":"Im","locid":"e2356d82-8e7b-49c9-b660-76e719a4058e","name":"Im, Ulas","orcid":"0000-0001-5177-5306","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36921285"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ije/dyad030","issn":["03005771","14643685"],"issn_org":["03005771"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Epidemiology","pages":"727-737","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Epidemiology","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85154618667"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-87ed83bd-4c9b-48cd-a4fb-76b2a9be1e9e","ruc-dc335edf-4894-4f99-848f-60dd3420c03d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"'Source-specific' air pollution and risk of stroke in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-716029","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Acute and chronic pancreatitis constitute a continuum of inflammatory disease of the pancreas with an increasing incidence in most high-income countries. A subset of patients with a history of pancreatitis suffer from recurrence of acute pancreatitis attacks, which accelerate disease progression towards end-stage chronic pancreatitis with loss of exocrine and endocrine function. There is currently no available prophylactic treatment for recurrent acute pancreatitis apart from removing risk factors, which is not always possible. Pain is the primary symptom of acute pancreatitis, which induces the endogenous release of opioids. This may further be potentiated by opioid administration for pain management. Increased exposure to opioids leads to potentially harmful effects on the gastrointestinal tract, including, e.g. increased sphincter tones and decreased fluid secretion, which may impair pancreatic ductal clearance and elevate the risk for new pancreatitis attacks and accelerate disease progression. Peripherally acting µ-opioid receptor antagonists (PAMORAs) have been developed to counteract the adverse effects of opioids on the gastrointestinal tract. We hypothesize that the PAMORA naldemedine will reduce the risk of new pancreatitis attacks in patients with recurrent acute pancreatitis and hence decelerate disease progression. METHODS: The study is a double-blind, randomized controlled trial with allocation of patients to either 0.2 mg naldemedine daily or matching placebo for 12 months. A total of 120 outpatients will be enrolled from five specialist centres in Denmark and Sweden. The main inclusion criteria is a history of recurrent acute pancreatitis (minimum of two confirmed pancreatitis attacks). The primary endpoint is time to acute pancreatitis recurrence after randomization. Secondary outcomes include changes in quality of life, gastrointestinal symptom scores, new-onset diabetes, exocrine pancreatic insufficiency, disease severity, health care utilization, adherence to treatment, and frequency of adverse events. Exploratory outcomes are included for mechanistic linkage and include the progression of chronic pancreatitis-related findings on magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) and changes in circulating blood markers of inflammation and fibrosis. DISCUSSION: This study investigates if naldemedine can change the natural course of pancreatitis in patients with recurrent acute pancreatitis and improve patient outcomes. TRIAL REGISTRATION: EudraCT no. 2021-000069-34. CLINICALTRIALS: gov NCT04966559. Registered on July 8, 2021.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Cook, Mathias E","Knoph, Cecilie S","Fjelsted, Camilla A","Frøkjær, Jens B","Bilgrau, Anders E","Novovic, Srdan","Jørgensen, Maiken Thyregod","Mortensen, Michael Bau","Nielsen, Liv B J","Hadi, Amer","Berner-Hansen, Mark","Rutkowski, Wiktor","Vujasinovic, Miroslav","Löhr, Matthias","Drewes, Asbjørn M","Olesen, Søren S"],"cuid":["S03-099.97-741370"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cook, Mathias E","Cook, Mathias Ellgaard","Olesen, Søren Schou"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska University Hospital"],"keyword":["Acute Disease","Analgesics Opioid adverse effects","Disease Progression","Double Blind Method","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Naldemedine","Narcotic Antagonists adverse effects","Opioid","Pancreatitis Chronic drug therapy","Peripherally acting µ opioid receptor antagonist","Quality of Life","Randomized Controlled Trial","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Recurrent acute pancreatitis","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of a peripherally acting µ opioid receptor antagonist for the prevention of recurrent acute pancreatitis study protocol for an investigator initiated randomized placebo controlled double blind clinical trial pamora rap trial","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-023-07287-z","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The PAMORA-RAP study is an investigator-initiated trial. It is funded as part of an unrestricted grant by the Novo Nordisk Foundation. Shionogi BV also supports the study through a supply of study drug materials. The financial supporters have no influence on publication, study design, and data collection."],"id":"S03-099.97-741370","identifier":[{"id":"85157960978","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10150502","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37127657","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-4d6fea01-527b-42d7-aa5a-672f781a9c5a","ku-38878411-60e0-44ce-a704-7000c39ed492","sdu-3b575bca-11e4-477c-ae43-5991eed2aebd"],"keyword":["Acute Disease","Analgesics, Opioid/adverse effects","Disease Progression","Double-Blind Method","Humans","Magnetic resonance imaging","Naldemedine","Narcotic Antagonists/adverse effects","Opioid","Pancreatitis, Chronic/drug therapy","Peripherally acting µ-opioid receptor antagonist","Quality of Life","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Randomized controlled trial","Recurrent acute pancreatitis","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-6E54932E71992F59F26EEEA4851C89F9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/533076225/Cook_et_al._2023_._Effects_of_a_peripherally_acting_opioid_receptor_antagonist_for_the_preven