aaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37265507"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.lanepe.2023.100655","issn":["26667762"],"journal":"The Lancet Regional Health - Europe","paperid":"100655","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Regional Health - Europe","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160355885"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d85dd7c6-2c76-4366-9b35-fe3ce23b0e11","ruc-991ca6f0-1e2c-4d0c-bfc0-dcfe447cd762"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Concomitant exposure to air pollution, green space, and noise and risk of stroke : a cohort study from Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-681442","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Risk factors for malignant tumours of the central nervous system (CNS) are largely unknown. Methods: We pooled six European cohorts (N = 302,493) and assessed the association between residential exposure to nitrogen dioxide (NO2), fine particles (PM2.5), black carbon (BC), ozone (O3) and eight elemental components of PM2.5 (copper, iron, potassium, nickel, sulfur, silicon, vanadium, and zinc) and malignant intracranial CNS tumours defined according to the International Classification of Diseases ICD-9/ICD-10 codes 192.1/C70.0, 191.0–191.9/C71.0–C71.9, 192.0/C72.2–C72.5. We applied Cox proportional hazards models adjusting for potential confounders at the individual and area-level. Results: During 5,497,514 person-years of follow-up (average 18.2 years), we observed 623 malignant CNS tumours. The results of the fully adjusted linear analyses showed a hazard ratio (95% confidence interval) of 1.07 (0.95, 1.21) per 10 μg/m³ NO2, 1.17 (0.96, 1.41) per 5 μg/m³ PM2.5, 1.10 (0.97, 1.25) per 0.5 10−5m−1 BC, and 0.99 (0.84, 1.17) per 10 μg/m³ O3. Conclusions: We observed indications of an association between exposure to NO2, PM2.5, and BC and tumours of the CNS. The PM elements were not consistently associated with CNS tumour incidence.","author_count":31,"contributors":["Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Chen, Jie","Rodopoulou, Sophia","Strak, Maciej","de Hoogh, Kees","Andersen, Zorana J.","Bellander, Tom","Brandt, Jørgen","Fecht, Daniela","Forastiere, Francesco","Gulliver, John","Hertel, Ole","Hoffmann, Barbara","Katsouyanni, Klea","Ketzel, Matthias","Leander, Karin","Magnusson, Patrik K.E.","Nagel, Gabriele","Pershagen, Göran","Rizzuto, Debora","Samoli, Evangelia","So, Rina","Stafoggia, Massimo","Tjønneland, Anne","Weinmayr, Gudrun","Wolf, Kathrin","Zhang, Jiawei","Zitt, Emanuel","Brunekreef, Bert","Hoek, Gerard","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-686021"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur"],"country":["Austria","Germany","Greece","Italy","Netherlands","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Agency for Preventive and Social Medicine","All Global Affiliations","Department of Epidemiology, Lazio Regional Health Service","Dept Epidemiol Lazio Reg","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","Imperial College London","Karolinska Institutet","LKH Feldkirch","MRC Centre for Environment and Health","National Institute for Public Health and the Environment (RIVM)","National Institute of Public Health and the Environment","National and Kapodistrian University of Athens","Region Stockholm","Stockholm Gerontology Research Center","Swiss Tropical and Public Health Institute","Ulm University","University of Athens","University of Basel","University of Leicester","University of Surrey","Utrecht University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term air pollution exposure and malignant intracranial tumours of the central nervous system a pooled analysis of six european cohorts","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10421949/pdf/41416_2023_Article_2348.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-686021","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10421949","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37420001","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85164186719","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b14336b0-1a9f-4988-bb04-53cf82e9dbac","ku-0057cb28-