{"abstract":"State-of-the-art industrial electrocatalysts for the oxygen evolution reaction (OER) under acidic conditions are Ir-based. Considering the scarce supply of Ir, it is imperative to use the precious metal as efficiently as possible. In this work, we immobilized ultrasmall Ir and Ir0.4Ru0.6 nanoparticles on two different supports to maximize their dispersion. One high-surface-area carbon support serves as a reference but has limited technological relevance due to its lack of stability. The other support, antimony-doped tin oxide (ATO), has been proposed in the literature as a possible better support for OER catalysts. Temperature-dependent measurements performed in a recently developed gas diffusion electrode (GDE) setup reveal that surprisingly the catalysts immobilized on commercial ATO performed worse than their carbon-immobilized counterparts. The measurements suggest that the ATO support deteriorates particularly fast at elevated temperatures.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bornet, Aline","Pittkowski, Rebecca K.","Nielsen, Tobias M.","Berner, Etienne","Maletzko, Annabelle","Schröder, Johanna","Quinson, Jonathan","Melke, Julia","Jensen, Kirsten M.Ø.","Arenz, Matthias"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-686024"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Arenz, Matthias"],"country":["Germany","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fraunhofer Institute for Chemical Technology","University of Bern"],"keyword":["Oxygen evolution reaction","PEM water electrolysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of temperature on the performance of carbon and ato supported oxygen evolution reaction catalysts in a gas diffusion electrode setup","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acscatal.3c01193","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-686024","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10242686","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85162772707","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37288094","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b258563c-be32-490c-b40a-1ea1b18ad1dd","ku-f1fcc12b-7e33-40cc-a67e-2f7ed5b4bcd9"],"keyword":["GDE setup","Ir-based nanoparticles","PEM water electrolysis","oxygen evolution reaction","supported OER catalysts"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AD404D502CD2FCF0963FF0F9BB0CB7E6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10242686/pdf/cs3c01193.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acscatal.3c01193","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/358086274/acscatal.3c01193.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"university of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bern","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"fraunhofer institute for chemical technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fraunhofer Institute for Chemical Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Aline","key":"bornetpau","last":"Bornet","name":"Bornet, Aline","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rebecca","key":"pittkowskipau","last":"Pittkowski","locid":"448337eb-bd1c-4704-bc22-452c2f734a25","name":"Pittkowski, Rebecca K.","name_org":"Pittkowski, Rebecca","orcid":"0000-0002-0351-4993","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tobias M.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"25600acf-cbd9-42bd-85b7-46efed7ff0d4","name":"Nielsen, Tobias M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Etienne","key":"bernerpau","last":"Berner","name":"Berner, Etienne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Annabelle","key":"maletzkopau","last":"Maletzko","name":"Maletzko, Annabelle","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Johanna","key":"schröderpau","last":"Schröder","name":"Schröder, Johanna","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","country":"dk","first":"Jonathan","key":"quinsonpau","last":"Quinson","locid":"cc8174db-da46-46b9-9514-b5f0821164be","name":"Quinson, Jonathan","orcid":"0000-0002-9374-9330","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Julia","key":"melkepau","last":"Melke","name":"Melke, Julia","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kirsten M. Ø.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"057e5b4d-da43-4523-b326-379b0c747d06","name":"Jensen, Kirsten M.Ø.","name_org":"Jensen, Kirsten M. Ø.","orcid":"0000-0003-0291-217X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"arenzpau","last":"Arenz","name":"Arenz, Matthias","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37288094"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acscatal.3c01193","issn":["21555435"],"issue":"11","journal":"ACS Catalysis","pages":"7568-7577","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"ACS Catalysis","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85162772707"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b258563c-be32-490c-b40a-1ea1b18ad1dd","ku-f1fcc12b-7e33-40cc-a67e-2f7ed5b4bcd9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Influence of Temperature on the Performance of Carbon- and ATO-supported Oxygen Evolution Reaction Catalysts in a Gas Diffusion Electrode Setup","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-686024","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Thrombocytopenia (platelet count < 150 × 109/L) is common in intensive care unit (ICU) patients and is likely associated with worse outcomes. In this study we present international contemporary data on thrombocytopenia in ICU patients. Methods: We conducted a prospective cohort study in adult ICU patients in 52 ICUs across 10 countries. We assessed frequencies of thrombocytopenia, use of platelet transfusions and clinical outcomes including mortality. We evaluated pre-selected potential risk factors for the development of thrombocytopenia during ICU stay and associations between thrombocytopenia at ICU admission and 90-day mortality using pre-specified logistic regression analyses. Results: We analysed 1166 ICU patients; the median age was 63 years and 39.5% were female. Overall, 43.2% (95% confidence interval (CI) 40.4-46.1) had thrombocytopenia; 23.4% (20-26) had thrombocytopenia at ICU admission, and 19.8% (17.6-22.2) developed thrombocytopenia during their ICU stay. Absence of acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS), non-cancer-related immune deficiency, liver failure, male sex, septic shock, and bleeding at ICU admission were associated with the development of thrombocytopenia during ICU stay. Among patients with thrombocytopenia, 22.6% received platelet transfusion(s), and 64.3% of in-ICU transfusions were prophylactic. Patients with thrombocytopenia had higher occurrences of bleeding and death, fewer days alive without the use of life-support, and fewer days alive and out of hospital. Thrombocytopenia at ICU admission was associated with 90-day mortality (adjusted odds ratio 1.7; 95% CI 1.19-2.42). Conclusion: Thrombocytopenia occurred in 43% of critically ill patients and was associated with worse outcomes including increased mortality. Platelet transfusions were given to 23% of patients with thrombocytopenia and most were prophylactic.","author_count":120,"contributors":["Anthon, Carl Thomas","Pène, Frédéric","Perner, Anders","Azoulay, Elie","Puxty, Kathryn","Van De Louw, Andry","Barratt-Due, Andreas","Chawla, Sanjay","Castro, Pedro","Póvoa, Pedro","Coelho, Luis","Metaxa, Victoria","Kochanek, Matthias","Liebregts, Tobias","Kander, Thomas","Hästbacka, Johanna","Andreasen, Jo Bønding","Péju, Edwige","Nielsen, Lene Bjerregaard","Hvas, Christine Lodberg","Dufranc, Etienne","Canet, Emmanuel","Lundqvist, Linda","Wright, Christopher John","Schmidt, Julien","Uhel, Fabrice","Ait-Oufella, Hafid","Krag, Mette","Cos Badia, Elisabet","Díaz-Lagares, Cándido","Menat, Sophie","Voiriot, Guillaume","Clausen, Niels Erikstrup","Lorentzen, Kristian","Kvåle, Reidar","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Holten, Aleksander Rygh","Strand, Kristian","Tzalavras, Asterios","Bestle, Morten H.","Klepstad, Pål","Fernandez, Sara","Vimpere, Damien","Costa, Carolina","Graça, Carina","Lueck, Catherina","Juhl, Christian Svendsen","Costa, Carolina","Bådstøløkken, Per Martin","Miranda, Teresa","Lêdo, Lia Susana Aires","Sousa Torres, Joao Carlos","Granholm, Anders","Møller, Morten Hylander","Russell, Lene","Khalil, Ahmed","Yehia, Ahmed","Salem, Haney","Farahat, Hesham","Sudevan, Manu","Biggart, Melissa","Fatima, Nirmeen","Elkhonezy, Mohammed","Bunzel, Anne Marie","Siegumfeldt, Rine M.","Vestergaard, Stine R.","Pelle, Juliette","Lê, Minh Pierre","Vigneron, Clara","Bertrix, Morgane","Cirera, Paul","Laghlam, Driss","Bredin, Swann","Marin, Nathalie","Toppenberg, Maria","Benelli, Brice","Seguin, Amélie","Garret, Charlotte","Guillotin, Florian","Blonz, Gauthier","Lascarrou, Jean Baptiste","Lemarie, Jérémie","Desmedt, Luc","Agbakou, Maïté","Carpentier, Mathieu","Martin, Maëlle","Benkalfate, Naïla","Zambon, Olivier","Decamps, Paul","Wilquin, Pauline L.","Benguerfi, Soraya","Gardner, John","Remor, Natalie","Carr, Sheila","Yang, Gloria","Gernez, Coralie","Thiry, Ingrid","Missri, Louai","Denneborg, Moritz K.G.","Brown, Katherine","Casares, Vanessa","Sivula, Mirka","Lappi, Elina","Pettilä, Leena","Heinonen, Jonna","Saario, Minttu","Mecheri, Manal K.","Elabb