rtal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695426","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"PARP14 is a mono-ADP-ribosyl transferase involved in the control of immunity, transcription, and DNA replication stress management. However, little is known about the ADP-ribosylation activity of PARP14, including its substrate specificity or how PARP14-dependent ADP-ribosylation is reversed. We show that PARP14 is a dual-function enzyme with both ADP-ribosyl transferase and hydrolase activity acting on both protein and nucleic acid substrates. In particular, we show that the PARP14 macrodomain 1 is an active ADP-ribosyl hydrolase. We also demonstrate hydrolytic activity for the first macrodomain of PARP9. We reveal that expression of a PARP14 mutant with the inactivated macrodomain 1 results in a marked increase in mono(ADP-ribosyl)ation of proteins in human cells, including PARP14 itself and antiviral PARP13, and displays specific cellular phenotypes. Moreover, we demonstrate that the closely related hydrolytically active macrodomain of SARS2 Nsp3, Mac1, efficiently reverses PARP14 ADP-ribosylation in vitro and in cells, supporting the evolution of viral macrodomains to counteract PARP14-mediated antiviral response.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Đukić, Nina","Strømland, Øyvind","Elsborg, Jonas D.","Munnur, Deeksha","Zhu, Kang","Schuller, Marion","Chatrin, Chatrin","Kar, Pulak","Duma, Lena","Suyari, Osamu","Rack, Johannes Gregor Matthias","Baretić, Domagoj","Crudgington, Dorian Richard Kenneth","Groslambert, Joséphine","Fowler, Gerissa","Wijngaarden, Sven","Prokhorova, Evgeniia","Rehwinkel, Jan","Schüler, Herwig","Filippov, Dmitri V.","Sanyal, Sumana","Ahel, Dragana","Nielsen, Michael L.","Smith, Rebecca","Ahel, Ivan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695671"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leiden University","Lund University","University of Bergen","University of Exeter","University of Oxford"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parp000000000014 is a parp with both adp ribosyl transferase and hydrolase activities","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.adi2687","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695671","identifier":[{"id":"85171240255","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10499325","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37703374","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-388a7770-2a26-49c1-b3f2-dfa51129d116"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2FB4F7AFC9AA443FA0FDDD9F3E387B4C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/380152676/sciadv.adi2687.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.adi2687","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of bergen","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Bergen","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Nielsen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of exeter","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","O