Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-388a7770-2a26-49c1-b3f2-dfa51129d116"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"PARP14 is a PARP with both ADP-ribosyl transferase and hydrolase activities","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695671","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Thrombocytopenia (platelet count < 150 × 109/L) is common in intensive care unit (ICU) patients and is likely associated with worse outcomes. In this study we present international contemporary data on thrombocytopenia in ICU patients. Methods: We conducted a prospective cohort study in adult ICU patients in 52 ICUs across 10 countries. We assessed frequencies of thrombocytopenia, use of platelet transfusions and clinical outcomes including mortality. We evaluated pre-selected potential risk factors for the development of thrombocytopenia during ICU stay and associations between thrombocytopenia at ICU admission and 90-day mortality using pre-specified logistic regression analyses. Results: We analysed 1166 ICU patients; the median age was 63 years and 39.5% were female. Overall, 43.2% (95% confidence interval (CI) 40.4–46.1) had thrombocytopenia; 23.4% (20–26) had thrombocytopenia at ICU admission, and 19.8% (17.6–22.2) developed thrombocytopenia during their ICU stay. Absence of acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS), non-cancer-related immune deficiency, liver failure, male sex, septic shock, and bleeding at ICU admission were associated with the development of thrombocytopenia during ICU stay. Among patients with thrombocytopenia, 22.6% received platelet transfusion(s), and 64.3% of in-ICU transfusions were prophylactic. Patients with thrombocytopenia had higher occurrences of bleeding and death, fewer days alive without the use of life-support, and fewer days alive and out of hospital. Thrombocytopenia at ICU admission was associated with 90-day mortality (adjusted odds ratio 1.7; 95% CI 1.19–2.42). Conclusion: Thrombocytopenia occurred in 43% of critically ill patients and was associated with worse outcomes including increased mortality. Platelet transfusions were given to 23% of patients with thrombocytopenia and most were prophylactic.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Anthon, Carl Thomas","Pène, Frédéric","Perner, Anders","Azoulay, Elie","Puxty, Kathryn","Van De Louw, Andry","Barratt-Due, Andreas","Chawla, Sanjay","Castro, Pedro","Póvoa, Pedro","Coelho, Luis","Metaxa, Victoria","Kochanek, Matthias","Liebregts, Tobias","Kander, Thomas","Hästbacka, Johanna","Andreasen, Jo Bønding","Péju, Edwige","Nielsen, Lene Bjerregaard","Hvas, Christine Lodberg","Dufranc, Etienne","Canet, Emmanuel","Lundqvist, Linda","Wright, Christopher John","Russell, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713884"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["The PLOT-ICU Collaborators and the Nine-I Study Group"],"corresponding_author":["Russell, Lene"],"country":["Finland","France","Germany","Norway","Portugal","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Essen University Hospital","Glasgow Royal Infirmary","Hospital Cochin","Hospital Henri Mondor","King's College London","Lund University","Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center","NOVA University Lisbon","Oslo University Hospital","Paris Hospitals and Paris Descartes University","San Francisco Xavier Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","Tampere University Hospital","The Pennsylvania State University","University Hospital Cologne","University Hospital of Nantes","University of Barcelona","University of Helsinki","Weill Cornell Medicine","the Queen Elisabeth University Hospital"],"keyword":["Adult","Bleeding","Cohort Studies","Critical Illness","Female","Hemorrhage etiology","Humans","Intensive Care Units","Intensive care unit","Male","Middle Aged","Platelet Transfusion","Platelet Transfusion adverse effects","Prospective Studies","Retrospective Studies","Thrombocytopenia","Thrombocytopenia epidemiology","Thrombosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thrombocytopenia and platelet transfusions in icu patients an international inception cohort study plot icu","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00134-023-07225-2","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by Royal Library, Copenhagen University Library. This study was funded by the Research Council of Rigshospitalet, the Ehrenreich’s Foundation, and the Dagmar Marshalls Foundation. The Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center part of the study was supported by the Core Grant, Grant/Award Number: P30CA008748; Department of Anaesthesiology & Critical Care Medicine, Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center, New York, NY, United States of America. None of the funders had any influence on the design, conduct or reporting of the study. The Department of Intensive Care at Rigshospitalet (CTA, AG, MHM, AP, LR) has received funding for other projects from the Novo Nordisk Foundation, Sygeforsikringen ‘danmark’, and Pfizer and has conducted contract research for AM-Pharma. FP has received honoraria for consulting and lectures from Gilead and an institutional grant from Alexion Pharma. AP has received honoraria from Novartis for participation in an advisory board. EA has received research grants from MSD Avenir and Alexion and honoraria for lectures from Alexion, Sanofi and Pfizer. . AVDL has received honoraria from Sanofi for participation in an advisory board. PC has received consulting fees from Sanofi, Gilead, Alexion and Janssen and honoraria for lectures from Merck Sharp & Dohme, Gilead, Alexion and Pfizer. PP has received consulting fees from Sanofi and Gilead and honoraria from Merck Sharp & Dohme, Gilead, Mundipharma and Pfizer for academic and educational work. JH has received consulting fees from Paion and honoraria for lectures from the Finnish Medical Association, Laboratory Medicine and Duodecim. EC received fees for lectures and conference talks and had travel and accommodation expenses related to attending scientific meetings covered by Gilead, Shionogi B.V. and Sanofi-Genzyme. ARH has received honoraria from Pfizer for lectures. MHB has received consulting fees from AM-pharma and Inotrem. Full disclosure forms from all authors are available on the publisher’s website."],"id":"S01-000.00-713884","identifier":[{"id":"85173919249","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37812225","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10622358","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-3fad97e7-4f48-4344-ae4b-da65d16ce35e"],"keyword":["Adult","Bleeding","Cohort Studies","Critical illness","Female","Hemorrhage/etiology","Humans","Intensive Care Units","Intensive care unit","Male","Middle Aged","Platelet Transfusion/adverse effects","Platelet transfusion","Prospective Studies","Retrospective Studies","Thrombocytopenia","Thrombocytopenia/epidemiology","Thrombosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-7-9ECC96A66D9A34EA2B4235917CCB7021"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00134-023-07225-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/244460272/s00134_023_07225_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"hospital cochin","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hospital Cochin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key