:"10.1056/evidoa2200137","issn":["27665526"],"issue":"11","journal":"NEJM Evidence","publisher":"NEJM Group","status":"p","title":"NEJM Evidence","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-eeb1fada-73fc-43cf-b382-6a5e6bed2223"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Hypothermic versus Normothermic Temperature Control after Cardiac Arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-641577","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Row-column (RC) arrays have the potential to yield full three-dimensional ultrasound imaging with a greatly reduced number of elements compared to fully populated arrays. They, however, have several challenges due to their special geometry. This review paper summarizes the current literature for RC imaging and demonstrate that full anatomic and functional imaging can attain a high quality using synthetic aperture (SA) sequences and modified delay-and-sum beamforming. Resolution can approach the diffraction limit with an isotropic resolution of half a wavelength with low side-lobe levels, and the field-of-view can be expanded by using convex or lensed RC probes. GPU beamforming allows for 3 orthogonal planes to be beamformed at 30 Hz, providing near real time imaging ideal for positioning the probe and improving the operator’s workflow. Functional imaging is also attainable using transverse oscillation and dedicated SA sequence for tensor velocity imaging for revealing the full 3-D velocity vector as a function of spatial position and time for both blood velocity and tissue motion estimation. Using RC arrays with commercial contrast agents can reveal super resolution imaging with isotropic resolution below 20 μm. RC arrays can, thus, yield full 3-D imaging at high resolution, contrast, and volumetric rates for both anatomic and functional imaging with the same number of receive channels as current commercial 1-D arrays.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","Schou, Mikkel","Jørgensen, Lasse Thurmann","Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Traberg, Marie Sand","Taghavi, Iman","Øygard, Sigrid Husebø","Ommen, Martin Lind","Steenberg, Kitty","Thomsen, Erik Vilain","Panduro, Nathalie Sarup","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin"],"cuid":["S02-083.59-036831"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Arrays","Focusing","Image resolution","Imaging","Probes","Transducers","Ultrasonic imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anatomic and functional imaging using row column arrays","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TUFFC.2022.3191391","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.59-036831","identifier":[{"id":"85135217571","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35839193","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-bacabf35-8103-484c-99cd-8876489e5018","ku-cd7494c5-36a5-4ee1-93da-9a89cbe0b554"],"keyword":["Arrays","Focusing","Image resolution","Imaging","Probes","Transducers","Ultrasonic imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-725464B637D51861F64024577807CFCE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/281006897/Anatomic_and_Functional_Imaging_using_Row_Column_Arrays.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TUFFC.2022.3191391","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/324605579/Anatomic_and_Functional_Imaging_Using_RowColumn_Arrays.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, UltraSound and Biomechanics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, UltraSound and Biomechanics, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Renal and Vascular Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"02abcc96-628c-467d-9117-1d3a80866a55","name":"Schou, Mikkel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lasse Thurmand","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"7b9450b3-eb94-4c95-92bd-38088a185f80","name":"Jørgensen, Lasse Thurmann","name_org":"Jørgensen, Lasse Thurmand","orcid":"0000-0002-2426-2502","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Borislav G.","key":"tomovpau","last":"Tomov","locid":"16c6d791-3a1a-47ad-a725-2da30c420dee","name":"Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev","name_org":"Tomov, Borislav G.","orcid":"0000-0003-4236-3056","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Sand","key":"trabergpau","last":"Traberg","locid":"4da6fca0-b677-4b9a-a006-a87b72ac6ee3","name":"Traberg, Marie Sand","orcid":"0000-0001-7090-6607","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iman","key":"taghavipau","last":"Taghavi","locid":"70860894-0180-4faf-a270-c7e761b81abc","name":"Taghavi, Iman","orcid":"0000-0002-2551-074X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sigrid Husebø","key":"øygardpau","last":"Øygard","locid":"91316990-5af9-4a30-8cfc-d293dc4bd2e5","name":"Øygard, Sigrid Husebø","orcid":"0000-0002-3021-7812","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Lind","key":"ommenpau","last":"Ommen","locid":"e7aebb26-b70d-4857-8c80-0040af9b6102","name":"Ommen, Martin Lind","orcid":"0000-0001-9206-6426","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kitty","key":"steenbergpau","last":"Steenberg","locid":"a72e02cb-f9b3-4cb6-a35e-d4690431e8b8","name":"Steenberg, Kitty","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Vilain","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"822fe159-0932-4e5e-aeb6-b8b7f8421ab0","name":"Thomsen, Erik Vilain","orcid":"0000-0002-2772-926X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nathalie Sarup","key":"panduropau","last":"Panduro","locid":"890df0ad-606b-47f5-bb91-ff2c12a142cf","name":"Panduro, Nathalie Sarup","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Mehlin","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","locid":"0ceca69d-e5cd-43dc-9995-305ac5855c4f","name":"Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","name_org":"Sorensen, Charlotte Mehlin","orcid":"0000-0002-9984-3125","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35839193"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tuffc.2022.3191391","issn":["08853010","15258955"],"issn_org":["15258955"],"issue":"10","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics and Frequency Control","pages":"2722-2738","paperid":"9830770","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics and Frequency Control","title_org":"IEEE Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics, and Frequency Control","volume":"69"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135217571"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bacabf35-8103-484c-99cd-8876489e5018","ku-cd7494c5-36a5-4ee1-93da-9a89cbe0b554"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Anatomic and Functional Imaging using Row-Column Arrays","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.59-036831","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Current super resolution imaging is conducted using ultrasound contrast agents, where a sparse distribution ofbubbles must be employed to separate individual targets. Thesparse targets make the acquisition time long in the range of1 to 10 minutes, and therefore demands an accurate motioncorrection over a long time. The employment of a contrastagent also lowers MI to below 0.2 to not disrupt the bubbles,with a corresponding lower signal-to-noise ratio in the images.A new method, SURE (SUper Resolution ultrasound imagingusing Erythrocytes), where erythrocytes are used as targets, issuggested to alleviate these problems. Perfused tissues containan abundance of targets, and the full clinical pressure rangecan be used. It is hypothesized that super resolution imagingbelow the diffraction limit can be attained in seconds usingSURE imaging. A SURE processing pipeline was developed withmodules for beamforming, tissue motion estimation, alignment,singular value decomposition for echo canceling, and subsequentpeak detection in the speckle pattern. The detected peaks weresummed in a high-resolution image for yielding the SURE image.Data were acquired using a 10 MHz linear array GE L10-18i probe (150 µm wavelength) and a Verasonics Vantage 256scanner. A synthetic aperture scan sequence with 12 emissionswas employed at a pulse repetition frequency of 5 kHz for a 417Hz frame rate. Kidneys of Sprague-Dawley rats were scanned for24 seconds and RF data stored for off-line processing. The excisedkidneys were micro-CT scanned for 11 hours for generatingreference maps of the vasculature with a voxel size of 21 µm.SURE images revealed vessels with sizes down to 50 µm. Fourierring correlations between independent images measured for 12s revealed a resolution between 25 to 49 µm, demonstrating thesuper resolution capability of the method. The SURE images areobtained in 1 to 12 seconds, demand no injection of intravenouscontrast agents, and can use the full pressure and intensityrange allowed in medical ultrasound, making the method easilyadaptable to clinical use.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","Schou, Mikkel","Andersen, Sofie Bech","Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev","Søgaard, Stinne Byrholdt","Sorensen, Charlotte Mehlin","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Gundlach, Carsten","Kjer, Hans Martin","Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","Stuart, Matthias Bo"],"cuid":["S02-086.95-033610"],"event":{"end":"2022-10-13","place":"Venice, it","start":"2022-10-10","title":"2022 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium, IUS 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Flow imaging","Super resolution imaging","Synthetic aperture","Ultrasound imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in vivo super resolution ultrasound imaging using the erythrocytes sure","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/298004686/sure_imaging.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-086.95-033610","identifier":[{"id":"85143770850","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2e8e67a1-b3b4-471b-90dc-d4c0808d8ab2","ku-e619008c-02f5-473b-a598-a6d781f85374"],"keyword":["Flow imaging","Super resolution imaging","Synthetic aperture","Ultrasound imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-84A02B709C3CDD5444C947DC79382EDB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/365659241/sure_imaging_2_5.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/298004686/sure_imaging.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, UltraSound and Biomechanics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, UltraSound and Biomechanics, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"02abcc96-628c-467d-9117-1d3a80866a55","name":"Schou, Mikkel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Sofie Bech","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"f3c55705-abf7-42f3-8a61-116b8a3f8a0c","name":"Andersen, Sofie Bech","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Borislav G.","key":"tomovpau","last":"Tomov","locid":"16c6d791-3a1a-47ad-a725-2da30c420dee","name":"Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev","name_org":"Tomov, Borislav G.","orcid":"0000-0003-4236-3056","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Stinne Byrholdt","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"bba245e9-b5c7-4b46-8a05-554f0d8380eb","name":"Søgaard, Stinne Byrholdt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Mehlin","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"0ceca69d-e5cd-43dc-9995-305ac5855c4f","name":"Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","orcid":"0000-0002-9984-3125","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten","key":"gundlachpau","last":"Gundlach","locid":"65d0727c-226e-4de2-8573-92fc7b62cce6","name":"Gundlach, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0002-2895-1882","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Martin","key":"kjerpau","last":"Kjer","locid":"a9705d27-ba4f-4760-8bb7-d2ddf31adf9f","name":"Kjer, Hans Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-7900-5733","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bjorholm","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"c2bad3c8-b172-481b-bb99-d3c2bc4004ef","name":"Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","orcid":"0000-0002-0068-8170","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ius54386.2022.9958236","eisbn":["9781665466578"],"isbn":["9781665478137"],"issn":["19485719"],"journal":"IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium, IUS","pages":"1-4","status":"p","title":"IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium, IUS","volume":"2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143770850"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2e8e67a1-b3b4-471b-90dc-d4c0808d8ab2","ku-e619008c-02f5-473b-a598-a6d781f85374"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"In Vivo Super Resolution Ultrasound Imaging using the Erythrocytes - SURE","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.95-033610","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Only few epidemiological studies have investigated whether chronic exposure to air pollution from different sources have different impacts on risk of diabetes. We aimed to investigate associations between air pollution from traffic versus non-traffic sources and risk of type 2 diabetes in the Danish population. Methods: We estimated long-term exposure to traffic and non-traffic contributions of particulate matter with a diameter <2.5 μg (PM2.5), elemental carbon (EC), ultrafine particles (UFP) and nitrogen dioxide (NO2) for all persons living in Denmark for the period 2005-17. In total, 2.6 million persons aged >35 years were included, of whom 148 020 developed type 2 diabetes during follow-up. We applied Cox proportional hazards models for analyses, using 5-year time-weighted running means of air pollution and adjustment for individual-and area-level demographic and socioeconomic covariates. Results: We found that 5-year exposure to all particle measures (PM2.5, UFP and EC) and NO2 were associated with higher type 2 diabetes risk. We observed that for UFP, EC and potentially PM2.5, the pollution originating from traffic was associated with higher risks than the non-traffic contributions, whereas for NO2 similar hazard ratios (HR) were observed. For example, in two-source models, hazard ratios (HRs) per interquartile change in traffic UFP, EC and PM2.5 were 1.025, 1.045 and 1.036, respectively, whereas for non-traffic UFP, EC and PM2.5, the HRs were 1.013, 1.018 and 1.001, respectively. Conclusions: Our finding of stronger associations with particulate matter from traffic compared with non-traffic sources implies that prevention strategies should focus on limiting traffic-related particulate matter air pollution.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Sørensen, Mette","Poulsen, Aslak H.","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","Frohn, Lise Marie","Ketzel, Matthias","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Brandt, Jørgen","Geels, Camilla","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-026655"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Mette"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Public health","Type 2 diabetes","Ultrafine particles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exposure to source specific air pollution and risk for type 000000000002 diabetes a nationwide study covering denmark","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://academic.oup.com/ije/article/51/4/1219/6548226?login=true","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-026655","identifier":[{"id":"85136176827","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000768460500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"35285908","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c0ae6804-d861-4195-8f3a-6852044af1c4","ruc-2cc5356f-2de1-47a7-9457-c0b0a854578f"],"keyword":["Air pollution","public health","type 2 diabetes","ultrafine particles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-789FD3B188092844554F43365B94EFF9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research cente