7c-aea1-1583ff080dc9","ku-4597cdf0-257b-46ea-b624-5c2f59c1187c","sdu-4a6861bf-45e5-4670-a7fa-e045c9e099e8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Polygenic risk modeling for prediction of epithelial ovarian cancer risk","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-088.69-008887","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We assessed mortality risks associated with sourcespecific fine particles (PM2.5) in a pooled European cohort of 323,782 participants. Cox proportional hazard models were applied to estimate mortality hazard ratios (HRs) for source-specific PM2.5 identified through a source apportionment analysis. Exposure to 2010 annual average concentrations of source-specific PM2.5 components was assessed at baseline residential addresses. The source apportionment resulted in the identification of five sources: traffic, residual oil combustion, soil, biomass and agriculture, and industry. In single-source analysis, all identified sources were significantly positively associated with increased natural mortality risks. In multisource analysis, associations with all sources attenuated but remained statistically significant with traffic, oil, and biomass and agriculture. The highest association per interquartile increase was observed for the traffic component (HR: 1.06; 95% CI: 1.04 and 1.08 per 2.86 mu g/m(3) increase) across five identified sources. On a 1 mu g/m(3) basis, the residual oil-related PM2.5 had the strongest association (HR: 1.13; 95% CI: 1.05 and 1.22), which was substantially higher than that for generic PM2.5 mass, suggesting that past estimates using the generic PM2.5 exposure response function have underestimated the potential clean air health benefits of reducing fossil-fuel combustion. Source-specific associations with cause-specific mortality were in general consistent with findings of natural mortality.","author_count":44,"contributors":["Chen, Jie","Hoek, Gerard","De Hoogh, Kees","Rodopoulou, Sophia","Andersen, Zorana J.","Bellander, Tom","Brandt, Jørgen","Fecht, Daniela","Forastiere, Francesco","Gulliver, John","Hertel, Ole","Hoffmann, Barbara","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Verschuren, W. M.Monique","Jöckel, Karl Heinz","Jørgensen, Jeanette T.","Katsouyanni, Klea","Ketzel, Matthias","Méndez, Diego Yacamán","Leander, Karin","Liu, Shuo","Ljungman, Petter","Faure, Elodie","Magnusson, Patrik K.E.","Nagel, Gabriele","Pershagen, Göran","Peters, Annette","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Rizzuto, Debora","Samoli, Evangelia","Van Der Schouw, Yvonne T.","Schramm, Sara","Severi, Gianluca","Stafoggia, Massimo","Strak, Maciej","Sørensen, Mette","Tjønneland, Anne","Weinmayr, Gudrun","Wolf, Kathrin","Zitt, Emanuel","Brunekreef, Bert","Thurston, George D."],"cuid":["S03-096.62-020553"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Chen, Jie"],"country":["Austria","France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Netherlands","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Agency for Preventive and Social Medicine","All Global Affiliations","Ctr Epidemiol & Community Med","Ctr Occupat & Environm Med","Danderyd Hospital","Danderyds Hospital","Department of Epidemiology Lazio Regional Health Service","Dept Epidemiol Lazio Reg","German Centre for Cardiovascular Research","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Helmholtz Munich","Imperial College London","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","LKH Feldkirch","LKH Feldkirch, Dept Internal Med","Lazio Region Hlth Serv, Dept Epidemiol","Ludwig Maximilian University","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","National Institute for Public Health and the Environment","National Institute for Public Health and the Environment (RIVM)","National and Kapodistrian University of Athens","New York University","Region Stockholm","Stockholm University","Swedish National Board of Health and Welfare","Swiss Tropical and Public Health Institute","Ulm University","Universite Paris-Saclay","University Medical Center Utrecht","University Medical Centre Utrecht","University of Athens","University of Basel","University of Duisburg-Essen","University of Florence","University of Leicester","University of Surrey","Université Paris-Saclay","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Components","Health","Heart disease","Mortality","NO2","Particulate matter","Risk Factors","Source apportionment","Spatial variation","USE REGRESSION MODELS","absolute principal component analysis APCA","fine particulate matter PM","fine particulate matter PM2 5"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to source specific fine particles and mortality a pooled analysis of 000000000014 european cohorts within the elapse project","src":["au","ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.est.2c01912","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-096.62-020553","identifier":[{"id":"85134084148","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000819118300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9261290","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35737879","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6c1a8cba-1cee-4e38-9986-8a460f90d3a2","ku-74d1c566-d302-4496-93de-6c3b3b79ce7a","ruc-50b5f648-c4da-4c5e-9d32-583bf14a6dd2"],"keyword":["AIR-POLLUTION","COMPONENTS","HEALTH","HEART-DISEASE","NO2","PARTICULATE MATTER","RISK-FACTORS","SPATIAL VARIATION","USE REGRESSION-MODELS","absolute principal component analysis (APCA)","fine particulate matter (PM)","fine particulate matter (PM2.5)","mortality","source apportionment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-BF27D3E9CB60FD715EED4E85C8578F9A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.est.2c01912","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license"