:42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bert","key":"brunekreefpau","last":"Brunekreef","name":"Brunekreef, Bert","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerard","key":"hoekpau","last":"Hoek","name":"Hoek, Gerard","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35717714"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envint.2022.107341","issn":["01604120","18736750"],"issn_org":["01604120"],"journal":"Environment International","paperid":"107341","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Environment International","volume":"166"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132333563"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-993e2595-fe03-4916-acd3-2a174f922ec0","ku-f5415a14-3c4d-4a0f-9ef3-eac247ba1fa5","ruc-bf4058ca-4295-43ad-ad8b-cb45003fab98"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Exposure to surrounding greenness and natural-cause and cause-specific mortality in the ELAPSE pooled cohort","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.68-023823","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"RATIONALE: Ambient air pollution exposure has been linked to mortality from chronic cardiorespiratory diseases, while evidence on respiratory infections remains more limited. OBJECTIVES: We examined the association between long-term exposure to air pollution and pneumonia related mortality in adults in a pool of eight European cohorts. METHODS: Within the multicenter project 'Effects of Low-Level Air Pollution: A Study in Europe' (ELAPSE), we pooled data from eight cohorts among six European countries. Annual mean residential concentrations in 2010 for fine particulate matter (PM 2.5), nitrogen dioxide (NO 2), black carbon (BC), and ozone (O 3) were estimated using Europe-wide hybrid land use regression models. We applied stratified Cox proportional hazard models to investigate the associations between air pollution and pneumonia, influenza, and acute lower respiratory infections (ALRI) mortality. MEASUREMENTS AND MAIN RESULTS: Of 325,367 participants, 712 died from pneumonia and influenza combined, 682 from pneumonia, and 695 from ALRI during a mean follow-up of 19.5 years. NO 2 and BC were associated with 10-12% increases in pneumonia and influenza combined mortality, but 95% confidence intervals included unity [hazard ratios: 1.12 (0.99-1.26) per 10 µg/m 3 for NO 2; 1.10 (0.97-1.24) per 0.5 10 -5m -1 for BC]. Associations with pneumonia and ALRI mortality were almost identical. We detected effect modification suggesting stronger associations with NO 2 or BC in overweight, employed, or currently smoking participants compared to normal weight, unemployed, or non-smoking participants. CONCLUSIONS: Long-term exposure to combustion-related air pollutants NO 2 and BC may be associated with mortality from lower respiratory infections, but larger studies are needed to estimate these associations more precisely.","author_count":51,"contributors":["Liu, Shuo","Lim, Youn Hee","Chen, Jie","Strak, Maciek","Wolf, Kathrin","Weinmayr, Gudrun","Rodopolou, Sophia","de Hoogh, Kees","Bellander, Tom","Brandt, Jørgen","Concin, Hans","Zitt, Emanuel","Fecht, Daniela","Forastiere, Francesco","Gulliver, John","Hertel, Ole","Hoffmann, Barbara","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","Monique Verschuren, W. M.","Jockel, Karl Heinz","Jørgensen, Jeanette T.","So, Rina","Amini, Heresh","Cole-Hunter, Thomas","Mehta, Amar J.","Mortensen, Laust H.","Ketzel, Matthias","Lager, Anton","Leander, Karin","Ljungman, Petter","Severi, Gianluca","Boutron-Ruault, Marie Christine","Magnusson, Patrik K.E.","Nagel, Gabriele","Pershagen, Goran","Peters, Annette","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Rizzuto, Debora","van der Schouw, Yvonne T.","Schramm, Sara","Sørensen, Mette","Stafoggia, Massimo","Tjønneland, Anne","Katsouyanni, Klea","Huang, Wei","Samoli, Evangelia","Brunekreef, Bert","Hoek, Gerard","Andersen, Zorana J."],"cuid":["S03-099.08-030467"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Zorana J."],"country":["Austria","China","France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Netherlands","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Agency for Preventive and Social Medicine","All Global Affiliations","Danderyds Hospital","Department of Epidemiology Lazio Regional Health Service","Dept Epidemiol Lazio Reg","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Helmholtz Munich","Imperial College London","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","King's College London","LKH Feldkirch","Ludwig Maximilian University","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","National Institute for Public Health and the Environment","National Institute for Public Health and the Environment (RIVM)","National and Kapodistrian University of Athens","Peking University","Region Stockholm","Stockholm Gerontology Research Center","Swiss Tropical and Public Health Institute","Ulm University","Universite Paris-Saclay","University Medical Center Utrecht","University of Athens","University of Basel","University of Duisburg-Essen","University of Florence","University of Leicester","University of Surrey","Université Paris-Saclay","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["ADULTS","Air pollution","Long term exposure","Respiratory infections"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term air pollution exposure and pneumonia related mortality in a large pooled european cohort","src":["au","ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1164/rccm.202106-1484OC","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.08-030467","identifier":[{"id":"85132314944","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35258439","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f6d824f1-5557-42a8-bd3e-cabbdfe6fe43","ku-a7e885be-56bb-41a1-a42b-6f86c9f7bbce","ruc-f7623604-9584-45f2-90be-a54247548203"],"keyword":["adults","air pollution","long-term exposure","respiratory infections"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-84D3B112484E09C9EBD763C3B3B11295"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1164/rccm.202106-1484OC","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379030576/511318117.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University o