{"abstract":"Since requirements of service demands are becoming increasingly complex and diversified, one of the success factors of a multimodal service system is its capability to design a specific service instance satisfying a specific set of requirements. This capability is further highlighted in Ad Hoc Multimodal Service Systems (AHMSSs), where service instances rarely follow a standard form of service delivery and exist only for a limited time. However, due to the increasing scale and frequency of services in many business and public sectors, meeting the desired level of capability has become troublesome. A well-designed Artificial Intelligence (AI) approach can be a solution to the difficulty by addressing the underlying complexity and uncertainty of the AHMSS design process. To conceptualize and foster AI applications to an AHMSS, this study identifies key decision-making problems in the AHMSS design process and discusses the role of AI in the process. The results will form the basis for AI development and implementation for an AHMSS and relevant service systems.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sung, Inkyung","Buderath, Matthias","Nielsen, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-076578"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["Airbus Group","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Decision support system","Machine learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unpacking the role of artificial intelligence for a multimodal service system design","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/electronics11040549","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-076578","identifier":[{"id":"85124289490","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5b6859dc-c9ca-4058-ad0b-b9ea94e9e33f"],"keyword":["Ad Hoc Multimodal Service System","Artificial intelligence","Decision support system","Decision-making augmentation","Decision-making automation","Machine learning","Resource constraint project scheduling problem"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B40CD27616A6207248CDF60F755C912D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/482738825/electronics_11_00549_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/electronics11040549","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Artificial Intelligence for Operations Research","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Production","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"airbus group","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Airbus Group","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Inkyung","key":"sungpau","last":"Sung","locid":"0838305b-c1e4-48fa-9494-07506f4fc072","name":"Sung, Inkyung","orcid":"0000-0002-7045-8143","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"buderathpau","last":"Buderath","name":"Buderath, Matthias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6e9311e7-df36-48ff-816c-ca6b88e405f0","name":"Nielsen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-4882-7942","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/electronics11040549","issn":["20799292"],"issue":"4","journal":"Electronics","paperid":"549","publisher":"MDPI AG","status":"p","title":"Electronics","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124289490"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5b6859dc-c9ca-4058-ad0b-b9ea94e9e33f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Unpacking the Role of Artificial Intelligence for a Multimodal Service System Design","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-076578","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) is a fatal neurodegenerative disease. Limited evidence suggests ALS diagnosis may be associated with air pollution exposure and specifically traffic-related pollutants. METHODS: In this population-based case-control study, we used 3,937 ALS cases from the Danish National Patient Register diagnosed during 1989-2013 and matched on age, sex, year of birth, and vital status to 19,333 population-based controls free of ALS at index date. We used validated predictions of elemental carbon (EC), nitrogen oxides (NO x ), carbon monoxide (CO), and fine particles (PM 2.5 ) to assign 1-, 5-, and 10-year average exposures pre-ALS diagnosis at study participants' present and historical residential addresses. We used an adjusted Bayesian hierarchical conditional logistic model to estimate individual pollutant associations and joint and average associations for traffic-related pollutants (EC, NO x , CO). RESULTS: For a standard deviation (SD) increase in 5-year average concentrations, EC (SD = 0.42 µg/m 3 ) had a high probability of individual association with increased odds of ALS (11.5%; 95% credible interval [CrI] = -1.0%, 25.6%; 96.3% posterior probability of positive association), with negative associations for NO x (SD = 20 µg/m 3 ) (-4.6%; 95% CrI = 18.1%, 8.9%; 27.8% posterior probability of positive association), CO (SD = 106 µg/m 3 ) (-3.2%; 95% CrI = 14.4%, 10.0%; 26.7% posterior probability of positive association), and a null association for nonelemental carbon fine particles (non-EC PM 2.5 ) (SD = 2.37 µg/m 3 ) (0.7%; 95% CrI = 9.2%, 12.4%). We found no association between ALS and joint or average traffic pollution concentrations. CONCLUSIONS: This study found high probability of a positive association between ALS diagnosis and EC concentration. Further work is needed to understand the role of traffic-related air pollution in ALS pathogenesis.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Parks, Robbie M.","Nunez, Yanelli","Balalian, Arin A.","Gibson, Elizabeth A.","Hansen, Johnni","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Ketzel, Matthias","Khan, Jibran","Brandt, Jørgen","Vermeulen, Roel","Peters, Susan","Goldsmith, Jeff","Re, Diane B.","Weisskopf, Marc G.","Kioumourtzoglou, Marianthi Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-198157"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Columbia University","Harvard University","University of Surrey","Utrecht University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term traffic related air pollutant exposure and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis diagnosis in denmark a bayesian hierarchical analysis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9381567/pdf/41396_2022_Article_1276.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-198157","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9560992","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85139739020","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35944145","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-78489551-34b2-4e53-8732-1db069c02ab9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-65DDD8B0EAA4490174E5904EABF32BFF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9381567/pdf/41396_2022_Article_1276.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"columbia university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],