Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139739020"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-78489551-34b2-4e53-8732-1db069c02ab9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Long-term Traffic-related Air Pollutant Exposure and Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis Diagnosis in Denmark : A Bayesian Hierarchical Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-198157","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Microbubble (MB) tracking is an integral part of super-resolution ultrasound imaging by providing sharper images and enabling velocity estimation. Tracking the MBs from the last to the first frame can generate different trajectories than tracking from the first to the last frame, when the next positions of a track depends on its previous positions, e.g., in Kalman-based methods. Our hypothesis is that tracking in a forward-backward manner can increase the overall tracking performance. In simulations, MB positions with a parabolic flow profile were generated inside two tubes. Three different tracking methods, including nearest-neighbor, Kalman, and hierarchical Kalman, were investigated. Using the proposed forward-backward strategy, all estimated velocity profiles for all trackers were improved and were closer to the actual velocity profiles with an improvement between 28% to 40% in the relative standard deviation (RSD) of the velocity values over 10 cross-sections of the tubes. A Sprague Dawley rat kidney was scanned for 10 minutes using a BK5000 scanner and X18L5s transducer, which is a linear array probe with 150 elements. The tracking results from the in vivo experiments showed that the combined image of the forward and backward tracks had 35% additional unique track positions. It showed a clear visual enhancement in the super-resolved velocity map. Overall, the improvement in visual aspects and velocity estimates suggest forward-backward strategy as an upgrade for Kalman-based trackers.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Taghavi, Iman","Andersen, Sofie Bech","Schou, Mikkel","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Jensen, Jorgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-394516"],"event":{"end":"2022-03-27","place":"Virtual, Online","start":"2022-03-21","title":"Medical Imaging 2022: Ultrasonic Imaging and Tomography","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Particle tracking","Super resolution imaging","Ultrasound microscopy","Velocity estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microbubble tracking with a forward backward strategy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359081117/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-394516","identifier":[{"id":"85132036747","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-01b9293e-e8ee-4d21-bf22-8a099a9f0b9b"],"keyword":["Particle tracking","Super-resolution imaging","ultrasound microscopy","velocity estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-B9E393953899DB660C5E664AD9294F73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359081117/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Iman","key":"taghavipau","last":"Taghavi","name":"Taghavi, Iman","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sofie Bech","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Sofie Bech","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","name":"Schou, Mikkel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Mehlin","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","locid":"0ceca69d-e5cd-43dc-9995-305ac5855c4f","name":"Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","name_org":"Sorensen, Charlotte Mehlin","orcid":"0000-0002-9984-3125","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jorgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jorgen Arendt","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1117/12.2610753","issn":["0277786X","1996756X"],"issn_org":["16057422"],"journal":"Proceedings of SPIE - The International Society for Optical Engineering","paperid":"120380C","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of SPIE - The International Society for Optical Engineering","title_org":"Progress in Biomedical Optics and Imaging - Proceedings of SPIE","volume":"12038"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132036747"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-01b9293e-e8ee-4d21-bf22-8a099a9f0b9b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Microbubble tracking with a forward-backward strategy","typ