":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bert","key":"brunekreefpau","last":"Brunekreef","name":"Brunekreef, Bert","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerard","key":"hoekpau","last":"Hoek","name":"Hoek, Gerard","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 13","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36154858"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envres.2022.114385","issn":["00139351","10960953"],"issn_org":["00139351"],"journal":"Environmental Research","paperid":"114385","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Environmental Research","volume":"215"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138810938"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-390bee12-1777-4d49-bc38-3cfca2d3f05b","ku-673f7213-7775-4f0f-b59a-fca8cc26facb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long term exposure to air pollution and kidney parenchyma cancer – Effects of low-level air pollution : a Study in Europe (ELAPSE)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.88-016836","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Targeted temperature management (TTM) is recommended following cardiac arrest; however, time to target temperature varies in clinical practice. We hypothesised the effects of a target temperature of 33 °C when compared to normothermia would differ based on average time to hypothermia and those patients achieving hypothermia fastest would have more favorable outcomes. Methods: In this post-hoc analysis of the TTM-2 trial, patients after out of hospital cardiac arrest were randomized to targeted hypothermia (33 °C), followed by controlled re-warming, or normothermia with early treatment of fever (body temperature, ≥ 37.8 °C). The average temperature at 4 h (240 min) after return of spontaneous circulation (ROSC) was calculated for participating sites. Primary outcome was death from any cause at 6 months. Secondary outcome was poor functional outcome at 6 months (score of 4–6 on modified Rankin scale). Results: A total of 1592 participants were evaluated for the primary outcome. We found no evidence of heterogeneity of intervention effect based on the average time to target temperature on mortality (p = 0.17). Of patients allocated to hypothermia at the fastest sites, 71 of 145 (49%) had died compared to 68 of 148 (46%) of the normothermia group (relative risk with hypothermia, 1.07; 95% confidence interval 0.84–1.36). Poor functional outcome was reported in 74/144 (51%) patients in the hypothermia group, and 75/147 (51%) patients in the normothermia group (relative risk with hypothermia 1.01 (95% CI 0.80–1.26). Conclusions: Using a hospital’s average time to hypothermia did not significantly alter the effect of TTM of 33 °C compared to normothermia and early treatment of fever.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Simpson, Rupert F.G.","Dankiewicz, Josef","Karamasis, Grigoris V.","Pelosi, Paolo","Haenggi, Matthias","Young, Paul J.","Jakobsen, Janus Christian","Bannard-Smith, Jonathan","Wendel-Garcia, Pedro D.","Taccone, Fabio Silvio","Nordberg, Per","Wise, Matt P.","Grejs, Anders Morten","Lilja, Gisela","Olsen, Roy Bjørkholt","Cariou, Alain","Lascarrou, Jean Baptiste","Saxena, Manoj","Hovdenes, Jan","Thomas, Matthew","Friberg, Hans","Davies, John R.","Nielsen, Niklas","Keeble, Thomas R."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-020035"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Keeble, Thomas R."],"country":["Australia","Belgium","France","Italy","New Zealand","Norway","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anglia Ruskin School of Medicine","Anglia Ruskin University","Bankstown-Lidcombe Hospital","Bansltwon-Lidcombe Hospital","Capital & Coast District Health Board","Cardiff University","Department of Genetic Medicine, Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, Manchester, United Kingdom.","Hospital of Southern Norway","IRCCS Azienda Ospedaliera Universitaria San Martino IST","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Lund University","MSE Trust","Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust","Medical Research Institute of New Zealand","Mid and South Essex NHS Foundation Trust","Monash University","Oslo University Hospital","Paris Cité University","San Martino Hospital Genoa","Universite Paris 5","Universite de Nantes","University Hospital Wales","University Hospital Zurich","University Hospital of Bern","University Hospital of Nantes","University Hospitals Bristol and Weston NHS Foundation Trust","University of Bern","University of Genoa","University of Manchester","University of Melbourne","University of New South Wales","University of Oslo","University of Zurich","Université Libre de Bruxelles","Wellington Hospital"],"keyword":["Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Cold Temperature","Fever therapy","Humans","Hypothermia","Hypothermia Induced","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest therapy","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Temperature management","Time to target temperature","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"speed of cooling after cardiac arrest in relation to the intervention effect a sub study from the ttm000000000002 trial","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-022-04231-6","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Dr Young reports receiving lecture fees from Bard Medical. Dr Wise receives honoraria from Gilead and Fisher & Paykel for educational lectures. Dr Keeble reports receiving lecture fees from BD, and a research grant from Zoll. Dr Cariou received fees from Bard Medical. Professor Taccone receives lecture fees from BD and ZOLL. Professor Friberg is a scientific advisor TEQCool (Lund, Sweden)."],"id":"S02-100.00-020035","identifier":[{"id":"85141954930","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9667681","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36380332","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-651ded4e-2e8c-46dd-af7f-bc4a2b39cdd6","sdu-7e41f1f5-de00-40bf-894b-ac56bbb5d34a"],"keyword":["Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation","Cold Temperature","Fever/therapy","Humans","Hypothermia","Hypothermia, Induced","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest/therapy","Temperature management","Time to target temperature","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C0C80909A930FA88CB6D7BCC12D6D28D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-022-04231-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files