Hans Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-7900-5733","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bjorholm","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"c2bad3c8-b172-481b-bb99-d3c2bc4004ef","name":"Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","orcid":"0000-0002-0068-8170","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Borislav Gueorguiev","key":"tomovpau","last":"Tomov","locid":"16c6d791-3a1a-47ad-a725-2da30c420dee","name":"Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev","orcid":"0000-0003-4236-3056","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1117/12.2612245","isbn":["9781510649514"],"issn":["0277786X"],"publisher":"SPIE - International Society for Optical Engineering","series":"Proceedings of SPIE - The International Society for Optical Engineering","status":"p","title":"Medical Imaging 2022: Ultrasonic Imaging and Tomography"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132027562"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6b040938-985f-41f2-b6d0-6c34655dd73c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fast super resolution ultrasound imaging using the erythrocytes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-336540","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Microbubble (MB) tracking is an integral part of super-resolution ultrasound imaging by providing sharper images and enabling velocity estimation. Tracking the MBs from the last to the first frame can generate different trajectories than tracking from the first to the last frame, when the next positions of a track depends on its previous positions, e.g., in Kalman-based methods. Our hypothesis is that tracking in a forward-backward manner can increase the overall tracking performance. In simulations, MB positions with a parabolic flow profile were generated inside two tubes. Three different tracking methods, including nearest-neighbor, Kalman, and hierarchical Kalman, were investigated. Using the proposed forward-backward strategy, all estimated velocity profiles for all trackers were improved and were closer to the actual velocity profiles with an improvement between 28% to 40% in the relative standard deviation (RSD) of the velocity values over 10 cross-sections of the tubes. A Sprague Dawley rat kidney was scanned for 10 minutes using a BK5000 scanner and X18L5s transducer, which is a linear array probe with 150 elements. The tracking results from the in vivo experiments showed that the combined image of the forward and backward tracks had 35% additional unique track positions. It showed a clear visual enhancement in the super-resolved velocity map. Overall, the improvement in visual aspects and velocity estimates suggest forward-backward strategy as an upgrade for Kalman-based trackers.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Taghavi, Iman","Bech Andersen, Sofie","Schou, Mikkel","Bachmann Nielsen, Michael","Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352185"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Particle tracking","Super resolution imaging","Ultrasound microscopy","Velocity estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microbubble tracking with a forward backward strategy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/273457541/Iman_SPIE2022_ver_4.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352185","identifier":[{"id":"85132036747","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9f935535-e2fd-43fb-ab43-07aac8d7e9a1"],"keyword":["Particle tracking","Super-resolution imaging","Ultrasound microscopy","Velocity estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-B9E393953899DB660C5E664AD9294F73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/273457541/Iman_SPIE2022_ver_4.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, UltraSound and Biomechanics, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iman","key":"taghavipau","last":"Taghavi","locid":"70860894-0180-4faf-a270-c7e761b81abc","name":"Taghavi, Iman","orcid":"0000-0002-2551-074X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie","key":"bechandersenpau","last":"Bech Andersen","name":"Bech Andersen, Sofie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"02abcc96-628c-467d-9117-1d3a80866a55","name":"Schou, Mikkel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"bachmannnielsenpau","last":"Bachmann Nielsen","name":"Bachmann Nielsen, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Mehlin","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1117/12.2610753","issn":["0277786X"],"publisher":"SPIE - International Society for Optical Engineering","series":"Proceedings of SPIE - The International Society for Optical Engineering","status":"p","subtitle":"Ultrasonic Imaging and Tomography","title":"Medical Imaging 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132036747"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9f935535-e2fd-43fb-ab43-07aac8d7e9a1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Microbubble tracking with a forward-backward strategy","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352185","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Targeted temperature management at 33 °C (TTM33) has been employed in effort to mitigate brain injury in unconscious survivors of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA). Current guidelines recommend prevention of fever, not excluding TTM33. The main objective of this study was to investigate if TTM33 is associated with mortality in patients with vasopressor support on admission after OHCA. Methods: We performed a post hoc analysis of patients included in the TTM-2 trial, an international, multicenter trial, investigating outcomes in unconscious adult OHCA patients randomized to TTM33 versus normothermia. Patients were grouped according to level of circulatory support on admission: (1) no-vasopressor support, mean arterial blood pressure (MAP) ≥ 70 mmHg; (2) moderate-vasopressor support MAP < 70 mmHg or any dose of dopamine/dobutamine or noradrenaline/adrenaline dose ≤ 0.25 µg/kg/min; and (3) high-vasopressor support, noradrenaline/adrenaline dose > 0.25 µg/kg/min. Hazard ratios with TTM33 were calculated for all-cause 180-day mortality in these groups. Results: The TTM-2 trial enrolled 1900 patients. Data on primary outcome were available for 1850 patients, with 662, 896, and 292 patients in the, no-, moderate-, or high-vasopressor support groups, respectively. Hazard ratio for 180-day mortality was 1.04 [98.3% CI 0.78–1.39] in the no-, 1.22 [98.3% CI 0.97–1.53] in the moderate-, and 0.97 [98.3% CI 0.68–1.38] in the high-vasopressor support groups with regard to TTM33. Results were consistent in an imputed, adjusted sensitivity analysis. Conclusions: In this exploratory analysis, temperature control at 33 °C after OHCA, compared to normothermia, was not associated with higher incidence of death in patients stratified according to vasopressor support on admission. Trial registration Clinical trials identifier NCT02908308, registered September 20, 2016.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Düring, Joachim","Annborn, Martin","Cariou, Alain","Chew, Michelle S.","Dankiewicz, Josef","Friberg, Hans","Haenggi, Matthias","Haxhija, Zana","Jakobsen, Janus Christian","Langeland, Halvor","Taccone, Fabio Silvio","Thomas, Matthew","Ullén, Susann","Wise, Matt P.","Nielsen, Niklas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-602939"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Düring, Joachim"],"country":["Belgium","France","Norway","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Erasme University Hospital ULB","Hospital Cochin","Linköping University","Lund University","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","St. Olav University Hospital","University Hospital Wales","University Hospital of Bern","University Hospitals Bristol and Weston NHS Foundation Trust"],"keyword":["Adult","Cardiac arrest","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation methods","Epinephrine therapeutic use","Heart Arrest","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Hypothermia Induced methods","Mortality","Norepinephrine therapeutic use","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest drug therapy","Shock","Sudden","Temperature","Vasoconstrictor Agents therapeutic use"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of temperature management at 000000000033 c versus normothermia on survival in patients with vasopressor support after out of hospital cardiac arrest a post hoc analysis of the ttm 000000000002 trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-022-04107-9","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by Lund University. Funding was supported by independent research grants from nonprofit or governmental agencies (the Swedish Research Council [Vetenskapsrådet], Swedish Heart–Lung Foundation, Stig and Ragna Gorthon Foundation, Knutsson Foundation, Laerdal Foundation, Hans-Gabriel and Alice Trolle-Wachtmeister Foundation for Medical Research, and Regional Research Support in Region Skåne), and by governmental funding of clinical research within the Swedish National Health Service."],"id":"S01-000.00-602939","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9339193","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35909163","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85135198391","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-67df65cc-2dc7-44c6-8a58-feda3bf7e60f"],"keyword":["Adult","Cardiac arrest","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation/methods","Epinephrine/therapeutic use","Heart arrest","Humans","Hypothermia induced","Hypothermia, Induced/methods","Mortality","Norepinephrine/therapeutic use","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest/drug therapy","Shock","Sudden","Temperature","Vasoconstrictor Agents/therapeutic use"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-21FB167B0574A9C3C81AFABA85D9535C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/205206413/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-022-04107-9","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"hospital cochin","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hospital Cochin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"linköping university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Linköping University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"university hospital of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital