ine","volume":"79"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130847985"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-430d7d38-5207-4ef7-a96f-a54f1dcb96a3","ruc-ea434095-301e-436a-9a30-ad2cc5298db9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Occupational noise exposure and risk of incident stroke : a pooled study of five Scandinavian cohorts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.86-017552","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: The aetiology of most childhood cancers remains poorly understood. We conducted a nationwide register-based case-control study to assess the association between residential road traffic and railway noise exposure and risk of childhood cancers. Methods: We identified all cases of first cancers diagnosed in children aged 0–19 years in 1985–2013 from the Danish Cancer Registry (N = 3962) and sampled four individually matched (by sex and date of birth) controls per case (N = 14,790) using the Central Population Register. We estimated time-weighted exposure averages of residential road traffic and railway noise at the most (Lden max) and least (Lden min) exposed façades from birth to index-date (for additional analysis: in utero period) based on the individual address history for the respective time windows. We fitted conditional logistic regression models to estimate odds ratios (OR) and their 95% confidence intervals (CI). Results: ORs varied by noise estimate and cancer type, with generally wide CIs mostly including 1.00. We found a tendency of higher ORs with increasing railway and road traffic noise for Hodgkin lymphoma (ORs for railway and road Lden min were 1.63 (95% CI 1.00; 2.66) and 1.14 (95% CI 0.87; 1.48) per 10 dB), as well as a tendency of higher ORs with increasing railway noise for non-Hodgkin lymphoma. For embryonal CNS tumours and astrocytoma and other glioma we observed also some weak suggestions of a positive association. Analysing exposure to traffic noise in utero revealed similar patterns to those of the main analyses. Conclusions: This nationwide study with minimal risk of bias suggests no strong associations between traffic noise and risk of most childhood cancers. We found however some suggestive evidence for a positive association with Hodgkin lymphoma, non-Hodgkin lymphoma and some CNS tumours. Further research is warranted to confirm these associations in other populations and elucidate the underlying biological mechanisms.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Erdmann, Friederike","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Ketzel, Matthias","Brandt, Jørgen","Khan, Jibran","Schüz, Joachim","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013683"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Erdmann, Friederike"],"country":["France","Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","International Agency for Research on Cancer","International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC)","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","University Medical Center Mainz","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Central nervous system tumours","Childhood cancer","Denmark","Lymphoma","Register based study","Residential environmental noise"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"residential road traffic and railway noise and risk of childhood cancer a nationwide register based case control study in denmark","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85127688442","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-013683","identifier":[{"id":"85127688442","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35395236","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0f10d5fc-eb5b-4c49-9aef-085b012fac0a","ruc-e81af6b2-5826-4973-8311-a424826d3519"],"keyword":["Central nervous system tumours","Childhood cancer","Denmark","Lymphoma","Register-based study","Residential environmental noise"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FE408BCBD9B29E50482C68A0453563E9"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"johannes gutenberg university mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"international agency for research on cancer","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC)","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university medical center mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Friederike","key":"erdmannpau","last":"Erdmann","name":"Erdmann, Friederike","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla Arthur","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":"schüzpau","last":"Schüz","name":"Schüz, Joachim","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 7","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35395236"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envres.2022.113180","issn":["00139351","10960953"],"issn_org":["00139351"],"issue":"Part A","journal":"Environmental Research","paperid":"113180","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Environmental Research","volume":"212"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127688442"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0f10d5fc-eb5b-4c49-9aef-085b012fac0a","ruc-e81af6b2-5826-4973-8311-a424826d3519"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Residential road traffic and railway noise and risk of childhood cancer : A nationwide register-based case-control study in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-013683","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Exposure to outdoor air pollution is associated with adverse health effects. Previous studies have indicated higher levels of air pollution in socially deprived areas. Aim: To investigate associations between air pollution and socio-demographic variables, comorbidity, stress, and green space at the residence in Denmark. Methods: We included 2,237,346 persons living in Denmark, aged 35 years or older in 2017. We used the high resolution, multi-scale DEHM/UBM/AirGIS air pollution modelling system to calculate mean concentrations of air pollution with PM2.5, elemental carbon, ultrafine particles and NO2 at residences held the preceding five years. We used nationwide registries to retrieve information about socio-demographic indicators at the individual and neighborhood levels. We used general linear regression models to analyze associations between socio-demographic indicators and air pollution at the residence. Results: Individuals with high SES (income, higher white-collar worker and high educational level) and of non-Danish origin were exposed to higher levels of air pollution than individuals of low SES and of Danish origin, respectively. We found comparable levels of air pollution according to sex, stress events and morbidity. For neighborhood level SES indicators, we found high air pollution levels in neighborhoods with low SES measured as proportion of social housing, sole providers, low income and unemployment. In contrast, we found higher air pollution levels in neighborhoods with higher educational level and a low proportion of manual labor. People living in an apartment and/or with little green space had higher air pollution levels. Conclusion: In Denmark, high levels of residential air pollution were associated with higher individual SES and non-Danish origin. For neighborhood-level indicators of SES, no consistent pattern was observed. These results highlight the need for analyzing many different socio-demographic indicators to understand the complex associations between SES and exposure to air pollution.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Taj, Tahir","Poulsen, Aslak H.","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","Ketzel, Matthias","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Brandt, Jørgen","Frohn, Lise Marie","Geels, Camilla","Valencia, Victor H.","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-025140"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Elemental carbon","PM","Social inequality","Socioeconomic","Ultrafine particles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"air pollution at the residence of danish adults by socio demographic characteristics morbidity and address level characteristics","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85122681400","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-025140","identifier":[{"id":"35031338","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85122681400","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ab096379-bc39-4735-97de-8946cacf468d","ruc-1c2e5a23-70c1-4f33-ac80-5c8ab5affbd7"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Elemental carbon","NO","PM","Social inequality","Socioeconomic","Ultrafine particles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-58A13E9CA6866B66796185E66A959E7C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affn