{"abstract":"Epidemiologic studies have indicated that cruciferous vegetables can influence the cancer risk; therefore, we examined with a cross-sectional approach the correlation between the frequent consumption of the total cruciferous vegetables and the formation of bulky DNA damage, a biomarker of carcinogen exposure and cancer risk, in the Gen-Air study within the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (EPIC) cohort. DNA damage measurements were performed in the peripheral blood of 696 of those apparently healthy without cancer controls, including 379 never-smokers and 317 former smokers from seven European countries by the P-32-postlabeling assay. In the Gen-Air controls, the median intake of cruciferous vegetables was 6.16 (IQR 1.16-13.66) g/day, ranging from 0.37 (IQR 0-6.00) g/day in Spain to 11.34 (IQR 6.02-16.07) g/day in the UK. Based on this information, participants were grouped into: (a) high consumers (>20 g/day), (b) medium consumers (3-20 g/day) and (c) low consumers (","author_count":26,"contributors":["Peluso, Marco","Munnia, Armelle","Russo, Valentina","Galli, Andrea","Pala, Valeria","van der Schouw, Yvonne T.","Schulze, Matthias B.","Weiderpass, Elisabete","Tumino, Rosario","Saieva, Calogero","Exezarreta Pilar, Amiano","Aune, Dagfinn","Heath, Alicia K.","Aglago, Elom","Agudo, Antonio","Panico, Salvatore","Petersen, Kristina Elin Nielsen","Tjønneland, Anne","Cirera, Lluis","Rodriguez-Barranco, Miguel","Katzke, Verena","Kaaks, Rudolf","Ricceri, Fulvio","Milani, Lorenzo","Vineis, Paolo","Sacerdote, Carlotta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-410948"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["AIRE ONLUS, Hyblean Assoc Epidemiol Res","All Global Affiliations","Bellvitge Biomedical Research Institute","Ctr Canc Prevent CPO","German Cancer Research Center","IRCCS Fondazione Istituto Nazionale per lo studio e la cura dei tumori - Milano","ISPRO Study Prevent & Oncol Network Inst, Canc Risk Factors & Life Style Epidemiol Unit","ISPRO Study Prevent & Oncol Network Inst, Reg Canc Prevent Lab, Res Branch","Imperial College London","Institute for Biosanitary Research of Granada (ibs.GRANADA)","Instituto de Salud Carlos III","International Agency for Research on Cancer (WHO-IARC), Lyon","University Medical Centre Utrecht","University of Florence","University of Murcia","University of Naples Federico II","University of Potsdam","University of Turin"],"keyword":["Apiaceous vegetables","Colorectal cancer","Cruciferous vegetables","DNA damage","Diet","EPIC","Lung cancer risk","Nutrition","Smoking"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cruciferous vegetable intake and bulky dna damage within non smokers and former smokers in the gen air study epic cohort","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu14122477","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-410948","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9231287","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35745207","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85132311366","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000819081600001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-1d6bca76-96b3-4a23-bb2e-743ec4d9b39f"],"keyword":["4-AMINOBIPHENYL-HEMOGLOBIN ADDUCTS","ADDUCT LEVELS","APIACEOUS VEGETABLES","B(a)P-adducts","COLORECTAL-CANCER","DNA damage","EPIC","LUNG-CANCER RISK","NUTRITION","P-32-POSTLABELING DETECTION","SMOKING","WESTERN LIGURIA","bulky oxidative lesions","cruciferous vegetables","diet"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ED3BD3016B2B1AF2756C087845DCDF05"],"oa