ntake and Bulky DNA Damage within Non-Smokers and Former Smokers in the Gen-Air Study (EPIC Cohort)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-410948","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The rate at which oral tobacco-derived nicotine (OTDN) and snus pouches release nicotine into saliva is crucial to determine product performance. As no standardized method is available for this purpose, this study sought to develop a biorelevant dissolution method that could both discriminate between different products and predict in vivo behavior. Using a mu DISS Profiler (TM) as a surrogate for the US Pharmacopoeia standard apparatuses and a custom-made sinker, nicotine release from an OTDN pouch product (ZYN(R) Dry Smooth) and a snus product (General(R) Pouched Snus White Portion Large) was determined in biorelevant volumes (10 mL) of artificial saliva. In addition, nicotine extraction in vivo was measured for both products. Strikingly, the method showed distinct dissolution curves for OTDN and snus pouches, and the nicotine release observed in vitro did not significantly differ from the nicotine extracted in vivo. The custom-made sinker was designed to accommodate both loose and pouched oral tobacco/nicotine products, and thus the proposed in vitro dissolution method is suitable to assess nicotine release from OTDN and snus pouches. Apart from providing individual dissolution curves, the method was also able to predict in vivo nicotine extraction. Thus, this method could serve as a (biorelevant) monograph for product equivalence studies.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Knopp, Matthias Manne","Kiil-Nielsen, Nikolai K.","Masser, Anna E.","Staaf, Mikael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-412474"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Swedish Match North Europe AB"],"keyword":["Equivalence","Snus","constituents"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introducing a novel biorelevant in vitro dissolution method for the assessment of nicotine release from oral tobacco derived nicotine otdn and snus products","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/separations9020052","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-412474","identifier":[{"id":"85125082013","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000765534300001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-1ff257be-d225-49ff-bfe8-8c7e0a1cf72c"],"keyword":["CONSTITUENTS","equivalence","nicotine dissolution","nicotine extraction","nicotine release","oral tobacco derived nicotine (OTDN) pouches","snus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-38C0B237615DD77AF656A0516F3E3E2E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/separations9020052","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/302450363/separations_09_00052.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Physiological Pharmaceutics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"swedish match north europe ab","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish Match North Europe AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias M.","key":"knopppau","last":"Knopp","locid":"6cca090a-8c4e-4190-8316-bf9826e6ce90","name":"Knopp, Matthias Manne","name_org":"Knopp, Matthias M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nikolai K.","key":"kiilnielsenpau","last":"Kiil-Nielsen","name":"Kiil-Nielsen, Nikolai K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anna E.","key":"masserpau","last":"Masser","name":"Masser, Anna E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mikael","key":"staafpau","last":"Staaf","name":"Staaf, Mikael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/separations9020052","issn":["22978739"],"issue":"2","journal":"Separations","paperid":"52","status":"p","title":"Separations","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125082013"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1ff257be-d225-49ff-bfe8-8c7e0a1cf72c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introducing a Novel Biorelevant In Vitro Dissolution Method for the Assessment of Nicotine Release from Oral Tobacco-Derived Nicotine (OTDN) and Snus Products","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-412474","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"ADP-ribosylation, a modification of proteins, nucleic acids, and metabolites, confers broad functions, including roles in stress responses elicited, for example, by DNA damage and viral infection and is involved in intra- and extracellular signaling, chromatin and transcriptional regulation, protein biosynthesis, and cell death. ADP-ribosylation is catalyzed by ADP-ribosyltransferases (ARTs), which transfer ADP-ribose from NAD+ onto substrates. The modification, which occurs as mono- or poly-ADP-ribosylation, is reversible due to the action of different ADP-ribosylhydrolases. Importantly, inhibitors of ARTs are approved or are being developed for clinical use. Moreover, ADP-ribosylhydrolases are being assessed as therapeutic targets, foremost as antiviral drugs and for oncological indications. Due to the development of novel reagents and major technological advances that allow the study of ADP-ribosylation in unprecedented detail, an increasing number of cellular processes and pathways are being identified that are regulated by ADP-ribosylation. In addition, characterization of biochemical and structural aspects of the ARTs and their catalytic activities have expanded our understanding of this protein family. This increased knowledge requires that a common nomenclature be used to describe the relevant enzymes. Therefore, in this viewpoint, we propose an updated and broadly supported nomenclature for mammalian ARTs that will facilitate future discussions when addressing the biochemistry and biology of ADP-ribosylation. This is combined with a brief description of the main functions of mammalian ARTs to illustrate the increasing diversity of mono- and poly-ADP-ribose mediated cellular processes.","author_count":47,"contributors":["Lüscher, Bernhard","Ahel, Ivan","Altmeyer, Matthias","Ashworth, Alan","Bai, Peter","Chang, Paul","Cohen, Michael","Corda, Daniela","Dantzer, Françoise","Daugherty, Matthew D.","Dawson, Ted M.","Dawson, Valina L.","Deindl, Sebastian","Fehr, Anthony R.","Feijs, Karla L.H.","Filippov, Dmitri V.","Gagné, Jean Philippe","Grimaldi, Giovanna","Guettler, Sebastian","Hoch, Nicolas C.","Hottiger, Michael O.","Korn, Patricia","Kraus, W. Lee","Ladurner, Andreas","Lehtiö, Lari","Leung, Anthony K.L.","Lord, Christopher J.","Mangerich, Aswin","Matic, Ivan","Matthews, Jason","Moldovan, George Lucian","Moss, Joel","Natoli, Gioacchino","Nielsen, Michael L.","Niepel, Mario","Nolte, Friedrich","Pascal, John","Paschal, Bryce M.","Pawłowski, Krzysztof","Poirier, Guy G.","Smith, Susan","Timinszky, Gyula","Wang, Zhao Qi","Yélamos, José","Yu, Xiaochun","Zaja, Roko","Ziegler, Mathias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460985"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","Canada","China","Finland","France","Germany","Hungary","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["ARase Therapeutics","All Global Affiliations","Centre National de la Recherche Scientifique (CNRS)","ELKH Secreteriat","Friedrich Schiller University Jena","IRCCS Istituto Europeo di Oncologia - Milano","Johns Hopkins University","Laval University","Leibniz Institute on Aging - Fritz Lipmann Institute","Leiden University","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Max Planck Institute for Biology of Ageing","National Institutes of Health","National Research Council of Italy (CNR)","New York University","Oregon Health and Science University","Pennsylvania State University","Pompeu Fabra University","RWTH Aachen University","Ribon Therapeutics, Inc.","The Institute of Cancer Research, London","Universidade de São Paulo","University of Bergen","University of California San Francisco","University of California at San Diego","University of Cologne","University of Debrecen","University of Hamburg","University of Kansas","Un