{"abstract":"Implementing precision medicine hinges on the integration of omics data, such as proteomics, into the clinical decision-making process, but the quantity and diversity of biomedical data, and the spread of clinically relevant knowledge across multiple biomedical databases and publications, pose a challenge to data integration. Here we present the Clinical Knowledge Graph (CKG), an open-source platform currently comprising close to 20 million nodes and 220 million relationships that represent relevant experimental data, public databases and literature. The graph structure provides a flexible data model that is easily extendable to new nodes and relationships as new databases become available. The CKG incorporates statistical and machine learning algorithms that accelerate the analysis and interpretation of typical proteomics workflows. Using a set of proof-of-concept biomarker studies, we show how the CKG might augment and enrich proteomics data and help inform clinical decision-making.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Santos, Alberto","Colaço, Ana R.","Nielsen, Annelaura Bach","Niu, Lili","Strauss, Maximilian T.","Geyer, Philipp E.","Coscia, Fabian","Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","Mundt, Filip","Jensen, Lars Juhl","Mann, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-479764"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","OmicEra Diagnostics GmbH (Biz)","University of Oxford"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a knowledge graph to interpret clinical proteomics data","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41587-021-01145-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-479764","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9110295","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000750630900002","type":"wos"},{"id":"85123916062","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35102292","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-907d8f2e-112e-4f6b-a278-3f4116a66b06"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D64C27622D5A74339B357D478B00EDA6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/309280940/A_knowledge_graph_to_interpret_clinical.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41587-021-01145-6","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Center for Health Data Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Mann Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"omicera diagnostics gmbh","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"OmicEra Diagnostics GmbH (Biz)","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Alberto","key":"santospau","last":"Santos","locid":"75866a6a-0c79-4882-b550-a6c550000e21","name":"Santos, Alberto","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ana R.","key":"colaçopau","last":"Colaço","locid":"aeb6cbaa-5d0f-4899-94af-c27505c10a63","name":"Colaço, Ana R.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annelaura B.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2a42eff8-3176-4b59-8e7c-3857eb418d8b","name":"Nielsen, Annelaura Bach","name_org":"Nielsen, Annelaura B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lili","key":"niupau","last":"Niu","locid":"f74df5eb-9404-4bdb-9d58-289bf2c90efa","name":"Niu, Lili","orcid":"0000-0003-4571-4368","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Maximilian","key":"strausspau","last":"Strauss","locid":"c396d94e-014c-4f75-9272-f7795bbc8b4f","name":"Strauss, Maximilian T.","name_org":"Strauss, Maximilian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1 4","first":"Philipp E.","key":"geyerpau","last":"Geyer","locid":"fc987200-bf00-477b-8c57-e83a7984b89e","name":"Geyer, Philipp E.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Fabian","key":"cosciapau","last":"Coscia","locid":"a95a0078-640b-4ef4-9f07-15ee9bb03fe7","name":"Coscia, Fabian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Nicolai J.Wewer","key":"albrechtsenpau","last":"Albrechtsen","locid":"0d59b767-fdca-42a0-b879-70fb0ec55651","name":"Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","name_org":"Albrechtsen, Nicolai J.Wewer","orcid":"0000-0003-4230-5753","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Filip","key":"mundtpau","last":"Mundt","locid":"4e0c0ac4-807c-40a7-971e-6718396ef306","name":"Mundt, Filip","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Juhl","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"cae227d4-1222-4c3a-a7b0-34ad91d42e5a","name":"Jensen, Lars Juhl","orcid":"0000-0001-7885-715X","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35102292"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41587-021-01145-6","issn":["10870156","15461696"],"issn_org":["10870156"],"journal":"Nature Biotechnology","pages":"692-702","status":"p","title":"Nature Biotechnology","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123916062"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-907d8f2e-112e-4f6b-a278-3f4116a66b06"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A knowledge graph to interpret clinical proteomics data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-479764","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Super resolution (SR) imaging is currently conducted using fragile ultrasound contrast agents. This precludes using the full acoustic pressure range, and the distribution of bubbles has to be sparse for them to be isolated for SR imaging. Images have to be acquired over minutes to accumulate enough positions for visualizing the vas- culature. A new method for SUper Resolution imaging using the Erythrocytes (SURE) as targets is introduced, which makes it possible to maximize the emitted pressure for good signal-to-noise ratios. The abundant number of erythrocyte targets make acquisition fast, and the SURE images can be acquired in seconds. A Verasonics Vantage 256 scanner was used in combination with a GE L8-18iD linear array probe operated at 10 MHz for a wavelength of 150 m. A 12 emissions synthetic aperture ultrasound sequence was employed to scan the kidney of a Sprague-Dawley rat for 24 seconds to visualize its vasculature. An ex vivo micro-CT image using the contrast agent Microfil was also acquired at a voxel size of 22.6 m for validating the SURE images. The SURE image revealed vessels with a size down to 29 fim, five times smaller than the ultrasound wavelength, and the dense grid of vessels in the full kidney was reliably shown for scan times between 1 to 24 seconds. Visually the SURE images revealed the same vasculature as the micro-CT images. SURE images are acquired in seconds rather than minutes without contrast injection for easy clinical use, and they can be measured at full regulatory levels for pressure, intensity, and probe temperature.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Jensen, Jorgen Arendt","Schou, Mikkel","Andersen, Sofie Bech","Søgaard, Stinne Byrholdt","Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Gundlach, Carsten","Kjer, Hans Martin","Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-480366"],"event":{"end":"2022-03-27","place":"Virtual, Online","start":"2022-03-21","title":"Medical Imaging 2022: Ultrasonic Imaging and Tomography","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast super resolution ultrasound imaging using the erythrocytes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.2612245","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-480366","identifier":[{"id":"85132027562","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-917530be-4179-45bb-ab3a-171a5e5baf5d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-1C7BEA0F3B74AEBBDFA64C189CB7FBD2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.2612245","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332929594/Fast_Super_Resolution_Ultrasound_Imaging_using_the.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of C