{"abstract":"Background: Epidemiological studies provide strong evidence for a role of endogenous sex hormones in the aetiology of breast cancer. The aim of this analysis was to identify genetic variants that are associated with urinary sex-hormone levels and breast cancer risk. Methods: We carried out a genome-wide association study of urinary oestrone-3-glucuronide and pregnanediol-3-glucuronide levels in 560 premenopausal women, with additional analysis of progesterone levels in 298 premenopausal women. To test for the association with breast cancer risk, we carried out follow-up genotyping in 90,916 cases and 89,893 controls from the Breast Cancer Association Consortium. All women were of European ancestry. Results: For pregnanediol-3-glucuronide, there were no genome-wide significant associations; for oestrone-3-glucuronide, we identified a single peak mapping to the CYP3A locus, annotated by rs45446698. The minor rs45446698-C allele was associated with lower oestrone-3-glucuronide (−49.2%, 95% CI −56.1% to −41.1%, P = 3.1 × 10–18); in follow-up analyses, rs45446698-C was also associated with lower progesterone (−26.7%, 95% CI −39.4% to −11.6%, P = 0.001) and reduced risk of oestrogen and progesterone receptor-positive breast cancer (OR = 0.86, 95% CI 0.82–0.91, P = 6.9 × 10–8). Conclusions: The CYP3A7*1C allele is associated with reduced risk of hormone receptor-positive breast cancer possibly mediated via an effect on the metabolism of endogenous sex hormones in premenopausal women.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Johnson, Nichola","Maguire, Sarah","Morra, Anna","Kapoor, Pooja Middha","Tomczyk, Katarzyna","Jones, Michael E.","Schoemaker, Minouk J.","Gilham, Clare","Bolla, Manjeet K.","Wang, Qin","Dennis, Joe","Ahearn, Thomas U.","Andrulis, Irene L.","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Antonenkova, Natalia N.","Arndt, Volker","Aronson, Kristan J.","Augustinsson, Annelie","Baynes, Caroline","Freeman, Laura E.Beane","Beckmann, Matthias W.","Benitez, Javier","Bermisheva, Marina","Blomqvist, Carl","Boeckx, Bram","Bogdanova, Natalia V.","Bojesen, Stig E","Brauch, Hiltrud","Brenner, Hermann","Burwinkel, Barbara","Campa, Daniele","Canzian, Federico","Castelao, Jose E.","Chanock, Stephen J.","Chenevix-Trench, Georgia","Clarke, Christine L.","Børresen-Dale, Anne Lise","Alnæs, Grethe I.Grenaker","Sahlberg, Kristine K.","Ottestad, Lars","Kåresen, Rolf","Schlichting, Ellen","Holmen, Marit Muri","Sauer, Toril","Haakensen, Vilde","Riis, Margit","Flyger, Henrik","Nielsen, Sune F","Nordestgaard, Børge G","Scott, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-452858"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["ABCTB Investigators","AOCS Group","NBCS Collaborators","kConFab Investigators"],"country":["Australia","Belarus","Belgium","Canada","Finland","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Russia","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Antoni van Leeuwenhoek Hospital","CIBER - Centro de Investigacion Biomedica en Red","Flanders Institute for Biotechnology","Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nürnberg","German Cancer Research Center","Hannover Medical School","Heidelberg University ","Instituto de Salud Carlos III","KU Leuven","London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","Lund University","N.N. Alexandrov Research Institute of Oncology and Medical Radiology","National Institutes of Health","Queen's University Belfast","Queen's University Kingston","Queensland Institute of Medical Research","Robert Bosch Krankenhaus Stuttgart","Royal Brisbane and Women's Hospital","Russian Academy of Sciences","The Institute of Cancer Research, London","University of California at Irvine","University of Cambridge","University of Helsinki","University of Oslo","University of Pisa","University of Sydney","University of Toronto","University of Tübingen","Vestre Viken Hospital Trust","Xerencia de Xestion Integrada de Vigo-SERGAS","Örebro University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i cyp000000000003a000000000007 000000000001c i allele linking premenopausal oestrone and progesterone levels with risk of hormone receptor positive breast cancers","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41416-020-01185-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-452858","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7884683","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85099996359","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33495599","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-635020ce-494e-4413-98ae-799efb553e08"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C2DB2258CE3C66053233447A2DB1C644"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/276333070/CYP3A71C_allele_linking_premenopausal_oestrone_and_progesterone_levels_with_risk_of_hormone_receptor_positive_breast_cancers","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41416-020-01185-w","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"the institute of cancer research london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Institute of Cancer Research, London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"queen s university belfast","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen's University Belfast","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"antoni van leeuwenhoek hospital","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Antoni van Leeuwenhoek Hospital","used":1},{"affno