responding":null,"first":"Danielle","key":"vienneaupau","last":"Vienneau","name":"Vienneau, Danielle","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"29","corresponding":null,"first":"Gudrun","key":"weinmayrpau","last":"Weinmayr","name":"Weinmayr, Gudrun","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerard","key":"hoekpau","last":"Hoek","name":"Hoek, Gerard","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zorana J.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8bffc514-d71e-40ba-b979-910dfb03ec5e","name":"Andersen, Zorana Jovanovic","name_org":"Andersen, Zorana J.","orcid":"0000-0003-4138-9828","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33276316"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envint.2020.106267","issn":["01604120","18736750"],"issn_org":["01604120"],"journal":"Environment International","paperid":"106267","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Environment International","volume":"146"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097128896"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-606c20fb-6f1d-4399-a0a8-23a6a056131c","ku-0b9ada21-f9a8-4570-813f-29c6cc605260"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long-term exposure to low-level air pollution and incidence of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease : The ELAPSE project","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-019666","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Non-invasive estimation of the cardiac iron concentration (CIC) by T2* cardiovascular magnetic resonance (CMR) has been validated repeatedly and is in widespread clinical use. However, calibration data are limited, and mostly from post-mortem studies. In the present study, we performed an in vivo calibration in a dextran-iron loaded minipig model. METHODS: R2* (= 1/T2*) was assessed in vivo by 1.5 T CMR in the cardiac septum. Chemical CIC was assessed by inductively coupled plasma-optical emission spectroscopy in endomyocardial catheter biopsies (EMBs) from cardiac septum taken during follow up of 11 minipigs on dextran-iron loading, and also in full-wall biopsies from cardiac septum, taken post-mortem in another 16 minipigs, after completed iron loading. RESULTS: A strong correlation could be demonstrated between chemical CIC in 55 EMBs and parallel cardiac T2* (Spearman rank correlation coefficient 0.72, P < 0.001). Regression analysis led to [CIC] = (R2* - 17.16)/41.12 for the calibration equation with CIC in mg/g dry weight and R2* in Hz. An even stronger correlation was found, when chemical CIC was measured by full-wall biopsies from cardiac septum, taken immediately after euthanasia, in connection with the last CMR session after finished iron loading (Spearman rank correlation coefficient 0.95 (P < 0.001). Regression analysis led to the calibration equation [CIC] = (R2* - 17.2)/31.8. CONCLUSIONS: Calibration of cardiac T2* by EMBs is possible in the minipig model but is less accurate than by full-wall biopsies. Likely explanations are sampling error, variable content of non-iron containing tissue and smaller biopsies, when using catheter biopsies. The results further validate the CMR T2* technique for estimation of cardiac iron in conditions with iron overload and add to the limited calibration data published earlier.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jensen, Peter-Diedrich Matthias","Nielsen, Asbjørn Haaning","Simonsen, Carsten Wiberg","Baandrup, Ulrik","Jensen, Svend Eggert","Bøgsted, Martin","Magnusdottir, Sigriður Olga","Jensen, Anne Birthe Helweg","Kjærgaard, Benedict"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-088668"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Peter-Diedrich Matthias"],"keyword":["Minipig model"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in vivo calibration of the t000000000002 cardiovascular magnetic resonance method at 000000000001 000000000005 t for estimation of cardiac iron in a minipig model of transfusional iron overload","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12968-021-00715-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-088668","identifier":[{"id":"85102240387","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33691716","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-84b58366-fd1c-4994-afd4-8fa3f2a47c75"],"keyword":["Cardiac iron","Cardiosiderosis","Dextran-iron loading","Minipig model","T2* calibration","T2* cardiovascular magnetic resonance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F304B936B9FBDD0683BAE68E2723B471"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/458820465/Jensen_et_al_2021_In_vivo_calibration_of_the_T2_cardiovascular_magnetic_resonance_method_at_1.5_T_for_estimation_of_cardiac_iron_in_a_minipig_model_of_transfusional_iron_overload.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12968-021-00715-6","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Haematology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Kirurgi og Kræftbehandling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter-Diedrich Matthias","key":"jensenpeterdiedrichmatthiaspau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ff32942b-108d-4d07-be3e-fd0d93742de8","name":"Jensen, Peter-Diedrich Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-3134-3973","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asbjørn Haaning","key":"nielsenasbjørnhaaningpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a8195f06-236e-45dc-a27c-e2125fceb03e","name":"Nielsen, Asbjørn Haaning","orcid":"0000-0003-4464-8549","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Wiberg","key":"simonsencarstenwibergpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"b2945eb5-0825-4469-a4c6-19db32d9b140","name":"Simonsen, Carsten Wiberg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik Thorngren","key":"baandrupulrikpau","last":"Baandrup","locid":"4d48105c-3cfc-4aa6-92c7-b96c77f03587","name":"Baandrup, Ulrik","name_org":"Baandrup, Ulrik Thorngren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Svend Eggert","key":"jensensvendeggertpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"41577b23-e500-42e1-b7cc-c6600c672fbd","name":"Jensen, Svend Eggert","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"bøgstedmartinpau","last":"Bøgsted","locid":"a51116b7-e9b7-4f83-a74b-2d76bb8b1475","name":"Bøgsted, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-9192-1814","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sigriður Olga","key":"magnusdottirsigriðurolgapau","last":"Magnusdottir","locid":"be8eebbf-329a-465c-9d1b-6a398c4f4334","name":"Magnusdottir, Sigriður Olga","orcid":"0000-0001-5948-9013","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Birthe Helweg","key":"jensenannebirthehelwegpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e684f7f3-8392-4500-bbb0-76f623781c3b","name":"Jensen, Anne Birthe Helweg","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Benedict","key":"kjærgaardbenedictpau","last":"Kjærgaard","locid":"3afc0400-089d-4805-be84-ecdf45e6e318","name":"Kjærgaard, Benedict","orcid":"0000-0001-5797-7638","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33691716"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12968-021-00715-6","issn":["10976647","1532429X"],"issn_org":["10976647"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Cardiovascular Magnetic Resonance","paperid":"27","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cardiovascular Magnetic Resonance","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102240387"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-84b58366-fd1c-4994-afd4-8fa3f2a47c75"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"In vivo calibration of the T2* cardiovascular magnetic resonance method at 1.5 T for estimation of cardiac iron in a minipig model of transfusional iron overload","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-088668","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The etiology of frontotemporal dementia (FTD) is poorly understood. To identify genes with predicted expression levels associated with FTD, we integrated summary statistics with external reference gene expression data using a transcriptome-wide association study approach. Methods: FUSION software was used to leverage FTD summary statistics (all FTD: n = 2154 cases, n = 4308 controls; behavioral variant FTD: n = 1337 cases, n = 2754 controls; semantic dementia: n = 308 cases, n = 616 controls; progressive nonfluent aphasia: n = 269 cases, n = 538 controls; FTD with motor neuron disease: n = 200 cases, n = 400 controls) from the International FTD-Genomics Consortium with 53 expression quantitative loci tissue type panels (n = 12,205; 5 consortia). Significance was assessed using a 5% false discovery rate threshold. Results: We identified 73 significant gene–tissue associations for FTD, representing 44 unique genes in 34 tissue types. Most significant findings were derived from dorsolateral prefrontal cortex splicing data (n = 19 genes, 26%). The 17q21.31 inversion locus contained 23 significant associations, representing 6 unique genes. Other top hits included SEC22B (a gene involved in vesicle trafficking), TRGV5, and ZNF302. A single gene finding (RAB38) was observed for behavioral variant FTD. For other clinical subtypes, no significant associations were observed. Conclusions: We identified novel candidate genes (e.g., SEC22B) and previously reported risk regions (e.g., 17q21.31) for FTD. Most significant associations were observed in dorsolateral prefrontal cortex splicing data despite the modest sample size of this reference panel. This suggests that our findings are specific to FTD and are likely to be biologically relevant highlights of genes at different FTD risk loci that are contributing to the disease pathology.","author_count":159,"contributors":["Reus, Lianne M.","Pasaniuc, Bogdan","Posthuma, Danielle","Boltz, Toni","Ferrari, Raffaele","Hernandez, Dena G.","Nalls, Michael A.","Rohrer, Jonathan D.","Ramasamy, Adaikalavan","Kwok, John B.J.","Dobson-Stone, Carol","Brooks, William S.","Schofield, Peter R.","Halliday, Glenda M.","Hodges, John R.","Piguet, Olivier","Bartley, Lauren","Thompson, Elizabeth","Hernández, Isabel","Ruiz, Agustín","Boada, Mercè","Borroni, Barbara","Padovani, Alessandro","Cruchaga, Carlos","Cairns, Nigel J.","Benussi, Luisa","Binetti, Giuliano","Ghidoni, Roberta","Forloni, Gianluigi","Galimberti, Daniela","Fenoglio, Chiara","Serpente, Maria","Scarpini, Elio","Clarimón, Jordi","Lleó, Alberto","Blesa, Rafael","Waldö, Maria Landqvist","Nilsson, Karin","Nilsson, Christer","Mackenzie, Ian R.A.","Hsiung, Ging Yuek R.","Mann, David M.A.","Grafman, Jordan","Morris, Christopher M.","Attems, Johannes","Griffiths, Timothy D.","McKeith, Ian G.","Thomas, Alan J.","Pietrini, Pietro","Huey, Edward D.","Wassermann, Eric M.","Baborie, Atik","Jaros, Evelyn","Tierney, Michael C.","Pastor, Pau","Razquin, Cristina","Ortega-Cubero, Sara","Alonso, Elena","Perneczky, Robert","Diehl-Schmid, Janine","Alexopoulos, Panagiotis","Kurz, Alexander","Rainero, Innocenzo","Rubino, Elisa","Pinessi, Lorenzo","Rogaeva, Ekaterina","St. George-Hyslop, Peter","Rossi, Giacomina","Tagliavini, Fabrizio","Giaccone, Giorgio","Rowe, James B.","Schlachetzki, Johannes C.M.","Uphill, James","Collinge, John","Mead, Simon","Danek, Adrian","Van Deerlin, Vivianna M.","Grossman, Murray","Trojanowski, John Q.","van der Zee, Julie","Van Broeckhoven, Christine","Cappa, Stefano F.","Le Ber, Isabelle","Hannequin, Didier","Golfier, Véronique","Vercelletto, Martine","Brice, Alexis","Nacmias, Benedetta","Sorbi, Sandro","Bagnoli, Silvia","Piaceri, Irene","Nielsen, Jørgen Erik","Hjermind, Lena E.","Riemenschneider, Matthias","Mayhaus, Manuel","Ibach, Bernd","Gasparoni, Gilles","Pichler, Sabrina","Gu, Wei","Rossor, Martin N.","Fox, Nick C.","Warren, Jason D.","Spillantini, Maria Grazia","Morris, Huw R.","Rizzu, Patrizia","Heutink, Peter","Snowden, Julie S.","Rollinson, Sara","Richardson, Anna","Gerhard, Alexander","Bruni, Amalia C.","Maletta, Raffaele","Frangipane, Francesca","Cupidi, Chiara","Bernardi, Livia","Anfossi, Maria","Gallo, Maura","Conidi, Maria Elena","Smirne, Nicoletta","Rademakers, Rosa","Baker, Matt","Dickson, Dennis W.","Graff-Radford, Neill R.","Petersen, Ronald C.","Knopman, David","Josephs, Keith A.","Boeve, Bradley F.","Parisi, Joseph E.","Seeley, William W.","Miller, Bruce L.","Karydas, Anna M.","Rosen, Howard","van Swieten, John C.","Dopper, Elise G.P.","Seelaar, Harro","Pijnenburg, Yolande A.L.","Scheltens, Philip","Logroscino, Giancarlo","Capozzo, Rosa","Novelli, Valeria","Puca, Annibale A.","Franceschi, Massimo","Postiglione, Alfredo","Milan, Graziella","Sorrentino, Paolo","Kristiansen, Mark","Chiang, Huei Hsin","Graff, Caroline","Pasquier, Florence","Rollin, Adeline","Deramecourt, Vincent","Lebert, Florence","Kapogiannis, Dimitrios","Ferrucci, Luigi","Pickering-Brown, Stuart","Singleton, Andrew B.","Hardy, John","Momeni, Parastoo","Ophoff, Roel A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-477814"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dorsolateral prefrontal cortex","Expression quantitative trait loci eQTL","Frontotemporal dementia","Transcriptome wide association study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gene expression imputation across multiple tissue types provides insight into the genetic architecture of frontotemporal dementia and its clinical subtypes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2020.12.023","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-477814","identifier":[{"id":"85101343818","ty