aperid":"3782","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088804005"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c1c030a3-f3ed-404a-940c-f757ded38e4e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On-chip deterministic operation of quantum dots in dual-mode waveguides for a plug-and-play single-photon source","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-509090","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Tracking plays an important role in super-resolution (SR) ultrasound imaging, as it improves the quality and sharpness of the final SR images. Moreover, tracking enables quantification of clinically important parameters, such as blood flow velocity. However, the tracking performance degrades in the presence of complex particle patterns and localization uncertainty due to noise and motion. This work presents and discusses multiple approaches for tracking evaluation and compares a nearestneighbor (NN) with a Kalman tracker through simulations and an in vivo experiment. It is shown that in the presence of a localization uncertainty with a standard deviation (SD) of λ/5, the bias and SD of the velocity estimates reach -1.04 ± 0.9 mm/s and -0.12 ± 0.72 mm/s in the NN and Kalman tracker, respectively (relative to the peak velocity of 10 mm/s). The precision of individual track positions is estimated for an in vivo experiment as 37.95 ± 21.37 µm and 23.9 ± 11.82 µm for the NN and Kalman trackers, respectively. The results indicate that the Kalman tracker achieves a better velocity estimation and reduces localization uncertainty.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Taghavi, Iman","Andersen, Sofie Bech","Hoyos, Carlos A. Villagomez","Schou, Mikkel","Øygard, Sigrid Husebø","Gran, Fredrik","Hansen, Kristoffer L.","Sørensen, Charlotte M.","Bachmann Nielsen, Michael","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S02-088.86-032816"],"event":{"acronym":"IUS","end":"2020-09-11","place":"Las Vegas, us","start":"2020-09-06","title":"2020 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium, IUS 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Analogic Corporation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tracking performance in ultrasound super resolution imaging","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/220607896/taghavi_et_al_2020.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-088.86-032816","identifier":[{"id":"85097910746","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-09ff4c1a-0f39-4ac2-95b6-7c4a592f818a","ku-f514622a-d4c3-4373-b4cf-ef663fc2e8d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4B2D33DFC5A950C07C21281E6D352529"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/290726485/taghavi_et_al_2020_2_5.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/220607896/taghavi_et_al_2020.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Biomedical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Biomedical Engineering, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Cop