l Health Perspectives","paperid":"057004","publisher":"Public Health Services, US Dept of Health and Human Services","status":"p","title":"Environmental Health Perspectives","volume":"128"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085158410"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ce131436-ac10-4ad1-b62b-c5ca35cea948","au-692cc6a8-3285-4e54-bce8-e848efff9f64","ku-3c7ca3fe-96f1-4536-b610-715be0121b9e","ruc-e681505c-cf45-4e70-bd72-ba9c3338615a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Road Traffic Noise Exposure and Filled Prescriptions for Antihypertensive Medication : A Danish Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-097.57-009888","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Operational parameters as feedstock layer thickness and gap size between die and roller were studied using a 15 kW ring die pellet press. The feedstock layer was tested at three different feedstock mass flow rates, 90 kg/h, 120 kg/h, and 150 kg/h, and three peripheral die speeds, 3.06 m/s, 4.08 m/s, and 5.10 m/s. Tests were also performed with three different roller gaps of 0.2 mm, 0.9 mm, and 1.6 mm. The specific energy consumption of the pellet press was measured during the tests, and the durability of the pellet was measured using a pellet tumbler. By using image processing on photos of pellet samples, the length distributions of the pellets were analysis. The results shows that increasing the thickness of the feedstock layer, decreases the specific energy consumption and increases the pellet durability. Increasing the size of the roller gap, increases the specific energy consumption and decreases the pellet durability. Analysis of the pellet length distributions, shows that the longest pellets were produced with a roller gap of 0.2 mm and the thickest feedstock layer, which also were the most durable pellets. In addition to the experimental tests, two empirical expressions for the specific energy consumption and pellet durability as a function of the feedstock layer are presented.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Simon Klinge","Mandø, Matthias","Rosenørn, Andreas Brinch"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-058033"],"event":{"end":"2021-06-25","place":"Wels, at","start":"2021-06-21","title":"World Sustainable Energy Days","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Andritz AG"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental investigation of feedstock layer thickness and die roller gap in wood pelleting","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-058033","ids":["aau-1b462da9-16dd-46a4-8cac-a14a8643e874"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DCD69A0449598B4CBB59B26E497E885C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Esbjerg Energy Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"andritz ag","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Andritz AG","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon Klinge","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d91cdb12-87dc-438a-8e14-f1ef8b16ab53","name":"Nielsen, Simon Klinge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"mandøpau","last":"Mandø","locid":"78efaa5a-edc5-4ba2-bf4a-36a9bcfd7c33","name":"Mandø, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0002-5692-278X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Brinch","key":"rosenørnpau","last":"Rosenørn","name":"Rosenørn, Andreas Brinch","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"1-10","series":"Proceedings of European Pellet Conference","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of European Pellet Conference 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1b462da9-16dd-46a4-8cac-a14a8643e874"],"src":["AAU Aalborg Univers