"Jensen, Steen Solvang","orcid":"0000-0001-5923-8441","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"masslingpau","last":"Massling","locid":"5bb9394c-7de2-4cb2-a79d-a5e2af778523","name":"Massling, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-8046-2798","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo Denier","key":"vandergonpau","last":"van der Gon","name":"van der Gon, Hugo Denier","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid","key":"mandersgrootpau","last":"Manders-Groot","name":"Manders-Groot, Astrid","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8199dae1-13a6-4f5c-9800-c10b0296a33e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"LONG TERM EXPOSURE ESTIMATES OF PARTICLE NUMBER CONCENTRATIONS IN DENMARK","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-203415","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Particulate matter (PM) air pollution is a complex mixture and the various PM constituents likely affect health differently. The literature on the relationships among specific PM constituents and the risk of cancer is sparse. In this study, we aimed to evaluate the association of PM 2.5 and its constituents with the incidence of non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL) and the two main NHL subtypes. Methods: We undertook a nationwide register-based case-control study including 20,847 cases registered in the Danish Cancer Registry with NHL between 1989 and 2014. Among the entire Danish population, we selected 41,749 age and sex-matched controls randomly from the Civil Registration System. We assessed modelled outdoor PM concentrations at addresses of cases and controls with a state-of-the-art multi scale air pollution modelling system and used conditional logistic regression to estimate odds ratios (ORs) adjusted for individual and neighborhood level socio-demographic variables. Results: The 10-year time-weighted average concentrations of PM 2.5, primary carbonaceous particles (BC/OC), secondary inorganic aerosols (SIA), secondary organic aerosols (SOA) and sea salt were 17.4, 2.3, 7.8, 0.3, and 4.1 μg/m 3, respectively among controls. The results showed higher risk for NHL in association with exposure to BC/OC (OR = 1.03; 95% CI: 1.00, 1.07, per interquartile range (IQR)) and SOA (OR = 1.54; 95% CI: 1.13, 2.09, per IQR). The results indicated a higher risk for follicular lymphoma in association with several PM components. Including PM 2.5 (OR = 1.16; 95% CI: 0.98–1.38), BC/OC (OR = 1.05; 95% CI: 0.97–1.14), SIA (OR = 1.44; 95% CI: 0.80–1.08), SOA (OR = 4.52; 95% CI: 0.86–23.83) per IQR. Conclusion: This is the first study on PM constituents and the risk of NHL. The results indicated an association with primary carbonaceous and secondary organic PM. The results need replication in other settings before any firm conclusion can be reached.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Taj, Tahir","Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Ketzel, Matthias","Geels, Camilla","Brandt, Jørgen","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Puett, Robin","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Sørensen, Mette","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-099.67-793316"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University System of Maryland","University of Maryland","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Case control study","Particulate matter","non Hodgkin lymphoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to pm sub 000000000002 000000000005 sub and its constituents and risk of non hodgkin lymphoma in denmark a population based case control study","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85086369006","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.67-793316","identifier":[{"id":"32535359","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85086369006","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7817d207-5d0d-43c0-b267-3db685121dea","ruc-75e1e379-1e4d-4b72-ac2a-ee279a831d05"],"keyword":["Case–control study","Non-hodgkin lymphoma","Particulate matter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BCD7F208A96220FA24FA6F33C07D181D"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university system of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University System of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tahir","key":"tajpau","last":"Taj","name":"Taj, Tahir","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"puettpau","last":"Puett","name":"Puett, Robin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla Arthur","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32535359"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envres.2020.109762","issn":["00139351","10960953"],"issn_org":["00139351"],"journal":"Environmental Research","paperid":"109762","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Environmental Research","volume":"188"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086369006"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7817d207-5d0d-43c0-b267-3db685121dea","ruc-75e1e379-1e4d-4b72-ac2a-ee279a831d05"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Long-term exposure to PM<sub>2.5</sub> and its constituents and risk of Non-Hodgkin lymphoma in Denmark : A population-based case–control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.67-793316","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Patients with blood transfusion-dependent anemias develop transfusional iron overload (TIO), which may cause cardiosiderosis. In patients with an ineffective erythropoiesis, such as thalassemia major, common transfusion regimes aim at suppression of erythropoiesis and of enteral iron loading. Recent data suggest that maintaining residual, ineffective erythropoiesis may protect from cardiosiderosis. We investigated the common consequences of TIO, including cardiosiderosis, in a minipig model of iron overload with normal erythropoiesis. TIO was mimicked by long-term, weekly iron-dextran injections. Iron-dextran loading for around one year induced very high liver iron concentrations, but extrahepatic iron loading, and iron-induced toxicities were mild and did not include fibrosis. Iron deposits were primarily in reticuloendothelial cells, and parenchymal cardiac iron loading was mild. Compared to non-thalassemic patients with TIO, comparable cardiosiderosis in minipigs required about 4-fold greater body iron loads. It is suggested that this resistance against extrahepatic iron loading and toxicity in minipigs may at least in part be explained by a protective effect of the normal erythropoiesis, and additionally by a larger total iron storage capacity of RES than in patients with TIO. Parenteral iron-dextran loading of minipigs is a promising and feasible large-animal model of iron overload, that may mimic TIO in non-thalassemic patients.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Jensen, Peter-Diedrich Matthias","Nielsen, Asbjørn Haaning","Simonsen, Carsten Wiberg","Baandrup, Ulrik","Vyberg, Mogens","Jensen, Svend Eggert","Magnusdottir, Sigriður Olga","Krarup, Henrik","Nielsen, Michael Festersen","Kjærgaard, Benedict"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-008965"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Peter Diedrich","Jensen, Peter-Diedrich Matthias"],"keyword":["Adult patients","Chelation therapy","Iron overload","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","NONINVASIVE ASSESSMENT"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"consequences of parenteral iron dextran loading investigated in minipigs a new model of transfusional iron overload","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85083775266&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by grants from the Det Obelske Familiefond (grant no. 20461 , 2015), Spar Nord Fonden (grant 2013 ), Aase og Ejnar Danielsens Fond (grant no. 10-000912 , 2013) and Karla og Verner Soerensens Almennyttige Forskningsfond (grant no. 701783 , 2014 and grant no. 701783 , 2018)."],"id":"S02-100.00-008965","identifier":[{"id":"32353700","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000539719700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85083775266","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b9dac4aa-8f3a-49bc-963b-187eaa28b0db","au-bab292ba-2477-498c-9296-7389d5a8d179"],"keyword":["ADULT PATIENTS","BETA-THALASSEMIA MAJOR","CHELATION-THERAPY","DEPENDENT PATIENTS","GERBIL MODEL","HEPATIC CIRRHOSIS","Iron dextran","Iron overload","MYOCARDIAL IRON","Magnetic resonance imaging","Mini-pig model","NONINVASIVE ASSESSMENT","PLASMA IRON","T2-ASTERISK-MAGNETIC RESONANCE","Transfusional iron overload"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C9B6E484D94EC9E785681EE4DFDB7D9B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg