44","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Europace","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091325022"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-875711d2-3cf0-474b-b0ed-3dd9011b1443"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Predictors of recurrence of atrial fibrillation within the first 3 months after ablation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-206595","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Inconclusive evidence has suggested a possible link between air pollution and central nervous system (CNS) tumors. We investigated a range of air pollutants in relation to types of CNS tumors. Methods: We identified all (n = 21,057) intracranial tumors in brain, meninges and cranial nerves diagnosed in Denmark between 1989 and 2014 and matched controls on age, sex and year of birth. We established personal 10-year mean residential outdoor exposure to particulate matter < 2.5 μm (PM2.5), nitrous oxides (NOX), primary emitted black carbon (BC) and ozone. We used conditional logistic regression to calculate odds ratios (OR) linearly (per interquartile range (IQR)) and categorically. We accounted for personal income, employment, marital status, use of medication as well as socio-demographic conditions at area level. Results: Malignant tumors of the intracranial CNS was associated with BC (OR: 1.034, 95%CI: 1.005-1.065 per IQR. For NOx the OR per IQR was 1.026 (95%CI: 0.998-1.056). For malignant non-glioma tumors of the brain we found associations with PM2.5 (OR: 1.267, 95%CI: 1.053-1.524 per IQR), BC (OR: 1.049, 95%CI: 0.996-1.106) and NOx (OR: 1.051, 95% CI: 0.996-1.110). Conclusion: Our results suggest that air pollution is associated with malignant intracranial CNS tumors and malignant non-glioma of the brain. However, additional studies are needed.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Sørensen, Mette","Puett, Robin","Ketzel, Matthias","Brandt, Jørgen","Geels, Camilla","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-092.34-013571"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University System of Maryland","University of Maryland","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","CNS tumors","Epidemiology","Register study"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intracranial tumors of the central nervous system and air pollution a nationwide case control study from denmark","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12940-020-00631-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.34-013571","identifier":[{"id":"85087708156","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32641060","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7346389","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-0d6f695b-7434-4c44-b228-a98d7e9ec277","ruc-f1d5c4c6-f994-445a-b5ed-c27005c97470"],"keyword":["Air pollution","CNS-tumors","Epidemiology","Register study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-177C139750A073F366FD31908074E95A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/77481983/s12940_020_00631_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12940-020-00631-9","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university system of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University System of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla Arthur","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"puettpau","last":"Puett","name":"Puett, Robin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper H.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","name_org":"Christensen, Jesper H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32641060"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12940-020-00631-9","issn":["1476069X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Environmental Health","paperid":"81","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Environmental Health","title_org":"Environmental Health: A Global Access Science Source","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087708156"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0d6f695b-7434-4c44-b228-a98d7e9ec277","ruc-f1d5c4c6-f994-445a-b5ed-c27005c97470"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Intracranial tumors of the central nervous system and air pollution - A nationwide case-control study from Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.34-013571","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"There is limited evidence regarding a possible association between exposure to ambient air pollutants and the risk of non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL). Previous epidemiological studies have relied on crude estimations for air pollution exposure and/or small numbers of NHL cases. The objective of our study was to analyze this association based on air pollution modeled at the address level and NHL cases identified from the nationwide Danish Cancer Registry. We identified 20,874 incident NHL cases diagnosed between 1989 and 2014 and randomly selected 41,749 controls matched on age and gender among the entire Danish population. We used conditional logistic regression to estimate odds ratios (ORs) and adjusted for individual and neighborhood level sociodemographic variables. There was no association between exposure to PM 2.5, BC, O 3, SO 2 or NO 2 and overall risk of NHL but several air pollutants were associated with higher risk of follicular lymphoma, but statistically insignificant, for example, PM 2.5 (OR = 1.15 per 5 μg/m 3; 95% CI: 0.98–1.34) and lower risk for diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (OR = 0.92 per 5 μg/m 3; 95% CI: 0.82–1.03). In this population-based study, we did not observe any convincing evidence of a higher overall risk for NHL with higher exposure to ambient air pollutants.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Taj, Tahir","Poulsen, Aslak H.","Ketzel, Matthias","Geels, Camilla","Brandt, Jørgen","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Puett, Robin","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","Sørensen, Mette","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-099.21-018141"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University System of Maryland","University of Maryland","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Case control study","non Hodgkin lymphoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to air pollution and risk of non hodgkin lymphoma in denmark a population based case control study","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85084741569","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.21-018141","identifier":[{"id":"85084741569","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32175588","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-4b37b712-f162-4b40-a68c-7089c7cdabe5","ruc-bc8433c5-a490-4c53-80a1-4ad7551fb113"],"keyword":["air pollution","case–control study","non-Hodgkin lymphoma"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-33456A5FCDE0BEEFB26B20FEC45B3D6D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university system of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University System of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tahir","key":"tajpau","last":"Taj","name":"Taj, Tahir","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak H.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"puettpau","last":"Puett","name":"Puett, Robin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla A.","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32175588"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ijc.32978","issn":["00207136"],"issue":"7","journal":"International Journal of Cancer","pages":"1874-1880","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cancer","volume":"147"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084741569"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4b37b712-f162-4b40-a68c-7089c7cdabe5","ruc-bc8433c5-a490-4c53-80a1-4ad7551fb113"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Long-term exposure to air pollution and risk of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in Denmark : A population‐based case–control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.21-018141","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Here we describe the LifeTime Initiative, which aims to track, understand and target human cells during the onset and progression of complex diseases, and to analyse their response to therapy at single-cell resolution. This mission will be implemented through the development, integration and application of single-cell multi-omics and imaging, artificial intelligence and patient-derived experimental disease models during the progression from health to disease. The analysis of large molecular and clinical datasets will identify molecular mechanisms, create predictive computational models of disease progression, and reveal new drug targets and therapies. The timely detection and interception of disease embedded in an ethical and patient-centred vision will be achieved through interactions across academia, hospitals, patient associations, health data management systems and industry. The application of this strategy to key medical challenges in cancer, neurological and neuropsychiatric disorders, and infectious, chronic inflammatory and cardiovascular diseases at the single-cell level will usher in cell-based interceptive medicine in Europe over the next decade.","author_count":52,"contributors":["Rajewsky, Nikolaus","Almouzni, Geneviève","Gorski, Stanislaw A.","Aerts, Stein","Amit, Ido","Bertero, Michela G.","Bock, Christoph","Bredenoord, Annelien L.","Cavalli, Giacomo","Chiocca, Susanna","Clevers, Hans","De Strooper, Bart","Eggert, Angelika","Ellenberg, Jan","Fernández, Xosé M.","Figlerowicz, Marek","Gasser, Susan M.","Hubner, Norbert","Kjems, Jørgen","Knoblich, Jürgen A.","Krabbe, Grietje","Lichter, Peter","Linnarsson, Sten","Marine, Jean Christophe","Marioni, John C.","Marti-Renom, Marc A.","Netea, Mihai G.","Nickel, Dörthe","Nollmann, Marcelo","Novak, Halina R.","Parkinson, Helen","Piccolo, Stefano","Pinheiro, Inês","Pombo, Ana","Popp, Christian","Reik, Wolf","Roman-Roman, Sergio","Rosenstiel, Philip","Schultze, Joachim L.","Stegle, Oliver","Tanay, Amos","Testa, Giuseppe","Thanos, Dimitris","Theis, Fabian J.","Torres-Padilla, Maria Elena","Valencia, Alfonso","Vallot, Céline","van Oudenaarden, Alexander","Vidal, Marie","Voet, Thierry"],"cuid":["S02-099.53-016565"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["LifeTime Community Working Groups"],"corresponding_author":["Almouzni, Geneviève","Gorski, Stanislaw A.","Rajewsky, Nikolaus"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","France","Germany","Greece","Israel","Italy","Netherlands","Poland","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Academy of Athens","All Global Affiliations","Austrian Academy of Sciences","Austrian Centre for Digital Humanities and Cultural Heritage, Austrian Academy of Sciences, Vienna","Babraham Institute","Barcelona Institute of Science and Technology (BIST)","Barcelona Supercomputing Center","Berlin Institute of Health","Centre for Genomic Regulation","Charité-Universitätsmedizin Berlin","European Molecular Biology Laboratory","European Molecular Biology Laboratory (EMBL)","FIRC Institute of Molecular Oncology","Flanders Institute for Biotechnology","Friedrich Miescher Institute for Biomedical Research","German Cancer Research Center","German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ)","German Center for Neurodegenerative Diseases","German Centre for Cardiovascular Research","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","Human Technopole","Humboldt University of Berlin","ICREA","IRCCS Istituto Europeo di Oncologia - Milano","Institut Curie","Institute of Molecular Biotechnology","KU Leuven","Karolinska Institutet","Kiel University","Ludwig Boltzmann Institute","Ludwig Maximilian University","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Max Delbrück Center for Molecular Medicine in the Helmholtz Associatio