{"abstract":"Networking is integral to quantum communications1 and has significant potential for upscaling quantum computer technologies2. Recently, it was realized that the sensing performances of multiple spatially distributed parameters may also be enhanced through the use of an entangled quantum network3,4,5,6,7,8,9,10. Here, we experimentally demonstrate how sensing of an averaged phase shift among four distributed nodes benefits from an entangled quantum network. Using a four-mode entangled continuous-variable state, we demonstrate deterministic quantum phase sensing with a precision beyond what is attainable with separable probes. The techniques behind this result can have direct applications in a number of areas ranging from molecular tracking to quantum networks of atomic clocks.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Guo, Xueshi","Breum, Casper Rubæk","Borregaard, Johannes","Izumi, Shuro","Larsen, Mikkel V.","Gehring, Tobias","Christandl, Matthias","Neergaard-Nielsen, Jonas Schou","Andersen, Ulrik Lund"],"cuid":["S02-095.74-034686"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Ulrik Lund","Guo, Xueshi","Neergaard-Nielsen, Jonas Schou"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distributed quantum sensing in a continuous variable entangled network","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/257240593/Distributed_quantum_sensing_in_a_continuous_variable_entangled_network.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-095.74-034686","identifier":[{"id":"85077170353","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5c3a6f09-d5a5-437a-b0e1-94dacf9dc79c","ku-c17afbc2-7784-436d-b022-a4912ad20fcf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0BDB5AA2B6924552FC197A25C4CBA2D6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/201064328/1905.09408.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/257240593/Distributed_quantum_sensing_in_a_continuous_variable_entangled_network.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Quantum Physics and Information Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xueshi","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"b1de55b9-19a2-45c4-b5ca-db35be5c9ad9","name":"Guo, Xueshi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper R.","key":"breumpau","last":"Breum","locid":"9ae9a285-1042-4ecf-88ad-477f25cef1ef","name":"Breum, Casper Rubæk","name_org":"Breum, Casper R.","orcid":"0000-0002-9762-5845","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Johannes","key":"b