{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Noise from wind turbines (WTs) is associated with annoyance and, potentially, sleep disturbances. OBJECTIVES: Our objective was to investigate whether long-term WT noise (WTN) exposure is associated with the redemption of prescriptions for sleep medication and antidepressants. METHODS: For all Danish dwellings within a radius of [Formula: see text] heights and for 25% of randomly selected dwellings within a radius of [Formula: see text] heights, we estimated nighttime outdoor and low-frequency (LF) indoor WTN, using information on WT type and simulated hourly wind. During follow-up from 1996 to 2013, 68,696 adults redeemed sleep medication and 82,373 redeemed antidepressants, from eligible populations of 583,968 and 584,891, respectively. We used Poisson regression with adjustment for individual and area-level covariates. RESULTS: Five-year mean outdoor nighttime WTN of [Formula: see text] was associated with a hazard ratio (HR) = 1.14 [95% confidence interval (CI]: 0.98, 1.33) for sleep medication and HR = 1.17 (95% CI: 1.01, 1.35) for antidepressants (compared with exposure to WTN of [Formula: see text]). We found no overall association with indoor nighttime LF WTN. In age-stratified analyses, the association with outdoor nighttime WTN was strongest among persons [Formula: see text] of age, with HRs (95% CIs) for the highest exposure group ([Formula: see text]) of 1.68 (1.27, 2.21) for sleep medication and 1.23 (0.90, 1.69) for antidepressants. For indoor nighttime LF WTN, the HRs (95% CIs) among persons [Formula: see text] of age exposed to [Formula: see text] were 1.37 (0.81, 2.31) for sleep medication and 1.34 (0.80, 2.22) for antidepressants. CONCLUSIONS: We observed high levels of outdoor WTN to be associated with redemption of sleep medication and antidepressants among the elderly, suggesting that WTN may potentially be associated with sleep and mental health. https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP3909.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Peña, Alfredo","Hahmann, Andrea N.","Nordsborg, Rikke Baastrup","Ketzel, Matthias","Brandt, Jørgen","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S03-089.68-017053"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Annoyance","Antidepressive Agents therapeutic use","Danish registers","Denmark epidemiology","Depression","Disturbance","Drug Prescriptions statistics numerical data","Energy Generating Resources","Environmental Exposure adverse effects","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Noise adverse effects","Proportional Hazards Models","Prospective Studies","Quality of Life","Responses","Road traffic noise","Symptoms","health problems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of long term exposure to wind turbine noise on redemption of sleep medication and antidepressants a nationwide cohort study","src":["au","dtu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP3909","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-089.68-017053","identifier":[{"id":"000462983500008","type":"wos"},{"id":"30864815","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6768316","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85062886360","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3c008ecb-e0c9-4b69-a976-54e692fc85e7","dtu-1030ecc3-0372-4213-bfac-265b82933f3d","ruc-5f6e344f-c203-4f3f-824a-22c7be4bdd03"],"keyword":["ANNOYANCE","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Antidepressive Agents/therapeutic use","DANISH REGISTERS","DEPRESSION","DISTURBANCE","Denmark/epidemiology","Drug Prescriptions/statistics & numerical data","Energy-Generating Resources","Environmental Exposure/adverse effects","Female","HEALTH-PROBLEMS","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Noise/adverse effects","Proportional Hazards Models","Prospective Studies","QUALITY-OF-LIFE","RESPONSES","ROAD TRAFFIC NOISE","SYMPTOMS","Sleep Aids, Pharmaceutical/therapeutic use"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-E6CFE8B277227B29292D8AE82F1E9E44"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/175440072/EHP3909.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/67676246/EHP3909.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP3909","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europ