{"abstract":"AirGIS, a Geographic Information Systems (GIS) based air pollution and human exposure modelling system, is routinely used in conjunction with the Operational Street Pollution Model (OSPM®), across the globe, to assess local- or street-scale air pollution. We developed a substantially revised version of AirGIS (hereafter, new AirGIS) as a new modelling system in open-source GIS i.e. PostgreSQL software with its spatial extension PostGIS to (1) optimize the model performance enabling model calculations for a large number of sites over a large geographical area, with limited computing resources (2) replace the outdated programming language Avenue (3) become independent of commercial GIS software. This paper, therefore, aims to describe the overall structure of new AirGIS modelling system together with its strengths and limitations. Furthermore, the new AirGIS has been evaluated against various measured datasets of ambient air pollution (NOx, NO2, PM10 and PM2.5). In terms of reproducing temporal variation (single location, time series of concentrations e.g. annual, daily etc.) of air pollution, the new model achieved correlations (R) in the range 0.45–0.96. While, in terms of reproducing the spatial variation (several locations, single time interval), the new AirGIS achieved correlations in the range 0.32–0.92. The new model, therefore, can be used for both short- and long-term air pollution exposure assessments to facilitate health related studies. However, the present evaluation of the new modelling system also revealed that the new AirGIS significantly overestimated the observed concentrations for two out of four datasets. The possible reasons for these errors and future directions to reducing the bias in the new model output have been discussed.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Khan, Jibran","Kakosimos K.E., Konstantinos E.","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Brandt, Jørgen","Jensen, Steen Solvang","Ellermann, Thomas","Ketzel, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-192215"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ketzel, Matthias"],"keyword":["AirGIS","GIS","Model evaluation","OSPM","Urban air pollution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development and performance evaluation of new airgis a gis based air pollution and human exposure modelling system","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85055636271","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-192215","identifier":[{"id":"85055636271","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6e33ca28-9b3a-4297-9441-f02e831a6c0d"],"keyword":["AirGIS","GIS","Human exposure modelling","Model evaluation","OSPM","PostgreSQL","Urban air pollution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FF057E674708727BAE2FBF95CEE5194D"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Konstantinos E.","key":"kakosimoskepau","last":"Kakosimos K.E.","name":"Kakosimos K.E., Konstantinos E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Solvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"0d52f91a-4eaa-46f9-ab5f-d7fd3c31440d","name":"Jensen, Steen Solvang","orcid":"0000-0001-5923-8441","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"ellermannpau","last":"Ellermann","locid":"5e5a2168-23db-4863-b6d5-bda7dcb1f662","name":"Ellermann, Thomas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.atmosenv.2018.10.036","issn":["13522310","18782442"],"issn_org":["13522310"],"journal":"Atmospheric Environment","pages":"102-121","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Atmospheric Environment","volume":"198"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055636271"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6e33ca28-9b3a-4297-9441-f02e831a6c0d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Development and performance evaluation of new AirGIS – A GIS based air pollution and human exposure modelling system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-192215","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"For various elements of Traffic-Related Air Pollution (TRAP) a relationship has been found with adverse health effects e.g. onset of childhood asthma, non-asthma respiratory symptoms, impaired lung function, total and cardiovascular mortality, and cardiovascular morbidity. Traditional components of TRAP such as NO 2, CO, O 3, PM 10, PM 2.5 and lately also BC/EC are included in exposure models and their effects are investigated in health studies for a long time. This has been done by application of e.g. the Danish THOR/AirGIS exposure modelling systems (http://envs.au.dk/en/knowledge/air/models/). Ultrafine particles (UFP) have attracted significant attention as another heath relevant component of TRAP in various recent studies, especially in studies of short-term effects of air pollution. The Health Effects Institute funded the project “Health Effects of Air Pollution Components, Noise and Socioeconomic Status (HERMES)” with one of the aims to establish particle number /UFP as new pollution component in all three Danish models that are used for exposure assessment: the regional model, Danish Eulerian Hemispheric Model (DEHM); the Urban Background Model (UBM) and the Operational Street Pollution Model (OSPM®). Based on a literature review focusing on ultrafine particle modelling studies conducted in Europe the M7 particle dynamics module was chosen for implementation into DEHM. The M7 module is developed mainly for air pollution modelling purposes and has been used by several groups in Europe and was recently applied in the EU TRANSPHORM project to model particle number concentration in five European cities. In this project the recently developed European particle number emission database by TNO, is used as modelling input for the European domain in an about 7 km x 7 km spatial resolution. A higher 1km x1km spatial resolution UFP database is developed for Denmark. Denmark has a unique dataset of 15 years of continuous UFP measurements (particle size distribution in size range 10-700 nm) carried out at three locations; a street and an urban background station in Copenhagen together with a rural background station about 35 km west of Copenhagen. We calibrate our developed UFP modelling approaches at all three model-scales. First results of this comprehensive model development will be presented.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Ketzel, Matthias","Im, Ulas","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Frohn, Lise Marie","Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","Jensen, Steen Solvang","Massling, Andreas","Hertel, Ole","Brandt, Jørgen","van der Gon, Hugo Denier","Manders-Groot, Astrid","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-223656"],"event":{"end":"2019-06-06","place":"Bruges, be","start":"2019-06-03","title":"19th International Conference on Harmonisation within Atmospheric Dispersion Modelling for Regulatory Purposes","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Netherlands Organization for Applied Scientific Research (TNO)"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling of particle number concentrations for exposure estimates at regional and street levels in denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-223656","identifier":[{"id":"85084161550","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a58108d3-a9b4-43dd-a00a-26ec8e9e36d0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F1DCA1907B483DBD0E17D6225C723951"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"A