e":"300","pages":"52","publisher":"Aarhus University, DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","repno":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi, No. 300","series":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-da92c42f-5c1f-41c0-9d80-0d8c70730eb1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Udvikling i luftkvalitet og helbredseffekter for 2020 og 2030 i relation til Nationalt program for reduktion af luftforurening (NAPCP) : Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE – Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi nr. 300","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-254112","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Noise from wind turbines (WTs) is reported as more annoying than traffic noise at similar levels, raising concerns as to whether WT noise (WTN) increases risk for cardiovascular disease, as observed for traffic noise. Objectives: We aimed to investigate whether long-term exposure to WTN increases risk of myocardial infarction (MI) and stroke. Methods: We identified all Danish dwellings within a radius 20 times the height of the closest WT and 25% of the dwellings within 20–40 times20–40 timesthe height of the closest WT. Using data on WT type and simulated hourly wind at each WT, we estimated hourly outdoor and low frequency (LF) indoor WTN for each dwelling and derived 1-y and 5-y running nighttime averages. We used hospital and mortality registries to identify all incident cases of MI (n=19,145n=19,145) and stroke (n=18,064n=18,064) among all adults age 25–85 y (n=717,453n=717,453), who lived in one of these dwellings for ≥one year≥one year over the period 1982–2013. We used Poisson regression to estimate incidence rate ratios (IRRs) adjusted for individual- and area-level covariates. Results: IRRs for MI in association with 5-y nighttime outdoor WTN >42>42 (vs. <24<24) dB(A) and indoor LF WTN >15>15 (vs. <5<5) dB(A) were 1.21 [95% confidence interval (CI): 0.91, 1.62; 47 exposed cases] and 1.29 (95% CI: 0.73, 2.28; 12 exposed cases), respectively. IRRs for intermediate categories of outdoor WTN [24–30, 30–36, and 36–42 dB(A)36–42 dB(A) vs. <24 dB(A)<24 dB(A)] were slightly above the null and of similar size: 1.08 (95% CI: 1.04, 1.12), 1.07 (95% CI: 1.00, 1.12), and 1.06 (95% CI: 0.93, 1.22), respectively. For stroke, IRRs for the second and third outdoor exposure groups were similar to those for MI, but near or below the null for higher exposures. Conclusions: We did not find convincing evidence of associations between WTN and MI or stroke.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Raasehau-Nielsen, Ole","Peña, Alfredo","Hahmann, Andrea N.","Nordsborg, Rikke Baastrup","Ketzel, Matthias","Brandt, Jorge","Sorensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316631"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Sorensen, Mette"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to wind turbine noise and risk for myocardial infarction and stroke a nationwide cohort study a nationwide cohort study","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP3340","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316631","identifier":[{"id":"85062867482","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6768320","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30864814","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-2890562b-98ca-4600-ae37-deaeb118c72e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-021234EA6F51312EF64F7067784500AC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP3340","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/175440357/EHP3340.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Meteorology & Remote Sensing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"raasehaunielsenpau","last":"Raasehau-Nielsen","name":"Raasehau-Nielsen, Ole","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfredo","key":"peñapau","last":"Peña","locid":"2292abbf-9c66-4504-a423-128432556c8c","name":"Peña, Alfredo","orcid":"0000-0002-7900-9651","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea N.","key":"hahmannpau","last":"Hahmann","locid":"c8315d00-83a0-43f3-85c8-cf51258cdc00","name":"Hahmann, Andrea N.","orcid":"0000-0001-8785-3492","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Baastrup","key":"nordsborgpau","last":"Nordsborg","name":"Nordsborg, Rikke Baastrup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jorge","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Jorge","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","name":"Sorensen, Mette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30864814"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1289/ehp3340","issn":["00916765","15529924"],"issn_org":["00916765"],"issue":"3","journal":"Environmental Health Perspectives","paperid":"037004","publisher":"Public Health Services, US Dept of Health and Human Services","status":"p","title":"Environmental Health Perspectives","volume":"127"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062867482"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2890562b-98ca-4600-ae37-deaeb118c72e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Long-Term Exposure to Wind Turbine Noise and Risk for Myocardial Infarction and Stroke: A Nationwide Cohort Study: A Nationwide Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316631","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Stratification of women according to their risk of breast cancer based on polygenic risk scores (PRSs) could improve screening and prevention strategies. Our aim was to develop PRSs, optimized for prediction of estrogen receptor (ER)-specific disease, from the largest available genome-wide association dataset and to empirically validate the PRSs in prospective studies. The development dataset comprised 94,075 case subjects and 75,017 control subjects of European ancestry from 69 studies, divided into training and validation sets. Samples were genotyped using genome-wide arrays, and single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) were selected by stepwise regression or lasso penalized regression. The best performing PRSs were validated in an independent test set comprising 11,428 case subjects and 18,323 control subjects from 10 prospective studies and 190,040 women from UK Biobank (3,215 incident breast cancers). For the best PRSs (313 SNPs), the odds ratio for overall disease per 1 standard deviation in ten prospective studies was 1.61 (95%CI: 1.57-1.65) with area under receiver-operator curve (AUC) = 0.630 (95%CI: 0.628-0.651). The lifetime risk of overall breast cancer in the top centile of the PRSs was 32.6%. Compared with women in the middle quintile, those in the highest 1% of risk had 4.37- and 2.78-fold risks, and those in the lowest 1% of risk had 0.16- and 0.27-fold risks, of developing ER-positive and ER-negative disease, respectively. Goodness-of-fit tests indicated that this PRS was well calibrated and predicts disease risk accurately in the tails of the distribution. This PRS is a powerful and reliable predictor of breast cancer risk that may improve breast cancer prevention programs.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Mavaddat, Nasim","Michailidou, Kyriaki","Dennis, Joe","Lush, Michael","Fachal, Laura","Lee, Andrew","Tyrer, Jonathan P","Chen, Ting-Huei","Wang, Qin","Bolla, Manjeet K","Yang, Xin","Adank, Muriel A","Ahearn, Thomas","Aittomäki, Kristiina","Allen, Jamie","Andrulis, Irene L","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Antonenkova, Natalia N","Arndt, Volker","Aronson, Kristan J","Auer, Paul L","Auvinen, Päivi","Barrdahl, Myrto","Beane Freeman, Laura E","Beckmann, Matthias W","Behrens, Sabine","Benitez, Javier","Bermisheva, Marina","Bernstein, Leslie","Blomqvist, Carl","Bogdanova, Natalia V","Bojesen, Stig E","Bonanni, Bernardo","Børresen-Dale, Anne-Lise","Brauch, Hiltrud","Bremer, Michael","Brenner, Hermann","Brentnall, Adam","Brock, Ian W","Brooks-Wilson, Angela","Brucker, Sara Y","Brüning, Thomas","Burwinkel, Barbara","Campa, Daniele","Carter, Brian D","Castelao, Jose E","Christiansen, Hans","Flyger, Henrik","Nielsen, Sune F","Nordestgaard, Børge G"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-502583"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["ABCTB Investigators"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"polygenic risk scores for prediction of breast cancer and breast cancer subtypes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajhg.2018.11.002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-502583","identifier":[{"id":"85059498503","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6323553","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30554720","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b6c57490-f744-4ad4-9a6a-3e8c30442cbb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C1C0282C2E875D15E57368D22760D4A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/224702210/1_s2.0_S0002929718304051_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajhg.2018.11.002","version":"Pu