{"abstract":"The increasing pellet production and a demand for making high quality biofuel pellets call for tools that can facilitate producers to meet these requirements and help understanding the effect feedstock and process parameters. In this study, mechanical and rheological properties of pine pellets made of different particle sizes and compression speeds were studied via pelleting tests and numerical simulations. Single pelleting tests were performed with six different particle size samples, ranging between 0.25 and 2.8 mm, and pelleted at compression speeds of 1, 5, and 10 mm min−1. The experimental results of specific compression and extrusion energy showed a positively linear correlation between particle size and energy consumption. The highest pellet durability was observed for pellets produced from small and mixed particle sizes. Eight different constitutive models were evaluated on their ability to simulate compression and stress relaxation, and their level of complexity. A non-linear Maxwell representation of the Standard Linear Solid (SLS) model was setup and fitted to the experimental compression data. The model coefficient of spring 1 composes the asymptotic stress level of the relaxed pellet, and the coefficient of spring 2 was found to be positively correlated with particle size. The viscosity of the dashpot is also found to be positively correlated with particle size, likewise it depends on the compression speed, where higher compression speed resulted in lower viscosities. The results of the study elucidate new insight into mechanical behavior of biomass particle compression, and the resultant simulations have utility for predicting the pressure requirements to produce pellets.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Simon Klinge","Rezaei, Hamid","Mandø, Matthias","Sokhansanj, Shahab"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-072123"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Andritz AG","University of British Columbia"],"keyword":["Biofuel","Biomass","Compression","Constitutive modelling","Energy","Pelleting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"constitutive modelling of compression and stress relaxation in pine pellets","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-072123","identifier":[{"id":"85072606802","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4c1fd404-185c-4cd0-a937-c8d127433ce1"],"keyword":["Biofuel","Biomass","Compression","Constitutive modelling","Energy","Pelleting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E5E7FF46A9E2E30BD7BB9ADBAE62B59C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Esbjerg Energy Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"andritz ag","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Andritz AG","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"university of british columbia","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of British Columbia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon Klinge","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d91cdb12-87dc-438a-8e14-f1ef8b16ab53","name":"Nielsen, Simon Klinge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hamid","key":"rezaeipau","last":"Rezaei","name":"Rezaei, Hamid","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"mandøpau","last":"Mandø","locid":"78efaa5a-edc5-4ba2-bf4a-36a9bcfd7c33","name":"Mandø, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0002-5692-278X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Shahab","key":"sokhansanjpau","last":"Sokhansanj","name":"Sokhansanj, Shahab","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biombioe.2019.105370","issn":["09619534","18732909"],"issn_org":["09619534"],"journal":"Biomass & Bioenergy","paperid":"105370","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biomass & Bioenergy","volume":"130"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072606802"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4c1fd404-185c-4cd0-a937-c8d127433ce1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Constitutive modelling of compression and stress relaxation in pine pellets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-072123","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Inflammatory signaling is restricted through degradation and the translational repression of cytokine mRNAs. A key factor in this regulation is tristetraprolin (TTP), an RNA-binding protein (RBP) that recruits RNA-destabilizing factors and the translation inhibitory complex 4EHP-GIGYF1/2 to AU-rich element (ARE)-containing mRNAs. Here, we show that the RBP ZNF598 contributes to the same regulatory module in a TTP-like manner. Similar to TTP, ZNF598 harbors three proline-rich motifs that bind the GYF domain of GIGYF1. RNA sequencing experiments showed that ZNF598 is required for the regulation of known TTP targets, including IL-8 and CSF2 mRNA. Furthermore, we demonstrate that ZNF598 binds to IL-8 mRNA, but not TNF mRNA. Collectively, our findings highlight that ZNF598 functions as an RBP that buffers the level of a range of mRNAs. We propose that ZNF598 is a TTP-like factor that can contribute to the regulation of the inflammatory potential of cytokine-producing cells.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Tollenaere, Maxim A X","Tiedje, Christopher","Rasmussen, Simon Horskjær","Nielsen, Julie C","Vind, Anna Constance","Blasius, Melanie","Batth, Tanveer S","Mailand, Niels","Olsen, Jesper V.","Gaestel, Matthias","Bekker-Jensen, Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416037"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hannover Medical School"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gigyf000000000001 000000000002 driven cooperation between znf000000000598 and ttp in posttranscriptional regulation of inflammatory signaling","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2019.03.006","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-416037","identifier":[{"id":"85062939661","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30917308","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-25d0b71e-69bd-46f9-8e40-897fea362dcc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6F1B85A0A8734C39EE164B48B076FADC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/229013033/1_s2.0_S2211124719303134_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2019.03.006","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Molecular Aging Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"hannover medical school","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hannover Medical School","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maxim A X","key":"tollenaerepau","last":"Tollenaere","locid":"ba650f40-cf41-4c3e-95e1-55fde12efbe5","name":"Tollenaere, Maxim A X","orcid":"0000-0002-2653-0777","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christopher","key":"tiedjepau","last":"Tiedje","locid":"9cec9c20-f420-413b-8042-fa8f94f70ff1","name":"Tiedje, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-3013-6967","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Simon","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"94a11552-488e-4c24-8ae4-a3af28299a71","name":"Rasmussen, Simon Horskjær","name_org":"Rasmussen, Simon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julie C","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"63e6e2ae-d9b9-4f1b-bc1a-66362d8f257e","name":"Nielsen, Julie C","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna C","key":"vindpau","last":"Vind","locid":"6140d67a-7c73-4ba9-a4c4-ed23fb89371a","name":"Vind, Anna Constance","name_org":"Vind, Anna C","orcid":"0000-0001-5074-2713","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Melanie","key":"blasiuspau","last":"Blasius","locid":"bfa6be59-4bcc-4a14-bda8-eec74686c529","name":"Blasius, Melanie","orcid":"0000-0001-5032-2209","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tanveer S","key":"batthpau","last":"Batth","locid":"431e679c-7605-4af9-978f-560724111462","name":"Batth, Tanveer S","orcid":"0000-0001-5346-4544","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"mailandpau","last":"Mailand","locid":"ce523cf9-bc5a-4ed1-b485-6a9b73b6fa7b","name":"Mailand, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-6623-709X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper V","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"16f5cd56-244f-4fe8-bebd-13ee7bd17822","name":"Olsen, Jesper V.","name_org":"Olsen, Jesper V","orcid":"0000-0002-4747-4938","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Matthias","key":"gaestelpau","last":"Gaestel","name":"Gaestel, Matthias","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Simon","key":"bekkerjensenpau","last":"Bekker-Jensen","locid":"b9115bc4-89d5-4f67-82c2-0ce170b114e2","name":"Bekker-Jensen, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-7308-4597","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30917308"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.celrep.2019.03.006","issn":["22111247"],"issue":"13","journal":"Cell Reports","status":"p","title":"Cell Reports","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062939661"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-25d0b71e-69bd-46f9-8e40-897fea362dcc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"GIGYF1/2-Driven Cooperation between ZNF598 and TTP in Posttranscriptional Regulation of Inflammatory Signaling","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-416037","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
