enmark"],"title":"Micro product and process fingerprints for zero-defect net-shape micromanufacturing","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-317872","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: We previously reported that in pathogenic mismatch repair (path_MMR) variant carriers, the incidence of colorectal cancer (CRC) was not reduced when colonoscopy was undertaken more frequently than once every 3 years, and that CRC stage and interval since last colonoscopy were not correlated. Methods: The Prospective Lynch Syndrome Database (PLSD) that records outcomes of surveillance was examined to determine survival after colon cancer in relation to the time since previous colonoscopy and pathological stage. Only path_MMR variants scored by the InSiGHT variant database as class 4 or 5 (clinically actionable) were included in the analysis. Results: Ninety-nine path_MMR carriers had no cancer prior to or at first colonoscopy, but subsequently developed colon cancer. Among these, 96 were 65 years of age or younger at diagnosis, and included 77 path_MLH1, 17 path_MSH2, and 2 path_MSH6 carriers. The number of cancers detected within < 1.5, 1.5-2.5, 2.5-3.5 and at > 3.5 years after previous colonoscopy were 9, 43, 31 and 13, respectively. Of these, 2, 8, 4 and 3 were stage III, respectively, and only one stage IV (interval 2.5-3.5 years) disease. Ten-year crude survival after colon cancer were 93, 94 and 82% for stage I, II and III disease, respectively (p < 0.001). Ten-year crude survival when the last colonoscopy had been < 1.5, 1.5-2.5, 2.5-3.5 or > 3.5 years before diagnosis, was 89, 90, 90 and 92%, respectively (p = 0.91). Conclusions: In path_MLH1 and path_MSH2 carriers, more advanced colon cancer stage was associated with poorer survival, whereas time since previous colonoscopy was not. Although the numbers are limited, together with our previously reported findings, these results may be in conflict with the view that follow-up of path_MMR variant carriers with colonoscopy intervals of less than 3 years provides significant benefit.","author_count":44,"contributors":["Dominguez-Valentin, Mev","Seppälä, Toni T","Sampson, Julian R","Macrae, Finlay","Winship, Ingrid","Evans, D Gareth","Scott, Rodney J","Burn, John","Möslein, Gabriela","Bernstein, Inge","Pylvänäinen, Kirsi","Renkonen-Sinisalo, Laura","Lepistö, Anna","Lindblom, Annika","Plazzer, John-Paul","Tjandra, Douglas","Thomas, Huw","Green, Kate","Lalloo, Fiona","Crosbie, Emma J","Hill, James","Capella, Gabriel","Pineda, Marta","Navarro, Matilde","Vidal, Joan Brunet","Rønlund, Karina","Nielsen, Randi Thyregaard","Yilmaz, Mette Karen","Elvang, Louise Laurberg","Katz, Lior","Nielsen, Maartje","Ten Broeke, Sanne W","Nakken, Sigve","Hovig, Eivind","Sunde, Lone","Kloor, Matthias","Knebel Doeberitz, Magnus V","Ahadova, Aysel","Lindor, Noralane","Steinke-Lange, Verena","Holinski-Feder, Elke","Mecklin, Jukka-Pekka","Møller, Pål"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-002780"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Dominguez-Valentin, Mev"],"country":["Australia","Finland","Germany","Israel","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CIBERONC - Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red Cáncer","Cardiff University","Central Finland Central Hospital","Central Hospital of Central Finland","Centro Investigación Biomédica en Red de Cáncer (CIBERONC)","German Cancer Research Center","German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ)","Heidelberg University ","Helsinki University Hospital","Hospital Clinic of Barcelona","Hospital Universitari de Bellvitge","Hunter Medical Research Institute","Imperial College London","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Leiden University","London North West University Healthcare NHS Trust","Ludwig Maximilian University","Ludwig-Maximilian University of Munich","MGZ- Medical Genetics Center","Manchester University","Mayo Clinic","Mayo Clinic Scottsdale, AZ","Medizinisch Genetisches Zentrum","Newcastle University","Oslo University Hospital","Royal Melbourne Hospital","Sheba Medical Center","Sheba Medical Center at Tel Hashomer","St. Mary's Hospital","University Hospital Heidelberg","University of Eastern Finland","University of Helsinki","University of Jyväskylä","University of Manchester","University of Melbourne","University of Oslo","Witten/Herdecke University"],"keyword":["Cancer stage","Colon cancer","Colonoscopy","Lynch syndrome","Surveillance","Survival"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"survival by colon cancer stage and screening interval in lynch syndrome a prospective lynch syndrome database report","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13053-019-0127-3","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We would like to express our gratitude to Heikki J?rvinen, Beatriz Alcala-Repo and Marianne Haeusler for their efforts during the years. TTS and J-PM are supported by the Emil Aaltonen Foundation, the Finnish Medical Foundation, the Instrumentarium Science Foundation, Sigrid Juselius Foundation, The Finnish Cancer Foundation, Jane and Aatos Erkko foundation and State Research Funding. DGE and EJC are both supported through the National Institute for Health Research Manchester Biomedical Research Centre (IS-BRC-1215-20007). The Spanish contribution: GC and MP were funded by the Spanish Ministry of Economy and Competitiveness and cofunded by FEDER funds -a way to build Europe- (grant SAF2015-68016-R) and the CIBERONC, the Carlos III Health Institute, the Scientific Foundation Asociaci?n Espa?ola Contra el C?ncer and the Government of Catalonia. The Welsh Contribution: Wales Gene Park. The Norwegian contribution: Norwegian Cancer Society, contract 194751- 2017 for funding. Work relevant for the German contribution was funded in part by Wilhelm Sander Foundation (2016.056.1) and German Research Foundation (Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft, DFG; KFO227, KL2354). The study sponsors did not have a role in planning the study design; in the collection, analysis, or interpretation of data; in the writing of the report; or in the decision to submit the paper for publication."],"id":"S03-100.00-002780","identifier":[{"id":"31636762","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85075119347","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6792227","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-3819d5ca-ad58-47bc-bd2e-64baf923c504","au-3fe05911-060a-42dd-9c74-d25c15b88870","sdu-2533c0f5-4bc7-4183-a5d1-d66f65188b72"],"keyword":["Cancer stage","Colon cancer","Colonoscopy","Lynch syndrome","Surveillance","Survival"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-5EE35C15B9E485157AB22AF67D25C16A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13053-019-0127-3","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/157400415/s13053_019_0127_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/320223352/Dominguez_Valentin_et_al._2019_Survival_by_colon_cancer_stage_and_screening_interval_in_Lynch_syndrome.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"oslo university hospital","loc":["Norway","Eu