{"abstract":"Noise from wind turbines (WTs) has been reported more annoying than traffic noise at similar levels, and concerns have been raised about whether WT noise (WTN) can increase risk for cardiovascular disease. We aimed to investigate if long-term exposure to WTN increases risk for hypertension, estimated as redemption of prescriptions for antihypertensive drugs. We identified all Danish dwellings within a radius of 20 WT heights from a WT and 25% randomly selected dwellings within 20–40 WT heights radius. Using data on WT type and hourly wind conditions at each WT, we estimated hourly outdoor (10–10,000 Hz) and low frequency (LF: 10–160 Hz) indoor WTN for all dwellings, and aggregated it as long-term nighttime running means. From nationwide registries, we identified 535,675 persons age 25–85 years living in these dwellings for >1 year from 1996 to 2013, of whom 83,729 fulfilled our case definition of redeeming ≥2 prescriptions and ≥180 defined daily doses of antihypertensive drugs within a year. Data were analyzed using Poisson regression according to categories of WTN exposure and adjustment for individual and area-level covariates. We found no associations between 5-year mean exposure to WTN during night and redemption of antihypertensives, with hazard ratios (HR) of 0.91 (95% confidence intervals (CI): 0.78–1.06) for outdoor WTN ≥ 42 dB(A) and of 1.06 (CI: 0.83–1.35) for indoor LF WTN ≥ 15 dB(A) when compared to the reference WTN levels (<24 dB(A) and <5 dB(A), respectively). The lack of association was consistent across sub-populations of people living on farms, far from major roads and with high validity of the noise estimate. For people younger than 65 years we found HRs of 0.81 (95% CI: 0.67–0.98) and 0.94 (95% CI: 0.68–1.30) for outdoor WTN ≥ 42 dB(A) and indoor WTN ≥ 15 dB(A), respectively, whereas for people above 65 years the corresponding HRs were 1.17 (95% CI: 0.90–1.52) and 1.28 (95% CI: 0.87–1.88). In conclusion, the present study does not support an association between WTN and redemption of antihypertensive medication.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Peña, Alfredo","Hahmann, Andrea N.","Nordsborg, Rikke Baastrup","Ketzel, Matthias","Brandt, Jørgen","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S03-095.69-021815"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo"],"keyword":["Antihypertensives","Epidemiology","Hypertension","Prescription","Prospective","Wind turbine noise"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to wind turbine noise and redemption of antihypertensive medication a nationwide cohort study","src":["au","dtu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envint.2018.08.054","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-095.69-021815","identifier":[{"id":"85053075705","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30216773","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-7d7732d0-91db-4a79-a790-e8446e53b305","dtu-7fb061e2-71a6-44b1-82db-9bc12368c70b","ruc-5caa0994-c730-4a99-8fb7-955c6bc8ac79"],"keyword":["Antihypertensives","Epidemiology","Hypertension","Prescription","Prospective","Wind turbine noise"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-78CA41338C61EE1A5033A7C8EDC25E00"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/156096098/1_s2.0_S0160412018303726_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/64744068/1_s2.0_S0160412018303726_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envint.2018.08.054","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/166646448/1_s2.0_S0160412018303726_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Meteorology & Remote Sensing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfredo","key":"penadiazpau","last":"Pena Diaz","locid":"2292abbf-9c66-4504-a423-128432556c8c","name":"Peña, Alfredo","name_org":"Pena Diaz, Alfredo","orcid":"0000-0002-7900-9651","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea N.","key":"hahmannpau","last":"Hahmann","locid":"c8315d00-83a0-43f3-85c8-cf51258cdc00","name":"Hahmann, Andrea N.","orcid":"0000-0001-8785-3492","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Baastrup","key":"nordsborgpau","last":"Nordsborg","name":"Nordsborg, Rikke Baastrup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30216773"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envint.2018.08.054","issn":["01604120","18736750"],"issn_org":["01604120"],"issue":"Part 1","journal":"Environment International","pages":"207-215","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Environment International","volume":"121"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053075705"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7d7732d0-91db-4a79-a790-e8446e53b305","dtu-7fb061e2-71a6-44b1-82db-9bc12368c70b","ruc-5caa0994-c730-4a99-8fb7-955c6bc8ac79"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Long-term exposure to wind turbine noise and redemption of antihypertensive medication : A nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-095.69-021815","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Treatment adherence is a prerequisite for treatment success and therefore an important consideration to assure that therapeutic goals are achieved both from a patient point of view and for optimal health care resource utilization. Published data on treatment adherence with fingolimod (Gilenya®) are limited. Therefore, this study investigated treatment adherence in patients with relapsing-remitting multiple sclerosis (RRMS) treated with fingolimod in Denmark. Patients and methods: This was a 24-month, multicenter, open-label study, investigating treatment adherence, satisfaction, motivation, and health-related quality of life (QoL) in RRMS patients treated with fingolimod. In addition, the effect of a motivational interview support program on these measures was evaluated. Treatment adherence was assessed by pill count. Treatment satisfaction, motivation, and QoL were assessed by patient-reported outcomes (PROs). Results: A total of 195 patients were enrolled in the study. A very high treatment adherence was observed during the entire study with no statistically significant difference between study visits before (99%) and after (97%) the motivational interview. In accordance, a high level of treatment satisfaction was found in the Treatment Satisfaction Questionnaire for Medication 9, which was scored high throughout the study with the highest scores seen for the convenience domain (ranging from 94.51 to 95.78). Furthermore, additional PROs demonstrated a high health-related QoL, a self-determined form of motivation for taking medication, and a patient perception of an autonomy supportive approach provided by the health care provider, at all study visits. Conclusion: High levels of treatment adherence, satisfaction, motivation, and QoL were observed in Danish RRMS patients treated with fingolimod. As these positive measures were observed at all study visits and throughout the study, no effect of the motivational interview support program was found.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Schreiber, Karen","Kant, Matthias","Pfleger, Claudia Christina","Jensen, Henrik Boye","Oesterberg, Ole","Hald, Anne Rieper","Nielsen, Frederik K","Rubak, Sune"],"cuid":["S03-098.45-006362"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Oesterberg, Ole"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Novartis Switzerland"],"keyword":["Gilenya®","Motivational interview","Multiple sclerosis","Quality of Life","Treatment adherence","Treatment satisfaction questionnaire for medication"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high treatment adherence satisfaction motivation and health related quality of life with fingolimod in patients with relapsing remitting multiple sclerosis results from a 000000000024 month multicenter open label danish study","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/PPA.S166278","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.45-006362","identifier":[{"id":"29988735","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6029605","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85058676433","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8360ff3b-e7e5-45f1-bd55-3446b856f966","au-4bbc150d-fbe8-4eb4-b8b3-dddbbda1f1ff","sdu-dac37830-fc62-4fed-a192-5c03dde5e146"],"keyword":["Gilenya (R)","Gilenya®","Motivational interview","Multiple sclerosis","Quality of life","Treatment adherence","Treatment satisfaction questionnaire for medication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-6A934FDE67BA7A6064562CC1DA48320C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/146550335/ppa_166278_high_treatment_adherence_satisfaction_motivation_and_quali_062818.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/PPA.S166278","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 3.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/286915347/ppa_166278_high_treatment_adherence_satisfaction_motivation_and_quali_062818.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Hospital Sønderjylland, Research Unit of Neurology (Sønderborg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"