optica spectrum disorders based on the 2015 International Panel for NMO Diagnosis (IPND) criteria.","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-603371","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Aims: The number of people exposed to wind turbine noise (WTN) is increasing. WTN is reported as more annoying than traffic noise at similar levels. Long-term exposure to traffic noise has consistently been associated with cardiovascular disease, whereas effects of short-term exposure are much less investigated due to little day-to-day variation of e.g. road traffic noise. WTN varies considerably due to changing weather conditions allowing investigation of short-term effects of WTN on cardiovascular events. Methods and results: We identified all hospitalisations and deaths from stroke (16,913 cases) and myocardial infarction (MI) (17,559 cases) among Danes exposed to WTN between 1982 and 2013. We applied a time-stratified, case-crossover design. Using detailed data on wind turbine type and hourly wind data at each wind turbine, we simulated mean nighttime outdoor (10â€“10,000 Hz) and nighttime low frequency (LF) indoor WTN (10â€“160 Hz) over the 4 days preceding diagnosis and reference days. For indoor LF WTN between 10 and 15 dB(A) and above 15 dB(A), odds ratios (ORs) for MI were 1.27 (95% confidence interval (CI): 0.97â€“1.67; cases = 198) and 1.62 (95% CI: 0.76â€“3.45; cases = 21), respectively, when compared to indoor LF WTN below 5 dB(A). For stroke, corresponding ORs were 1.17 (95% CI: 0.95â€“1.69; cases = 166) and 2.30 (95% CI: 0.96â€“5.50; cases = 15). The elevated ORs above 15 dB(A) persisted across sensitivity analyses. When looking at specific lag times, noise exposure one day before MI events and three days before stroke events were associated with the highest ORs. For outdoor WTN at night, we observed both increased and decreased risk estimates. Conclusion: This study did not provide conclusive evidence of an association between WTN and MI or stroke. It does however suggest that indoor LF WTN at night may trigger cardiovascular events, whereas these events seemed largely unaffected by nighttime outdoor WTN. These findings need reproduction, as they were based on few cases and may be due to chance.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Peña, Alfredo","Hahmann, Andrea N.","Nordsborg, Rikke Baastrup","Ketzel, Matthias","Brandt, Jørgen","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-095.52-019793"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Myocardial Infarction","Noise","Stroke","Wind turbines"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short term nighttime wind turbine noise and cardiovascular events a nationwide case crossover study from denmark","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85042719530","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.52-019793","identifier":[{"id":"29505969","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85042719530","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-624ceb32-3b6c-4e63-a13b-7d070c433fba","dtu-65490a53-17e3-45de-9c3f-746c6b216ae8"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Myocardial infarction","Noise","Stroke","Wind turbines"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D82EF078CF91BFD2604E369B5122B5AE"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Meteorology & Remote Sensing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfredo","key":"penadiazpau","last":"Pena Diaz","locid":"2292abbf-9c66-4504-a423-128432556c8c","name":"Peña, Alfredo","name_org":"Pena Diaz, Alfredo","orcid":"0000-0002-7900-9651","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea N.","key":"hahmannpau","last":"Hahmann","locid":"c8315d00-83a0-43f3-85c8-cf51258cdc00","name":"Hahmann, Andrea N.","orcid":"0000-0001-8785-3492","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Baastrup","key":"nordsborgpau","last":"Nordsborg","name":"Nordsborg, Rikke Baastrup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29505969"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envint.2018.02.030","issn":["01604120","18736750"],"issn_org":["01604120"],"journal":"Environment International","pages":"160-166","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Environment International","volume":"114"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85042719530"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-624ceb32-3b6c-4e63-a13b-7d070c433fba","dtu-65490a53-17e3-45de-9c3f-746c6b216ae8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Short-term nighttime wind turbine noise and cardiovascular events : A nationwide case-crossover study from Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.52-019793","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: Oral insulin as a preventive strategy and/or treatment of type 1 diabetes has been the target of much research. Producing oral insulins is a complex and challenging task, with numerous pitfalls, due to physiological, physical, and biochemical barriers. Our aim was to determine the impact of oral insulin on the delicate gut microbiota composition. Methods: Female nonobese diabetic mice were given oral porcine insulin 2 times a week from 5 weeks of age for 4 weeks, and then subsequently once a week for 21 weeks, or until euthanized. The mice were divided into groups on a gluten-reduced diet or a standard diet. Gut microbiota composition was analysed based on faecal samples, and the type 1 diabetes incidence of the mice was monitored. Results: We observed no influence of the oral porcine insulin on the gut microbiota composition of mice on a gluten-reduced or a standard diet at 9 weeks of age. Also, the administration of oral insulin did not influence the incidence of type 1 diabetes at 30 weeks of age. Conclusions: Oral porcine insulin does not alter the gut microbiota composition of nonobese diabetic mice on either a gluten-reduced diet or standard diet. Also, the oral porcine insulin did not influence the incidence of type 1 diabetes in the groups.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kihl, Pernille","Krych, Lukasz","Buschard, Karsten","Wesley, Johnna D.","Kot, Witold","Hansen, Axel Kornerup","Nielsen, Dennis S.","von Herrath, Matthias G."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-018935"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kihl, Pernille"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Novo Nordisk, USA"],"keyword":["Insulin","Microbiota","NOD","Oral","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oral insulin does not alter gut microbiota composition of nod mice","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85046119879","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-018935","identifier":[{"id":"85046119879","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29637693","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-56331334-0bd1-4e1b-b76f-eeaae74ddaad","ku-0ce279b7-e3a1-4251-9cce-ba9076617fca"],"keyword":["Insulin","Microbiota","NOD","Oral","Type 1 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6D3FFCF3D908EFBD0D4FBA4E37B8C510"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Lifepharm","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Preclinical Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"novo nordisk usa","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk, USA","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Environmental Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Pernille","key":"kihlpau","last":"Kihl","locid":"e974d661-5548-4349-a8f0-997b41fec98f","name":"Kihl, Pernille","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lukasz","key":"krychpau","last":"Krych","locid":"a9463259-048d-4fd6-8218-dde9fb94c96b","name":"Krych, Lukasz","orcid":"0000-0003-3224-1346","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Karsten","key":"buschardpau","last":"Buschard","name":"Buschard, Karsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Johnna D.","key":"wesleypau","last":"Wesley","name":"Wesley, Johnna D.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Witold","key":"kotpau","last":"Kot","locid":"1ed8825e-1c59-4e9b-bcd7-974d5f6d8f01","name":"Kot, Witold","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Axel Kornerup","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ecc439ea-5c9b-4e25-814a-3ee8960bc0d0","name":"Hansen, Axel Kornerup","orcid":"0000-0003-1575-2507","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dennis S.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08539a0e-05f4-454e-ad2a-de195363dbd1","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","name_org":"Nielsen, Dennis S.","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias G.","key":"vonherrathpau","last":"von Herrath","name":"von Herrath, Matthias G.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29637693"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/dmrr.3010","issn":["15207552","15207560"],"issn_org":["15207552"],"issue":"6","journal":"Diabetes/Metabolism Research and Reviews","paperid":"e3010","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Diabetes/Metabolism Research and Reviews","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046119879"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-56331334-0bd1-4e1b-b76f-eeaae74ddaad","ku-0ce279b7-e3a1-4251-9cce-ba9076617fca"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Oral insulin does not alter gut microbiota composition of NOD mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-018935","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To estimate the nationwide population-based incidence, prevalence, and geographical distribution of neuromyelitis optica (NMO) spectrum disorder (NMOSD) in Denmark based on the 2015 International Panel for NMO Diagnosis (IPND) criteria. METHODS: We conducted a multicentre, historically prospective study. Data were sourced from the Danish National Patient Registry, the Danish Multiple Sclerosis Registry, departments of neurology, and laboratories providing aquaporin-4 antibody test. Cases were selected based on the 2006 Wingerchuk and the 2015 IPND criteria and were individually validated by an expert panel. RESULTS: We confirmed NMO in 30 cases (2006 criteria) and NMOSD in 56 cases (2015 IPND criteria) between 2007 and 2014. Defined by the 2006 criteria, the incidence of NMO was 0.029 per 100,000 person-years (95% confidence interval [CI] 0.014-0.051), and the prevalence (aged 16 years and older) was 0.566 per 100,000 (95% CI 0.370-0.830). Based on the 2015 IPND criteria, the incidence of NMOSD was 0.070 per 100,000 person-years (95% CI 0.046-0.102), and the prevalence (aged 16 years and older) was 1.09 per 100,000 (95% CI 0.808-1.440), without regional differences. CONCLUSIONS: Our estimates of incidence and prevalence are similar to other Caucasian population-based studies using the 2015 IPND criteria. We found no geographical clustering in Denmark.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Papp, Viktoria","Illes, Zsolt","Magyari, Melinda","Koch-Henriksen, Nils","Kant, Matthias","Pfleger, Claudia Christina","Roemer, Shanu Faerch","Jensen, Michael Broksgaard","Petersen, Annett Evelyn","Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted","Rosendahl, Lene","Mezei, Zsolt","Christensen, Tove","Svendsen, Kristina","Hyldgaard Jensen, Poul Erik","Lydolph, Magnus Christian","Heegaard, Niels","Frederiksen, Jette Lautrup","Sellebjerg, Finn","Stenager, Egon","Petersen, Thor"],"cuid":["S04-099.39-004500"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 cont