{"abstract":"Overexploitation is one of the main pressures driving wildlife closer to extinction, yet broad-scale data to evaluate species’ declines are limited. Using African pangolins (Family: Pholidota) as a case study, we demonstrate that collating local-scale data can provide crucial information on regional trends in exploitation of threatened species to inform conservation actions and policy. We estimate that 0.4-2.7 million pangolins are hunted annually in Central African forests. The number of pangolins hunted has increased by ∼150% and the proportion of pangolins of all vertebrates hunted increased from 0.04% to 1.83% over the past four decades. However, there were no trends in pangolins observed at markets, suggesting use of alternative supply chains. We found evidence that the price of giant (Smutsia gigantea) and arboreal (Phataginus sp.) pangolins in urban markets has increased, mirroring trends in Asian pangolins. Efforts and resources are needed to increase law enforcement and population monitoring, and investigate linkages between subsistence hunting and illegal wildlife trade.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Ingram, Daniel J.","Coad, Lauren","Abernethy, Katharine A.","Maisels, Fiona","Stokes, Emma J.","Bobo, Kadiri S.","Breuer, Thomas","Gandiwa, Edson","Ghiurghi, Andrea","Greengrass, Elizabeth","Holmern, Tomas","Kamgaing, Towa O. W.","Obiang, Anne-Marie Ndong","Poulsen, John R.","Schleicher, Judith","Nielsen, Martin Reinhardt","Solly, Hilary","Vath, Carrie L.","Waltert, Matthias","Whitham, Charlotte E. L.","Wilkie, David S.","Scharlemann, Jörn P. W."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-514855"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Cameroon","Czechia","Gabon","Germany","Indonesia","Japan","Norway","United Kingdom","United States","Zimbabwe"],"glorg":["Agence Nationale des Parcs Nationaux, Libreville, Gabon","All Global Affiliations","Born Free Foundation","Center for International Forestry Research, West Java","Chinhoyi University of Technology","Czech Academy of Sciences","Duke University","Institut de Recherches en Ecologie Tropicale, CENAREST, Libreville, Gabon","Kyoto University","Ministry of Forestry and Wildlife, Garoua, Cameroon","Montana Tech","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","UN Environment World Conservation Monitoring Centre","University of Florida","University of Göttingen","University of Stirling","University of Sussex","Université de Dschang","Wildlife Conservation Society, NY, USA"],"keyword":["Africa","Hunting","Market","Offtake","Trade","Wild meat"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessing africa wide pangolin exploitation by scaling local data","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/conl.12389","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-514855","identifier":[{"id":"85026376384","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cb565f18-9959-4bf7-9f89-77e4f34e82f4"],"keyword":["Africa","OFFTAKE","hunting","market","pangolins","trade","wild meat"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FC054410BFDF27FF766F5F1410F1C8F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/210977133/Ingram_et_al_2018_Conservation_Letters.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/conl.12389","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of sussex","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"