{"abstract":"Despite broad agreement that the Americas were initially populated via Beringia, the land bridge that connected far northeast Asia with northwestern North America during the Pleistocene epoch, when and how the peopling of the Americas occurred remains unresolved. Analyses of human remains from Late Pleistocene Alaska are important to resolving the timing and dispersal of these populations. The remains of two infants were recovered at Upward Sun River (USR), and have been dated to around 11.5 thousand years ago (ka). Here, by sequencing the USR1 genome to an average coverage of approximately 17 times, we show that USR1 is most closely related to Native Americans, but falls basal to all previously sequenced contemporary and ancient Native Americans. As such, USR1 represents a distinct Ancient Beringian population. Using demographic modelling, we infer that the Ancient Beringian population and ancestors of other Native Americans descended from a single founding population that initially split from East Asians around 36 ± 1.5 ka, with gene flow persisting until around 25 ± 1.1 ka. Gene flow from ancient north Eurasians into all Native Americans took place 25-20 ka, with Ancient Beringians branching off around 22-18.1 ka. Our findings support a long-term genetic structure in ancestral Native Americans, consistent with the Beringian 'standstill model'. We show that the basal northern and southern Native American branches, to which all other Native Americans belong, diverged around 17.5-14.6 ka, and that this probably occurred south of the North American ice sheets. We also show that after 11.5 ka, some of the northern Native American populations received gene flow from a Siberian population most closely related to Koryaks, but not Palaeo-Eskimos, Inuits or Kets, and that Native American gene flow into Inuits was through northern and not southern Native American groups. Our findings further suggest that the far-northern North American presence of northern Native Americans is from a back migration that replaced or absorbed the initial founding population of Ancient Beringians.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Moreno-Mayar, J Víctor","Potter, Ben A","Vinner, Lasse","Steinrücken, Matthias","Rasmussen, Simon","Terhorst, Jonathan","Kamm, John A","Albrechtsen, Anders","Malaspinas, Anna-Sapfo","Sikora, Martin","Reuther, Joshua D","Irish, Joel D","Malhi, Ripan S","Orlando, Ludovic","Song, Yun S","Nielsen, Rasmus","Meltzer, David J","Willerslev, Eske"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-356104"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Liverpool John Moores University","University of Alaska Fairbanks","University of California at Berkeley","University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","University of Massachusetts"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"terminal pleistocene alaskan genome reveals first founding population of native americans","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/185058992/UpwardSun_Nature_paper_MS_DEC17.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-356104","identifier":[{"id":"29323294","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85040467287","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ac82345e-74cf-4e76-9b98-5555138108de"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-08B567E5C65CBF2BE1132AB11BC46C1A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/185058992/UpwardSun_Nature_paper_MS_DEC17.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of alaska fairbanks","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Alaska Fairbanks","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of massachusetts","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Massachusetts","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Bio and Health Informatics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Bio and Health Informatics, Metagenomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of california at berkeley","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Berkeley","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"liverpool john moores university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Liverpool John Moores University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"university of illinois at urbana champaign","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J Víctor","key":"morenomayarpau","last":"Moreno-Mayar","name":"Moreno-Mayar, J Víctor","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben A","key":"potterpau","last":"Potter","name":"Potter, Ben A","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse","key":"vinnerpau","last":"Vinner","name":"Vinner, Lasse","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"steinrückenpau","last":"Steinrücken","name":"Steinrücken, Matthias","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"7dcb9d6e-8054-4bcf-a087-82517b291a32","name":"Rasmussen, Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-6323-9041","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan","key":"terhorstpau","last":"Terhorst","name":"Terhorst, Jonathan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"John A","key":"kammpau","last":"Kamm","name":"Kamm, John A","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"albrechtsenpau","last":"Albrechtsen","name":"Albrechtsen, Anders","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna-Sapfo","key":"malaspinaspau","last":"Malaspinas","name":"Malaspinas, Anna-Sapfo","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"sikorapau","last":"Sikora","name":"Sikora, Martin","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joshua D","key":"reutherpau","last":"Reuther","name":"Reuther, Joshua D","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Joel D","key":"irishpau","last":"Irish","name":"Irish, Joel D","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Ripan S","key":"malhipau","last":"Malhi","name":"Malhi, Ripan S","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ludovic","key":"orlandopau","last":"Orlando","name":"Orlando, Ludovic","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Yun S","key":"songpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Yun S","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David J","key":"meltzerpau","last":"Meltzer","name":"Meltzer, David J","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eske","key":"willerslevpau","last":"Willerslev","name":"Willerslev, Eske","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29323294"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/nature25173","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"7687","journal":"Nature","pages":"203-207","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"553"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040467287"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ac82345e-74cf-4e76-9b98-5555138108de"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Terminal Pleistocene Alaskan genome reveals first founding population of Native Americans","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-356104","year":"2017","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Standard infrared spectroscopy techniques are well-developed and widely used. However, they typically require milligrams of sample and can involve time-consuming sample preparation. A promising alternative is represented by nanomechanical infrared spectroscopy (NAM-IR) based on the photothermal response of a nanomechanical resonator, which enables the chemical analysis of picograms of analyte directly from a liquid solution in only a few minutes. Herein, we present NAM-IR using perforated membranes (filters). The method was tested with the pharmaceutical compound indomethacin to successfully perform a chemical and morphological analysis on roughly 100 pg of sample. With an absolute estimated sensitivity of 109±15 fg, the presented method is suitable for ultrasensitive vibrational spectroscopy.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kurek, Maksymilian","Carnoy, Matthias","Larsen, Peter Emil","Nielsen, Line Hagner","Hansen, Ole","Rades, Thomas","Schmid, Silvan","Boisen, Anja"],"cuid":["S02-092.86-032611"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","TU Wien"],"keyword":["Crystallization","IR spectroscopy","Journal Article","Nanomechanics","Nanoparticles"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nanomechanical infrared spectroscopy with vibrating filters for pharmaceutical analysis","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/179892595/PP_Nanomechanical_Infrared_Spectroscopy_with_Vibrating_Filters_for_Pharm.._.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-092.86-032611","identifier":[{"id":"28266106","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85014729669","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-01e16958-b43e-4117-a936-3a2b0044e6fa","ku-54d59565-01d4-474d-8f64-2fec6d335428"],"keyword":["IR spectroscopy","Journal Article","crystallization","nanomechanics","nanoparticles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F9093B68E9E15092E57BDAA293B45B7B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/179892595/PP_Nanomechanical_Infrared_Spectroscopy_with_Vibrating_Filters_for_Pharm.._.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, Nanoprobes"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Design and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"tu wien","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"TU Wien","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maksymilian","key":"kurekpau","last":"Kurek","locid":"cc2e7ba8-55af-4e5d-94f0-b78a868454c4","name":"Kurek, Maksymilian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"carnoypau","last":"Carnoy","name":"Carnoy, Matthias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Emil","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"32b8c221-c511-48f7-894a-c1f3616c8eeb","name":"Larsen, Peter Emil","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Hagner","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a9a7a51b-9e8f-40cc-b691-6e64d62e7765","name":"Nielsen, Line Hagner","orcid":"0000-0002-3789-4816","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8d678857-a721-4f7f-9a33-1dadb7401ce4","name":"Hansen, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-6090-8323","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"radespau","last":"Rades","locid":"e3c9db98-a0f8-4161-911f-d6ffdccbfdc6","name":"Rades, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7521-6020","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Silvan","key":"schmidpau","last":"Schmid","name":"Schmid, Silvan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anja","key":"boisenpau","last":"Boisen","locid":"898c472f-7fe0-4454-83d8-564450caa2cb","name":"Boisen, Anja","orcid":"0000-0002-9918-6567","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28266106"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/anie.201700052","issn":["14337851","15213773"],"issn_org":["14337851"],"issue":"14","journal":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","pages":"3901-3905","status":"p","title":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","title_org":"Angewandte Chemie (International ed. in English)","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85014729669"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-01e16958-b43e-4117-a936-3a2b0044e6fa","ku-54d59565-01d4-474d-8f64-2fec6d335428"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nanomechanical Infrared Spectroscopy with Vibrating Filters for Pharmaceutical Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.86-032611","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Road traffic is a main source of air pollution and noise. Both exposures have been associated with type 2 diabetes, but associations with gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) have been studied less. OBJECTIVES: We aimed to examine single and joint associations of exposure to air pollution and road traffic noise on GDM in a prospective cohort. METHODS: We identified GDM cases from self-reports and hospital records, using two different criteria, among 72,745 singleton pregnancies (1997-2002) from the Danish National Birth Cohort. We modeled nitrogen dioxide (NO2) and noise from road traffic (Lden) exposure at all pregnancy addresses. RESULTS: According to the two diagnostic criteria: the Danish clinical guidelines, which was our main outcome, and the WHO standard during recruitment period, a total of 565 and 210 women, respectively, had GDM. For both exposures no risk was evident for the common Danish criterion of GDM. A 10-μg/m(3) increase in NO2 exposure during first trimester was, however, associated with an increased risk of WHO-GDM (adjusted odds ratio (OR)=1.24; 95% confidence interval (CI): 1.03, 1.49). The corresponding OR associated with a 10-dB higher road traffic noise level was 1.15 (0.94 to 1.18). In mutually adjusted models the OR for NO2 remained similar 1.22 (0.98, 1.53) whereas that for road traffic noise decreased to 1.03 (0.80, 1.32). Significant associations were also observed for exposure averaged over the 2nd and 3rd trimesters and the full pregnancy. CONCLUSIONS: No risk was evident for the common Danish criterion of GDM. NO2 was associated with higher risk for GDM according to the WHO criterion, which might be due to selection bias.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Pedersen, Marie","Olsen, Sjurdur F","Halldorsson, Thorhallur I","Zhang, Cuilin","Hjortebjerg, Dorrit","Ketzel, Matthias","Grandström, Charlotta","Sørensen, Mette","Damm, Peter","Langhoff-Roos, Jens","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-099.92-024057"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Iceland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University","Landspitali University Hospital","University of Iceland"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Environment","Gestational diabetes mellitus","Journal Article","Noise","Pregnancy","Traffic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gestational diabetes mellitus and exposure to ambient air pollution and road traffic noise a cohort study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85028934463","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.92-024057","identifier":[{"id":"28892786","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85028934463","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9c21142a-24b6-40e1-9e9d-05565f4ea6f8","ku-f316efdf-aa59-4ba9-858e-fa183c92e772"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Environment","Gestational diabetes mellitus","Journal Article","Noise","Pregnancy","Traffic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5BCE9D8249E89F8FD4788B6C39639A78"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Center of Epidemiology and Screening","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"is","key":"university of iceland","loc":["Iceland","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Iceland","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"is","key":"landspitali university hospital","loc":["Iceland","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Landspitali University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"f9e8bb91-df6a-44b7-94ea-b1e18961767b","name":"Pedersen, Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-9930-0446","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sjurdur F","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Sjurdur F","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorhallur I","key":"halldorssonpau","last":"Halldorsson","name":"Halldorsson, Thorhallur I","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Cuilin","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Cuilin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorrit","key":"hjortebjergpau","last":"Hjortebjerg","name":"Hjortebjerg, Dorrit","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotta","key":"grandströmpau","last":"Grandström","name":"Grandström, Charlotta","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"dammpau","last":"Damm","locid":"884d03d5-5981-4d33-80c6-adb21f836deb","name":"Damm, Peter","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"langhoffroospau","last":"Langhoff-Roos","name":"Langhoff-Roos, Jens","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28892786"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envint.2017.09.003","issn":["01604120","18736750"],"issn_org":["01604120"],"journal":"Environment International","pages":"253-260","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Environment International","volume":"108"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85028934463"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9c21142a-24b6-40e1-9e9d-05565f4ea6f8","ku-f316efdf-aa59-4ba9-858e-fa183c92e772"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gestational diabetes mellitus and exposure to ambient air pollution and road traffic noise : A cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.92-024057","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Malaria remains one of the most serious infections for travellers to tropical countries. Due to the lack of harmonized guidelines a large variety of treatment regimens is used in Europe to treat severe malaria. METHODS: The European Network for Tropical Medicine and Travel Health (TropNet) conducted an 8-year, multicentre, observational study to analyse epidemiology, treatment practices and outcomes of severe malaria in its member sites across Europe. Physicians at participating TropNet centres were asked to report pseudonymized retrospective data from all patients treated at their centre for microscopically confirmed severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria according to the 2006 WHO criteria. RESULTS: From 2006 to 2014 a total of 185 patients with severe malaria treated in 12 European countries were included. Three patients died, resulting in a 28-day survival rate of 98.4%. The majority of infections were acquired in West Africa (109/185, 59%). The proportion of patients treated with intravenous artesunate increased from 27% in 2006 to 60% in 2013. Altogether, 56 different combinations of intravenous and oral drugs were used across 28 study centres. The risk of acute renal failure (36 vs 17% p = 0.04) or cerebral malaria (54 vs 20%, p = 0.001) was significantly higher in patients ≥60 years than in younger patients. Respiratory distress with the need for mechanical ventilation was significantly associated with the risk of death in the study population (13 vs 0%, p = 0.001). Post-artemisinin delayed haemolysis was reported in 19/70 (27%) patients treated with intravenous artesunate. CONCLUSION: The majority of patients with severe malaria in this study were tourists or migrants acquiring the infection in West Africa. Intravenous artesunate is increasingly used for treatment of severe malaria in many European treatment centres and can be given safely to European patients with severe malaria. Patients treated with intravenous artesunate should be followed up to detect and manage late haemolytic events.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Kurth, Florian","Develoux, Michel","Mechain, Matthieu","Malvy, Denis","Clerinx, Jan","Antinori, Spinello","Gjørup, Ida E","Gascon, Joaquím","Mørch, Kristine","Nicastri, Emanuele","Ramharter, Michael","Bartoloni, Alessandro","Visser, Leo","Rolling, Thierry","Zanger, Philipp","Calleri, Guido","Salas-Coronas, Joaquín","Nielsen, Henrik","Just-Nübling, Gudrun","Neumayr, Andreas","Hachfeld, Anna","Schmid, Matthias L","Antonini, Pietro","Lingscheid, Tilman","Kern, Peter","Kapaun, Annette","da Cunha, José Saraiva","Pongratz, Peter","Soriano-Arandes, Antoni","Schunk, Mirjam","Suttorp, Norbert","Hatz, Christoph","Zoller, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-057404"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Spain","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Heidelberg University Hospital","Heidelberg University ","Hospital Universitari Vall d'Hebron, Barcelona, Spain.","University Hospital Basel"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Hôpital Saint-Antoine, Paris, France."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"severe malaria in europe an 000000000008 year multi centre observational study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12936-016-1673-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-057404","identifier":[{"id":"000393624300005","type":"wos"},{"id":"28143519","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5286792","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85011349865","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-192085e0-5742-47eb-9dc9-21f52991b6ce"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D11142ECF651D45EA3B39697CB5E2709"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5286792/pdf/12936_2016_Article_1673.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12936-016-1673-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/272987596/Severe_malaria_in_Europe_an_8_year_multi_centre_observational_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"charité universitätsmedizin berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Hôpital Saint-Antoine, Paris, France."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"heidelberg university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Heidelberg University ","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Infektionsmedicin [Klinik Medicin]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ch","key":"university hospital basel","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital Basel","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"heidelberg university hospital","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Heidelberg University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"es","key":"hospital universitari vall d hebron barcelona spain","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hospital Universitari Vall d'Hebron, Barcelona, Spain.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Florian","key":"kurthpau","last":"Kurth","name":"Kurth, Florian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michel","key":"develouxpau","last":"Develoux","name":"Develoux, Michel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthieu","key":"mechainpau","last":"Mechain","name":"Mechain, Matthieu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Denis","key":"malvypau","last":"Malvy","name":"Malvy, Denis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"clerinxpau","last":"Clerinx","name":"Clerinx, Jan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Spinello","key":"antinoripau","last":"Antinori","name":"Antinori, Spinello","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida E","key":"gjøruppau","last":"Gjørup","name":"Gjørup, Ida E","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joaquím","key":"gasconpau","last":"Gascon","name":"Gascon, Joaquím","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine","key":"mørchpau","last":"Mørch","name":"Mørch, Kristine","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emanuele","key":"nicastripau","last":"Nicastri","name":"Nicastri, Emanuele","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"ramharterpau","last":"Ramharter","name":"Ramharter, Michael","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"bartolonipau","last":"Bartoloni","name":"Bartoloni, Alessandro","r