{"abstract":"The purpose of this study was to investigate the accuracy and precision of fast plane wave 2-D vector flow imaging (VFI) under laminar and complex flow conditions in a human subject. The method has previously been validated in simulations and straight-vessel phantoms, however, complex flow patterns remain challenging to study, since there are no other imaging techniques accurately enough to compare with. Here, the approach was to study (1) the accuracy by comparing VFI obtained from a patient-specific phantom measurement to computational fluid dynamics (CFD) simulated velocities derived from the same geometry; and (2) the precision in vivo by calculating the standard deviation (SD) of VFI estimates at several evaluation points.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Jensen, Jonas","Hoyos, Carlos Armando Villagomez","Olesen, Jacob Bjerring","Tomov, Borislav","Traberg, Marie Sand","Moshavegh, Ramin","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Ewertsen, Caroline","Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Jensen, Jorgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-494446"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-09","place":"Washington, us","start":"2017-09-06","title":"2017 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium, IUS 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accuracy and precision study of plane wave vector flow imaging for laminar and complex flow in vivo","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-494446","identifier":[{"id":"85039449336","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a91c7143-728a-413d-8b87-41f9f8ff4a10"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-16B075E5904F8EB6768B9F1AD408D895"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas","key":"jensenjonaspau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jonas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carlos Armando Villagomez","key":"hoyoscarlosarmandovillagomezpau","last":"Hoyos","name":"Hoyos, Carlos Armando Villagomez","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob Bjerring","key":"olesenjacobbjerringpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Jacob Bjerring","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Borislav","key":"tomovborislavpau","last":"Tomov","name":"Tomov, Borislav","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Sand","key":"trabergmariesandpau","last":"Traberg","name":"Traberg, Marie Sand","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ramin","key":"moshaveghraminpau","last":"Moshavegh","name":"Moshavegh, Ramin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartmatthiasbopau","last":"Stuart","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Caroline","key":"ewertsencarolinepau","last":"Ewertsen","locid":"51880e6f-4b00-4868-9005-6a0464367816","name":"Ewertsen, Caroline","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kristoffer Lindskov","key":"hansenkristofferlindskovpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"13d27542-8511-49cf-aec4-45950ec963b0","name":"Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenmichaelbachmannpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jorgen Arendt","key":"jensenjorgenarendtpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jorgen Arendt","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a91c7143-728a-413d-8b87-41f9f8ff4a10"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Accuracy and precision study of plane wave vector flow imaging for laminar and complex flow in vivo","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-494446","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Several techniques can estimate the 2-D velocity vector in ultrasound. Directional beamforming (DB) estimates blood flow velocities with a higher precision and accuracy than transverse oscillation (TO), but at the cost of a high beamforming load when estimating the flow angle. In this paper, it is proposed to use TO to estimate an initial flow angle, which is then refined in a DB step. Velocity magnitude is estimated along the flow direction using cross correlation. It is shown that the suggested TO-DB method can improve the performance of velocity estimates compared with TO, and with a beamforming load, which is 4.6 times larger than for TO and seven times smaller than for conventional DB. Steered plane wave transmissions are employed for high frame rate imaging, and parabolic flow with a peak velocity of 0.5 m/s is simulated in straight vessels at beam-to-flow angles from 45° to 90°. The TO-DB method estimates the angle with a bias and standard deviation (SD) less than 2°, and the SD of the velocity magnitude is less than 2%. When using only TO, the SD of the angle ranges from 2° to 17° and for the velocity magnitude up to 7%. Bias of the velocity magnitude is within 2% for TO and slightly larger but within 4% for TO-DB. The same trends are observed in measurements although with a slightly larger bias. Simulations of realistic flow in a carotid bifurcation model provide visualization of complex flow, and the spread of velocity magnitude estimates is 7.1 cm/s for TO-DB, while it is 11.8 cm/s using only TO. However, velocities for TO-DB are underestimated at peak systole as indicated by a regression value of 0.97 for TO and 0.85 for TO-DB. An in vivo scanning of the carotid bifurcation is used for vector velocity estimations using TO and TO-DB. The SD of the velocity profile over a cardiac cycle is 4.2% for TO and 3.2% for TO-DB.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jensen, Jonas","Villagómez Hoyos, Carlos Armando","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Ewertsen, Caroline","Nielsen, Michael Bachamnn","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S02-093.30-033216"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Blood flow","Medical ultrasound","Plane wave imaging","Vector flow imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast plane wave 000000000002 d vector flow imaging using transverse oscillation and directional beamforming","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/190320074/TUFFC2693403.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-093.30-033216","identifier":[{"id":"85029114905","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28422656","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-1d25d514-53ea-49fa-bfdd-b48b7fe8cc58","ku-b3985d0e-c019-4544-bd7b-98c4ce4b7b0c"],"keyword":["Blood flow","Medical ultrasound","Plane wave imaging","Vector flow imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-48E1182C8B1B548A13BDB3D24EDB3AB7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/190320074/TUFFC2693403.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, MEMS-AppliedSensors"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"jensenjonaspau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ce6e719b-4e0f-4795-a9ac-91265cc918a8","name":"Jensen, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0003-4456-0838","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carlos Armando","key":"villagómezhoyoscarlosarmandopau","last":"Villagómez Hoyos","locid":"dfb725c3-c502-44e8-80b9-ed3b63177248","name":"Villagómez Hoyos, Carlos Armando","orcid":"0000-0002-2157-5677","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carlos Armando","key":"villagomezhoyoscarlosarmandopau","last":"Villagomez Hoyos","name":"Villagomez Hoyos, Carlos Armando","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartmatthiasbopau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Caroline","key":"ewertsencarolinepau","last":"Ewertsen","locid":"51880e6f-4b00-4868-9005-6a0464367816","name":"Ewertsen, Caroline","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenmichaelbachmannpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Bachamnn","key":"nielsenmichaelbachamnnpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachamnn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenjørgenarendtpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jorgen Arendt","key":"jensenjorgenarendtpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jorgen Arendt","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28422656"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tuffc.2017.2693403","issn":["08853010","15258955"],"issn_org":["08853010"],"issue":"7","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics and Frequency Control","pages":"1050-1062","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics and Frequency Control","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics and Frequency Control","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029114905"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1d25d514-53ea-49fa-bfdd-b48b7fe8cc58","ku-b3985d0e-c019-4544-bd7b-98c4ce4b7b0c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fast Plane Wave 2-D Vector Flow Imaging Using Transverse Oscillation and Directional Beamforming","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.30-033216","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Although air pollution and road traffic noise have been associated with higher risk of cardiovascular diseases, associations with heart failure have received only little attention. OBJECTIVES: We aimed to investigate whether long-term exposure to road traffic noise and nitrogen dioxide (NO2) were associated with incident heart failure. METHODS: In a cohort of 57,053 people 50-64 y of age at enrollment in the period 1993-1997, we identified 2,550 cases of first-ever hospital admission for heart failure during a mean follow-up time of 13.4 y. Present and historical residential addresses from 1987 to 2011 were found in national registers, and road traffic noise (Lden) and NO2 were modeled for all addresses. Analyses were done using Cox proportional hazard model. RESULTS: An interquartile range higher 10-y time-weighted mean exposure for Lden and NO2 was associated with incidence rate ratios (IRR) for heart failure of 1.14 (1.08-1.21) and 1.11 (1.07-1.16), respectively, in models adjusted for gender, lifestyle, and socioeconomic status. In models with mutual exposure adjustment, IRRs were 1.08 (1.00-1.16) for Lden and 1.07 (1.01-1.14) for NO2. We found statistically significant modification of the NO2-heart failure association by gender (strongest association among men), baseline hypertension (strongest association among hypertensive), and diabetes (strongest association among diabetics). The same tendencies were seen for noise, but interactions were not statistically significant. CONCLUSIONS: Long-term exposure to NO2 and road traffic noise was associated with higher risk of heart failure, mainly among men, in both single- and two-pollutant models. High exposure to both pollutants was associated with highest risk. https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP1272.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sørensen, Mette","Wendelboe Nielsen, Olav","Sajadieh, Ahmad","Ketzel, Matthias","Tjønneland, Anne","Overvad, Kim","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-003394"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Aged","Air Pollutants","Air pollution","Cohort Studies","Environmental Exposure","Female","Heart failure","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Nitrogen dioxide","Noise Transportation","Proportional Hazards Models"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to road traffic noise and nitrogen dioxide and risk of heart failure a cohort study","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP1272","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-003394","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5915207","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85032152401","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28953453","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-45471175-8ae4-4324-acf4-a26ae9e2964a","au-b8ad7488-3035-4684-8cd9-7870a7af79a0","ku-0897e3af-e5e6-470b-935a-c184a1e34766"],"keyword":["Aged","Air Pollutants","Air Pollution","Cohort Studies","Environmental Exposure","Female","Heart Failure","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Nitrogen Dioxide","Noise, Transportation","Proportional Hazards Models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-2C48A2C7A09767CCCB5143CB4459EF16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/185943395/EHP1272.alt_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC0 1.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/283366721/EHP1272.alt_.pdf","version":