:"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthias","key":"löbelpau","last":"Löbel","name":"Löbel, Matthias","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"R.J.","key":"warburtonpau","last":"Warburton","name":"Warburton, R.J.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"lodahlpau","last":"Lodahl","locid":"fa2dbf58-7de5-4c4c-a7fc-6c96dc6d6937","name":"Lodahl, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-9348-9591","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevb.96.165306","issn":["1550235X","24699950"],"issn_org":["24699950"],"journal":"Physical Review B","paperid":"165306","status":"p","title":"Physical Review B","volume":"96"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85038122113"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c90b6329-5725-4a40-90b6-7ec55274f93f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Indistinguishable and efficient single photons from a quantum dot in a planar nanobeam waveguide","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-513503","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background: Road traffic is a major source of air pollution and noise. Both exposures have been associated with hypertension in adults, but pregnant women have been less studied. Methods: We examined single and joint effects of ambient air pollution and road traffic noise on pre-eclampsia and pregnancy-induced hypertensive disorders among 72,745 singleton pregnancies (1997-2002) from the Danish National Birth Cohort with complete covariate data and residential address history from conception until live born birth. Nitrogen dioxide (NO 2) and noise from road traffic (L den) were modeled at all addresses. Outcome and covariate data were derived from registries, hospital records, and questionnaires. Results: A 10-μg/m 3 increase in NO 2 exposure during first trimester was associated with increased risk of pre-eclampsia (n = 1,880, adjusted odds ratio = 1.07 [95% confidence interval = 1.01, 1.14]) and pregnancy-induced hypertensive disorders (n = 2,430, adjusted odds ratio = 1.07 [1.01, 1.13]). A 10 dB higher road traffic noise was also associated with increased risk of pre-eclampsia (1.10 [1.02, 1.18]) and pregnancy-induced hypertensive disorders (1.08 [1.02, 1.15]). For both exposures, the associations were strongest for mild pre-eclampsia (n = 1,393) and early-onset pre-eclampsia (n = 671), whereas higher risk for severe pre-eclampsia (n = 487) was not evident. In mutually adjusted models, estimates for both exposures decreased and only the association between NO 2 and mild pre-eclampsia remained. Conclusions: Road traffic may increase the risk of pre-eclampsia and hypertensive disorders in pregnancy through exposure to both ambient air pollution and noise, although associations with the two exposures were generally not found to be independent of one another. See video abstract, http://links.lww.com/EDE/B112.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pedersen, Marie","Halldorsson, Thorhallur I","Olsen, Sjurdur F","Hjortebjerg, Dorrit","Ketzel, Matthias","Grandström, Charlotta","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-089.36-029189"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of road traffic pollution on pre eclampsia and pregnancy induced hypertensive disorders","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/EDE.0000000000000555","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.36-029189","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5380106","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84988664760","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27648591","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-e41a575c-26f3-4344-9dac-30366e30bc55","ku-0fc41b4b-3f30-4035-9807-7592ede16dc7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BBE5CA49E93CA477E6AD688628573CD6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/EDE.0000000000000555","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/191970034/00001648_201701000_00016.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Center of Epidemiology and Screening"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Marie","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"f9e8bb91-df6a-44b7-94ea-b1e18961767b","name":"Pedersen, Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-9930-0446","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thorhallur I.","key":"halldorssonpau","last":"Halldorsson","name":"Halldorsson, Thorhallur I.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Sjurdur F.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Sjurdur F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorrit","key":"hjortebjergpau","last":"Hjortebjerg","name":"Hjortebjerg, Dorrit","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Charlotta","key":"grandströmpau","last":"Grandström","name":"Grandström, Charlotta","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27648591"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/ede.0000000000000555","issn":["10443983","15315487"],"issn_org":["10443983"],"issue":"1","journal":"Epidemiology","pages":"99-106","status":"p","title":"Epidemiology","title_org":"Epidemiology (Cambridge, Mass.)","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84988664760"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e41a575c-26f3-4344-9dac-30366e30bc55","ku-0fc41b4b-3f30-4035-9807-7592ede16dc7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impact of road traffic pollution on pre-eclampsia and pregnancy-induced hypertensive disorders","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.36-029189","year":"2017","yearsub":2017}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Road traffic is a source of both air pollution and noise; two environmental hazards both found to increase the risk of ischemic heart disease. Given the high correlation between these pollutants, it is important to investigate combined effects, in relation to myocardial infarction (MI). METHODS: Among 50,744 middle-aged Danes enrolled into the Diet, Cancer and Health cohort from 1993 to 97, we identified 2403 cases of incident MI during a median follow-up of 14.5 years. Present and historical residential addresses from 1987 to 2011 were found in national registries, and traffic noise (Lden) and air pollution (NO2) were modelled for all addresses. Analyses were performed using Cox proportional hazard models. RESULTS: Road traffic noise and NO2 were both individually associated with a higher risk of MI, with hazard ratios of 1.14 (1.07-1.21) and 1.08 (1.03-1.12) per inter-quartile range higher 10-year mean of road traffic noise and NO2, respectively. Mutual exposure adjustment reduced the association with 10-year NO2 exposure (1.02 (0.96-1.08)), whereas the association with road traffic noise remained: 1.12 (1.03-1.21). For fatal incident MI, the pattern was similar, but the associations for both pollutants were stronger. In analyses of tertiles across both pollutants, the strongest effects were seen for combined medium/high exposure, especially for fatal MI's. CONCLUSION: Both road traffic noise and NO2 were associated with a higher risk of MI in single-pollutant models. In two-pollutant models, mainly noise was associated with MI. Combined exposure to both pollutants was associated with the highest risk.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Roswall, Nina","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Ketzel, Matthias","Gammelmark, Anders","Overvad, Kim","Olsen, Anja","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-000389"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Air pollution","Cohort study","Epidemiology","Journal Article","Myocardial Infarction","Traffic noise"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Danish Cancer Society Research Center, Strandboulevarden 49, DK-2100 Copenhagen Ø, Denmark; Department of Environmental Science, Aarhus University, Frederiksborgvej 399, DK-4000 Roskilde, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","Danish Cancer Society Research Center, Strandboulevarden 49, DK-2100 Copenhagen Ø, Denmark; Department of Environmental Science, Aarhus University, Frederiksborgvej 399, DK-4000 Roskilde, Denmark."]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term residential road traffic noise and no000000000002 exposure in relation to risk of incident myocardial infarction a danish cohort study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85015738537","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-000389","identifier":[{"id":"85015738537","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000403735300011","type":"wos"},{"id":"28334645","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-078c7a29-f987-4b54-9091-2b211907ad5b","au-238e1be9-5795-462d-8b6a-5b2a74962d6d"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Cohort study","Epidemiology","Journal Article","Myocardial infarction","Traffic noise"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1EDDC818449F7CC94876C92DDB5EB4E8"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"