{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Traffic noise has become an increasing public health concern, associated with pervasive negative health effects, most likely through pathways of sleep disruption and stress. Both sleep disruption and stress have been associated with colorectal cancer. The purpose of this study was to investigate the association between residential traffic noise and colorectal cancer incidence. METHODS: Traffic noise was calculated for all residential addresses from 1987 to 2012 for 51,283 Danes in the Diet, Cancer and Health Cohort. We used Cox proportional hazard models to investigate the association between residential traffic noise 5 and 10 years before diagnosis, and overall colorectal cancer incidence, as well as subtypes (rectal, proximal, and distal colon). Hazard ratios (HRs) were calculated as crude and adjusted for potential confounders. RESULTS: During follow-up, 1,134 colorectal cancers developed (737 colon, 397 rectal). We found no association between residential road traffic noise and rectal cancer. We observed an association with distal colon cancer: HR 1.18, 95% CI 1.00-1.40, but not for proximal colon cancer: 0.99 (0.83-1.18), per 10 dB, 10 years preceding diagnosis. There was no association between railway noise and colorectal cancer, or any subtype. CONCLUSION: The present study suggested that long-term exposure to residential road traffic noise might increase the risk for colon cancer, especially distal colon cancer.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Roswall, Nina","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Ketzel, Matthias","Overvad, Kim","Halkjaer, Jytte","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-190095"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeled traffic noise at the residence and colorectal cancer incidence a cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85019757366","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-190095","identifier":[{"id":"28516298","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85019757366","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6a7ced73-80f6-497c-a35d-3c00dace4ac3"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5D5EB2BC3686C593A2E3D554050474F1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"roswallpau","last":"Roswall","name":"Roswall, Nina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"overvadpau","last":"Overvad","locid":"83738c57-45d4-41e0-b807-ad0f6dec597c","name":"Overvad, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-6429-7921","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jytte","key":"halkjaerpau","last":"Halkjaer","name":"Halkjaer, Jytte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28516298"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10552-017-0904-0","issn":["09575243","15737225"],"issn_org":["09575243"],"issue":"7","journal":"Cancer Causes & Control","pages":"745-753","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Cancer Causes & Control","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019757366"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6a7ced73-80f6-497c-a35d-3c00dace4ac3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Modeled traffic noise at the residence and colorectal cancer incidence : a cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-190095","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Domain experts dealing with big data are typically not familiar with advanced data mining tools. This especially holds true for domain experts within energy management. In this paper, we introduce a visual analytics approach that empowers such users to visually analyze energy behavior based on consumption meters, sensors and user reported survey data. The approach is aimed at visual analysis of resource consumption data and occupant survey data (e.g. from questionnaires) from apartment buildings. We discuss the principles and architecture of the affine visualization tool, AffinityViz, that interactively maps data from real world buildings. It is an overview +detail inter-active visual analytics tool supporting both rapid ad hoc explorations and structured evaluation of hypotheses about patterns and anomalies in resource consumption data mixed with occupant survey data. We have evaluated the approach with five domain experts within energy management, and further with 10 data analytics experts and found that it was easily attainable and that it supported visual analysis of mixed consumption and survey data. Finally, we discuss future perspectives of affine visual analytics for mixed, explorative visual analysis of resource consumption and occupant survey data.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Matthias","Brewer, Robert S.","Grønbæk, Kaj"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-135511"],"event":{"end":"2016-12-02","place":"Launceston, au","start":"2016-11-29","title":"OzCHI '16 - the 28th Australian Conference on Computer-Human Interaction","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Applications","Design","Human factors","Information visualization","Interaction","Visual analytics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"supporting interactive visual analytics of energy behavior in buildings through affine visualizations","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85012025557","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-135511","identifier":[{"id":"85012025557","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0ae43e44-1217-478b-8c97-1934460b1706"],"keyword":["Applications","Design","Human factors","Information visualization","Interaction","Visual analytics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9FC8B90C5CD7DD54EB924788776BDE0C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"790b96d1-cd52-41e3-84ae-cd5a795fb3dc","name":"Nielsen, Matthias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert S.","key":"brewerpau","last":"Brewer","locid":"ed396415-65bb-4d83-bb46-ef7e907f29e5","name":"Brewer, Robert S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaj","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"c7b908c7-ad69-4b60-bfb2-f6d7f490bb4f","name":"Grønbæk, Kaj","orcid":"0000-0002-3752-6714","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3010915.3010950","eisbn":["9781450346184"],"pages":"238-247","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"OzCHI: Australian Conference on Human-Computer Interaction","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 28th Australian Computer-Human Interaction Conference, OzCHI 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85012025557"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0ae43e44-1217-478b-8c97-1934460b1706"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Supporting interactive visual analytics of energy behavior in buildings through affine visualizations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-135511","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The wide availability of touch-enabled devices is a unique opportunity for visualization research to invent novel techniques to fluently explore, analyse, and understand complex and large-scale data. In this paper, we introduce Scribble Query, a novel interaction technique for fluid freehand scribbling (casual drawing) on touch-enabled devices to support interactive querying in data visualizations. Inspired by the low-entry yet rich interaction of touch drawing applications, a Scribble Query can be created with a single touch stroke yet have the expressiveness of multiple brushes (a conventionally used interaction technique). We have applied the Scribble Query interaction technique in a multivariate visualization tool, deployed the tool with domain experts from five different domains, and conducted deployment studies with these domain experts on their utilization of multivariate visualization with Scribble Query. The studies suggest that Scribble Query has a low entry barrier facilitating easy adoption, casual and infrequent usage, and in one case, enabled live dissemination of findings by the domain expert to managers in the organization.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Matthias","Elmqvist, Niklas","Grønbæk, Kaj"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-139118"],"event":{"end":"2016-12-02","place":"Launceston, au","start":"2016-11-29","title":"OzCHI '16 - the 28th Australian Conference on Computer-Human Interaction","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University System of Maryland"],"keyword":["Information visualization","Interaction techniques","Touch interaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scribble query fluid touch brushing for multivariate data visualization","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85012024610","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-139118","identifier":[{"id":"85012024610","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-10f8741e-dc85-4b06-a345-1fd3df8c004d"],"keyword":["Information visualization","Interaction techniques","Touch interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-94C08A6264CCB89DCE9499F2CF4BE05A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university system of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University System of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"790b96d1-cd52-41e3-84ae-cd5a795fb3dc","name":"Nielsen, Matthias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas","key":"elmqvistpau","last":"Elmqvist","name":"Elmqvist, Niklas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaj","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"c7b908c7-ad69-4b60-bfb2-f6d7f490bb4f","name":"Grønbæk, Kaj","orcid":"0000-0002-3752-6714","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3010915.3010951","eisbn":["9781450346184"],"pages":"381-390","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"OzCHI: Australian Conference on Human-Computer Interaction","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 28th Australian Computer-Human Interaction Conference, OzCHI 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85012024610"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-10f8741e-dc85-4b06-a345-1fd3df8c004d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Scribble query : fluid touch brushing for multivariate data visualization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-139118","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":8,"contributors":["Andersen, Sophie Esmann","Nielsen, Anne Ellerup","Høvring, Christiane Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-176127"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"communicative dilemmas of csr towards an integrative framework of csr communication","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-176127","ids":["au-52030ad9-6c18-49ba-8c94-c91422d21051"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C163F45F4F08F6E85C6F3230B3AFFEDB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management, Department of Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sophie Esmann","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"5b5a1388-f438-45a5-bdeb-6cd669f3693b","name":"Andersen, Sophie Esmann","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Ellerup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"607e3181-37dc-49b9-8c3e-e140cfa8359f","name":"Nielsen, Anne Ellerup","orcid":"0000-0002-1422-6663","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christiane Marie","key":"høvringpau","last":"Høvring","locid":"6641f8ce-f4c8-4c87-a0f4-7f9c5b4520c5","name":"Høvring, Christiane Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-6428-7982","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sandra","key":"diehlpedh","last":"Diehl","name":"Diehl, Sandra","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthias","key":"karmasinpedh","last":"Karmasin","name":"Karmasin, Matthias","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Barbara","key":"muellerpedh","last":"Mueller","name":"Mueller, Barbara","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ralf","key":"terlutterpedh","last":"Terlutter","name":"Terlutter, Ralf","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Franzisca","key":"wederpedh","last":"Weder","name":"Weder, Franzisca","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783319447001"],"isbn":["9783319446981"],"issn":["21967075"],"pages":"51-69","publisher":"Springer","series":"CSR, Sustainability, Ethics & Governance","status":"p","title":"Handbook of Integrated CSR Communication"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019072657"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-52030ad9-6c18-49ba-8c94-c91422d21051"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Communicative Dilemmas of CSR: Towards an Integrative Framework of CSR Communication","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-176127","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This work presents the first in vivo results of 2-D high frame rate vector velocity imaging for transthoracic cardiac imaging. Measurements are made on a healthy volunteer using the SARUS experimental ultrasound scanner connected to an intercostal phased-array probe. Two parasternal long-axis view (PLAX) are obtained, one centred at the aortic valve and another centred at the left ventricle. The acquisition sequence was composed of 3 diverging waves for high frame rate synthetic aperture flow imaging. For verification a phantom measurement is performed on a transverse straight 5 mm diameter vessel at a depth of 100 mm in a tissue-mimicking phantom. A flow pump produced a 2 ml/s constant flow with a peak velocity of 0.2 m/s. The average estimated flow anglein the ROI was 86.22◦ ± 6.66◦ with a true flow angle of 90◦. A relative velocity bias of −39% with a standard deviation of 13% was found. In-vivo acquisitions show complex flow patterns in the heart. In the aortic valve view, blood is seen exiting the left ventricle cavity through the aortic valve into the aorta during the systolic phase of the cardiac cycle. In the left ventricle view, blood flow is seen entering the left ventricle cavity through the mitral valve and splitting in two ways when approximating the left ventricle wall. The work presents 2-D velocity estimates on the heart from a non-invasive transthoracic scan. The ability of the method detecting flow regardless of the beam angle could potentially reveal a more complete view of the flow patterns presented on the heart.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Villagómez Hoyos, Carlos Armando","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Bechsgaard, Thor","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-372520"],"event":{"end":"2016-03-03","place":"San Diego, us","start":"2016-02-27","title":"SPIE Medical Imaging 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blood flow","Cardiac imaging","Medical ultrasound","Synthetic aperture","Vector flow imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high frame rate synthetic aperture vector flow imaging for transthoracic echocardiography","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/122015662/villagomez_hoyos_et_al.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-372520","identifier":[{"id":"84976510399","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e352c73d-1f24-4e3c-aaad-7a66397245b2"],"keyword":["Blood Flow","Cardiac Imaging","Medical Ultrasound","Synthetic Aperture","Vector Flow Imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-CC938441886824B10B22C5A4FE64E804"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/122015662/villagomez_hoyos_et_al.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.2216707","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carlos Armando","key":"villagómezhoyospau","last":"Villagómez Hoyos","locid":"dfb725c3-c502-44e8-80b9-ed3b63177248","name":"Villagómez Hoyos, Carlos Armando","orcid":"0000-0002-2157-5677","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thor","key":"bechsgaardpau","last":"Bechsgaard","name":"Bechsgaard, Thor","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Neb","key":"duricpedh","last":"Duric","name":"Duric, Neb","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brecht","key":"heydepedh","last":"Heyde","name":"Heyde, Brecht","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1117/12.2216707","publisher":"SPIE - International Society for Optical Engineering","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of SPIE","volume":"9790"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84976510399"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e352c73d-1f24-4e3c-aaad-7a66397245b2"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"High frame rate synthetic aperture vector flow imaging for transthoracic echocardiography.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-372520","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVR) has become an established therapeutic option for patients with symptomatic, severe aortic valve stenosis (AS) who are ineligible or at high risk for conventional valvular surgery. In Northwestern Europe, the TAVR technology is also increasingly used to treat patients with an intermediate risk profile. METHODS AND RESULTS: The study was designed as an independent Nordic multicenter registry of intermediate risk patients treated with the Lotus Valve System (Boston Scientific, MA, USA; N=154). Valve Academic Research Consortium (VARC)-defined device success was obtained in 97.4%. A Lotus Valve was successfully implanted in all patients. There was no valve migration, embolization, ectopic valve deployment, or TAV-in-TAV deployment. The VARC-defined combined safety rate at 30days was 92.2%, with a mortality rate of 1.9% and stroke rate of 3.2%. The clinical efficacy rate after 30days was 91.6% - only one patient had moderate aortic regurgitation. When considering only those patients in the late experience group (N=79), the combined safety and clinical efficacy rates were 93.7% and 92.4%, respectively. The pacemaker implantation rate was 27.9% - this rate was 12.8% in case of a combined implantation depth <4mm and a device/annulus ratio<1.05. CONCLUSIONS: The present study demonstrates the efficacy and safety of the repositionable, retrievable Lotus Valve System in intermediate risk patients with AS. The VARC-defined device success rate was 97.4% with a 30-day patient safety and clinical efficacy rate of more than 90%. Less than moderate aortic regurgitation was obtained in 99.4% of patients.","author_count":13,"contributors":["De Backer, Ole","Götberg, Matthias","Ihlberg, Leo","Packer, Erik","Savontaus, Mikko","Nielsen, Niels E","Jørgensen, Troels H","Nykänen, Antti","Baranowski, Jacek","Niemelä, Matti","Eskola, Markku","Bjursten, Henrik","Søndergaard, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-415225"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficacy and safety of the lotus valve system for treatment of patients with severe aortic valve stenosis and intermediate surgical risk results from the nordic lotus tavr registry","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-415225","identifier":[{"id":"84976564393","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27288972","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-248c5a72-1df7-4afe-90d3-85a22f382af2"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-96E8FE902B48C82BE160503AFF0BA0C5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Ole","key":"debackerpau","last":"De Backer","name":"De Backer, Ole","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthias","key":"götbergpau","last":"Götberg","name":"Götberg, Matthias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Leo","key":"ihlbergpau","last":"Ihlberg","name":"Ihlberg, Leo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik","key":"packerpau","last":"Packer","name":"Packer, Erik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mikko","key":"savontauspau","last":"Savontaus","name":"Savontaus, Mikko","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels E","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niels E","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Troels H","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Troels H","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Antti","key":"nykänenpau","last":"Nykänen","name":"Nykänen, Antti","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacek","key":"baranowskipau","last":"Baranowski","name":"Baranowski, Jacek","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matti","key":"niemeläpau","last":"Niemelä","name":"Niemelä, Matti","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Markku","key":"eskolapau","last":"Eskola","name":"Eskola, Markku","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"bjurstenpau","last":"Bjursten","name":"Bjursten, Henrik","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"6a064e1f-1f3e-480c-a5a2-53086732b169","name":"Søndergaard, Lars","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27288972"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijcard.2016.05.072","issn":["01675273","18741754"],"issn_org":["01675273"],"journal":"International Journal of Cardiology","pages":"92-97","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cardiology","volume":"219"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84976564393"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-248c5a72-1df7-4afe-90d3-85a22f382af2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Efficacy and safety of the Lotus Valve System for treatment of patients with severe aortic valve stenosis and intermediate surgical risk : Results from the Nordic Lotus-TAVR registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-415225","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background: Traffic noise has been associated with cardiovascular and metabolic disorders. Potential modes of action are through stress and sleep disturbance, which may lead to endocrine dysregulation and overweight. Objectives: We aimed to investigate the relationship between residential traffic and railway noise and adiposity. Methods: In this cross-sectional study of 57,053 middle-aged people, height, weight, waist circumference, and bioelectrical impedance were measured at enrollment (1993–1997). Body mass index (BMI), body fat mass index (BFMI), and lean body mass index (LBMI) were calculated. Residential exposure to road and railway traffic noise exposure was calculated using the Nordic prediction method. Associations between traffic noise and anthropometric measures at enrollment were analyzed using general linear models and logistic regression adjusted for demographic and lifestyle factors. Results: Linear regression models adjusted for age, sex, and socioeconomic factors showed that 5-year mean road traffic noise exposure preceding enrollment was associated with a 0.35-cm wider waist circumference (95% CI: 0.21, 0.50) and a 0.18-point higher BMI (95% CI: 0.12, 0.23) per 10 dB. Small, significant increases were also found for BFMI and LBMI. All associations followed linear exposure–response relationships. Exposure to railway noise was not linearly associated with adiposity measures. However, exposure > 60 dB was associated with a 0.71-cm wider waist circumference (95% CI: 0.23, 1.19) and a 0.19-point higher BMI (95% CI: 0.0072, 0.37) compared with unexposed participants (0–20 dB). Conclusions: The present study finds positive associations between residential exposure to road traffic and railway noise and adiposity.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Christensen, Jeppe S","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Tjønneland, Anne","Overvad, Kim","Nordsborg, Rikke B","Ketzel, Matthias","Sørensen, Thorkild I","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S03-098.75-001519"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Journal Article","Research Support Non U S Gov t"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"road traffic and railway noise exposures and adiposity in adults a cross sectional analysis of the danish diet cancer and health cohort","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/ehp.1409052","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.75-001519","identifier":[{"id":"84959294597","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000371442500019","type":"wos"},{"id":"26241990","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4786981","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-1e2c1825-2a30-4a6b-84bd-3464c04a215a","au-23e5e416-2140-4298-9e6c-3f11bbcb2dfe","ku-6d78b28f-6f6b-453b-8459-96cd9c4b1f42"],"keyword":["Journal Article","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-4111B0D86D62FC53CD571C2E225D0736"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4786981/pdf/ehp.1409052.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/ehp.1409052","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjertemedicin (Kardiologi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Human Genomics and Metagenomics in Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe S","key":"christensenjeppespau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jeppe S","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jeppe Schultz","key":"christensenjeppeschultzpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jeppe Schultz","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielseno