try":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hertelolepau","last":"Hertel","locid":"6a33f2b3-9140-4f59-a55e-e68a73c9fa32","name":"Hertel, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-0972-7735","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulas","key":"imulaspau","last":"Im","locid":"e2356d82-8e7b-49c9-b660-76e719a4058e","name":"Im, Ulas","orcid":"0000-0001-5177-5306","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne","key":"jensenannepau","last":"Jensen","locid":"0fb1f5a2-4301-429f-bad9-f0dc048ed310","name":"Jensen, Anne","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-8693","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Solvang","key":"jensensteensolvangpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"0d52f91a-4eaa-46f9-ab5f-d7fd3c31440d","name":"Jensen, Steen Solvang","orcid":"0000-0001-5923-8441","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelmatthiaspau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole-Kenneth","key":"nielsenolekennethpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"17ec76bb-7916-4024-867b-3aca60ca0c40","name":"Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","orcid":"0000-0003-4350-0956","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marlene Schmidt","key":"plejdrupmarleneschmidtpau","last":"Plejdrup","locid":"9dede80b-ff3e-4171-9504-bf8547fec74d","name":"Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"sigsgaardtorbenpau","last":"Sigsgaard","locid":"5d7f5dc8-00ea-48ba-9467-a93703b015b7","name":"Sigsgaard, Torben","orcid":"0000-0002-2043-7571","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelscamillapau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["13955241"],"issn_org":["16014146"],"issue":"1","journal":"Miljø og sundhed","pages":"25-33","status":"p","title":"Miljø og sundhed","volume":"22"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-31b34279-a7b9-496b-b0c0-0a7bb5deae34"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Helbredseffekter og eksterne omkostninger fra luftforurening i Danmark over 37 år (1979-2015)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-157760","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background Disease-modifying therapies (DMT) for multiple sclerosis (MS) has shown to reduce the risk of disability progression. However, injection therapy may not be preferred by patients because of injection-related problems and may negatively affect the therapeutic outcome. Low adherence to treatment in Multiple Sclerosis has shown to lead to poor health outcomes (ref. 1). Patients outcome could be greatly improved by the introduction of new orally administered agents, which may promote better adherence by avoiding injection- related problems (ref. 2) however few studies investigate adherence. Differences in treatment adherence to various disease modifying drugs in the treatment of MS are not well understood and the impact of treatment satisfaction, motivation and quality of life on treatment adherence is infrequently investigated. Lack of adherence or even treatment discontinuation may be a result of patient dissatisfaction with the treatment or low motivation to treatment. The unpredictable nature of relapses in RRMS may also lead to perceived lack of efficacy and decreased adherence. Objectives The objective of this study was to investigate adherence to fingolimod therapy and to evaluate to what extend treatment satisfaction, motivation and Quality of Life influence adherence in Danish patients with RRMS. Methods The study was conducted in Denmark from May 2013 to May 2016 at 8 out of 10 possible MS clinics. A total of 195 MS patients treated with fingolimod were included in the study over a period of 6 months (Table 1). All patients had received fingolimod treatment for at least 6-months prior to study inclusion. The patients were asked to bring all their study medication to the clinic at baseline and at 6 months post baseline. Adherence to fingolimod therapy was measured by pill count conducted by MS nurses (Table 2). The patients Quality of Life (QoL) was evaluated with the short form health survey (SF-12). Patient self-motivation was measured using the treatment self-regulation questionnaire (TSRQ). Physicians support to motivate the patient was measured by the Health Care Climate Questionnaire (HCCQ). All questionnaires were completed by the patients alone at a discrete place after instructions by the clinic personnel. The questioners were then filled and sealed by the patients in envelope and sent directly to data management. Results A high level of treatment adherence to fingolimod was initially calculated (103%). However, the study steering committee decided to limit patient compliance to maximum 100%. This meant that 25.7% of the patients had their adherence lowered to 100%. With a limit of 100% (individual adherence) the average adherence was calculated to 96% (Table 2). Background Disease-modifying therapies (DMT) for multiple sclerosis (MS) has shown to reduce the risk of disability progression. However, injection therapy may not be preferred by patients because of injection-related problems and may negatively affect the therapeutic outcome. Low adherence to treatment in Multiple Sclerosis has shown to lead to poor health outcomes (ref. 1). Patients outcome could be greatly improved by the introduction of new orally administered agents, which may promote better adherence by avoiding injection- related problems (ref. 2) however few studies investigate adherence. Differences in treatment adherence to various disease modifying drugs in the treatment of MS are not well understood and the impact of treatment satisfaction, motivation and quality of life on treatment adherence is infrequently investigated. Lack of adherence or even treatment discontinuation may be a result of patient dissatisfaction with the treatment or low motivation to treatment. The unpredictable nature of relapses in RRMS may also lead to perceived lack of efficacy and decreased adherence. Objectives The objective of this study was to investigate adherence to fingolimod therapy and to evaluate to what extend treatment satisfaction, motivation and Quality of Life influence adherence in Danish patients with RRMS. Methods The study was conducted in Denmark from May 2013 to May 2016 at 8 out of 10 possible MS clinics. A total of 195 MS patients treated with fingolimod were included in the study over a period of 6 months (Table 1). All patients had received fingolimod treatment for at least 6-months prior to study inclusion. The patients were asked to bring all their study medication to the clinic at baseline and at 6 months post baseline. Adherence to fingolimod therapy was measured by pill count conducted by MS nurses (Table 2). The patients Quality of Life (QoL) was evaluated with the short form health survey (SF-12). Patient self-motivation was measured using the treatment self-regulation questionnaire (TSRQ). Physicians support to motivate the patient was measured by the Health Care Climate Questionnaire (HCCQ). All questionnaires were completed by the patients alone at a discrete place after instructions by the clinic personnel. The questioners were then filled and sealed by the patients in envelope and sent directly to data management. Results A high level of treatment adherence to fingolimod was initially calculated (103%). However, the study steering committee decided to limit patient compliance to maximum 100%. This meant that 25.7% of the patients had their adherence lowered to 100%. With a limit of 100% (individual adherence) the average adherence was calculated to 96% (Table 2). Conclusions As most of the patients have a high adherence to fingolimod therapy it was not possible to elucidate a clear link between adherence and treatment satisfaction, QoL, or patient motivation","author_count":8,"contributors":["Schreiber, Karen","Kant, Matthias","Pfleger, Claudia","Jensen, Henrik Boye","Oesterberg, Ole","Hald, Anne Rieper","Nielsen, Frederik","Rubak, Sune Leisgaard Mørck"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-200060"],"event":{"end":"2016-10-29","place":"us","start":"2016-10-27","title":"Multiple Sclerosis Brain 2016 International Symposium","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a 000000000036 months danish multicenter open label study to investigate adherence treatment satisfaction motivation and quality of life in rrms patients treated with fingolimod","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-200060","ids":["au-7ba45db3-5b2d-409c-9c46-5c9b7f41db32"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D8C61B2A741F3D6A84901FCE65D1F7AC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics","Aarhus University, Health, HE Centre, HE Centre - Centre for Health Sciences Education"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"schreiberpau","last":"Schreiber","name":"Schreiber, Karen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"kantpau","last":"Kant","name":"Kant, Matthias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Claudia","key":"pflegerpau","last":"Pfleger","name":"Pfleger, Claudia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Boye","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Henrik Boye","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"oesterbergpau","last":"Oesterberg","name":"Oesterberg, Ole","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Rieper","key":"haldpau","last":"Hald","name":"Hald, Anne Rieper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Frederik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sune Leisgaard Mørck","key":"rubakpau","last":"Rubak","locid":"9ee438b5-e9a3-4877-9d93-9267f9d1ab22","name":"Rubak, Sune Leisgaard Mørck","orcid":"0000-0001-7010-2350","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7ba45db3-5b2d-409c-9c46-5c9b7f41db32"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A 36 months, Danish multicenter, open-label, study to investigate adherence, treatment satisfaction, motivation and quality of life in RRMS patients treated with fingolimod.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-200060","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Dennis Ulsøe","Lian, Zhong","Lindhardt, Anders Thyboe","Skrydstrup, Troels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-235350"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pd catalyzed carbonylative synthesis of other membered heterocycles from aryl halides","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-235350","ids":["au-b9b98e06-fe23-4d21-a37d-f2c09de8820a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-0D1F549857D63A438C13D497BACEE32D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Kemi, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Ulsøe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"9f5c8e9b-7797-40b6-909c-fb36601afd5d","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Ulsøe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhong","key":"lianpau","last":"Lian","locid":"d9c30296-e547-40c1-98a5-9d7e5f0121f3","name":"Lian, Zhong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Thyboe","key":"lindhardtpau","last":"Lindhardt","locid":"14a66f7a-665d-469e-81f7-df24b20795ea","name":"Lindhardt, Anders Thyboe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Troels","key":"skrydstruppau","last":"Skrydstrup","locid":"67f8ccf9-98a3-4760-a864-1d012fffc489","name":"Skrydstrup, Troels","orcid":"0000-0001-8090-5050","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao-Feng","key":"wupedh","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Xiao-Feng","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthias","key":"bellerpedh","last":"Beller","name":"Beller, Matthias","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783319249636"],"isbn":["9783319249612"],"pages":"89-99","publisher":"Springer","series":"Topics in Heterocyclic Chemistry","status":"p","subtitle":"Transition Metal Catalyzed Carbonylative Synthesis of Heterocycles","title":"Topics in Heterocyclic Chemistry","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b9b98e06-fe23-4d21-a37d-f2c09de8820a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pd-Catalyzed Carbonylative Synthesis of Other-Membered Heterocycles from Aryl Halides","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-235350","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Ruthenium PNP complex 1a (RuH(CO)Cl(HN(C2H4Pi-Pr2)2)) represents a state-of-the-art catalyst for low-temperature (<100 °C) aqueous methanol dehydrogenation to H2 and CO2. Herein, we describe an investigation that combines experiment, spectroscopy, and theory to provide a mechanistic rationale for this process. During catalysis, the presence of two anionic resting states was revealed, Ru–dihydride (3–) and Ru–monohydride (4–) that are deprotonated at nitrogen in the pincer ligand backbone. DFT calculations showed that O- and CH- coordination modes of methoxide to ruthenium compete, and form complexes 4– and 3–, respectively. Not only does the reaction rate increase with increasing KOH, but the ratio of 3–/4– increases, demonstrating that the “inner-sphere” C—H cleavage, via C—H coordination of methoxide to Ru, is promoted by base. Protonation of 3– liberates H2 gas and formaldehyde, the latter of which is rapidly consumed by KOH to give the corresponding gem-diolate and provides the overall driving force for the reaction. Full MeOH reforming is achieved through the corresponding steps that start from the gem-diolate and formate. Theoretical studies into the mechanism of the catalyst Me-1a (N-methylated 1a) revealed that C—H coordination to Ru sets-up C—H cleavage and hydride delivery; a process that is also promoted by base, as observed experimentally. However, in this case, Ru–dihydride Me-3 is much more stable to protonation and can even be observed under neutral conditions. The greater stability of Me-3 rationalizes the lower rates of Me-1a compared to 1a, and also explains why the reaction rate then drops with increasing KOH concentration.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Alberico, Elisabetta","Lennox, Alastair J. J.","Vogt, Lydia K.","Jiao, Haijun","Baumann, Wolfgang","Drexler, Hans-Joachim","Nielsen, Martin","Spannenberg, Anke","Checinski, Marek P.","Junge, Henrik","Beller, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-314347"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CreativeQuantum GmbH","University of Rostock"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unravelling the mechanism of basic aqueous methanol dehydrogenation catalyzed by ru pnp pincer complexes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84996774842","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-314347","identifier":[{"id":"27759392","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84996774842","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-20e7016a-8bfd-4d5a-8bf1-7680f7f1b1e9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F37DA4A8EFD7E3B08D973B65BA5E9516"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of rostock","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Rostock","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, Centre for Catalysis and Sustainable Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, Organic Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"creativequantum gmbh","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"CreativeQuantum GmbH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabetta","key":"albericopau","last":"Alberico","name":"Alberico, Elisabetta","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alastair J. J.","key":"lennoxpau","last":"Lennox","name":"Lennox, Alastair J. J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lydia K.","key":"vogtpau","last":"Vogt","name":"Vogt, Lydia K.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Haijun","key":"jiaopau","last":"Jiao","name":"Jiao, Haijun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wolfgang","key":"baumannpau","last":"Baumann","name":"Baumann, Wolfgang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans-Joachim","key":"drexlerpau","last":"Drexler","name":"Drexler, Hans-Joachim","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"9d6dc371-b9a6-4a82-8f8a-d1dc95332c6d","name":"Nielsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-3170-1198","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anke","key":"spannenbergpau","last":"Spannenberg","name":"Spannenberg, Anke","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marek P.","key":"checinskipau","last":"Checinski","name":"Checinski, Marek P.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"jungepau","last":"Junge","name":"Junge, Henrik","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"bellerpau","last":"Beller","name":"Beller, Matthias","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27759392"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/jacs.6b05692","issn":["00027863","15205126"],"issn_org":["00027863"],"issue":"45","journal":"Journal of the American Chemical Society","pages":"14890-14904","publisher":"ACS Publications","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Chemical Society","title_org":"American Chemical Society. Journal","volume":"138"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84996774842"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-20e7016a-8bfd-4d5a-8bf1-7680f7f1b1e9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Unravelling The Mechanism of Basic Aqueous Methanol Dehydrogenation Catalyzed By Ru-PNP Pincer Complexes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-314347","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The development of vaccines against porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus (PRRSV) has been hampered by the high mutation rate and the multiple immunoevasive strategies of the virus. With the overall aim of designing a broad coverage vaccine that induces an effective CTL response against PRRSV, we have used a bioinformatics approach to identify common PRRSV type 2 epitopes predicted to react broadly with predominant swine MHC (SLA) alleles. All possible 9- and 10-mer peptides derived from 104 wild-type strains were analyzed in silico for their predicted binding affinity to 3 common SLA class I alleles and ranked according to genomic conservation and SLA binding coverage. Of the 53 top-ranked peptides, 33 were verified in vitro as high affinity binders. Polyepitope gene cassettes of these peptides, flanked by an upstream ubiquitin sequence and a downstream FLAG tag, were cloned into a classical swine fever virus (CSFV)-derived replicon vector. Virus replicon particles (VRP) were rescued by transfection of a complementing cell line with replicon RNA. Polyepitope expression and subsequent proteasomal degradation was confirmed indirectly by increased FLAG-tagged protein detection in the presence of a proteasome inhibitor. Finally, a vaccination-challenge experiment using 18 SLA-matched pigs is currently being conducted until July 2016 in which a test group and a control group are being vaccinated twice with VRPs expressing PRRSV epitopes and non-sense control epitopes, respectively, before challenged with live wild type PRRSV. The induced epitope specific cell-mediated immune responses are being monitored by ELISPOT, flow cytometry and cytotoxicity assays, and the degree of protection against infection will be characterized by qPCR and antibody analysis. The results will be available for IVIS. This study exemplifies how bioinformatics epitope prediction, recombinant SLA molecules and RNA virus replicon design can be used to engineer a replicating non-propagating vaccine tailored to deliver conserved and immunogenic CTL epitopes.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Welner, Simon","Werder, Simea","Nielsen, Morten","Lund, Ole","Gerber, Markus","Liniger, Matthias","Ruggli, Nicolas","Summerfield, Artur","Larsen, Lars Erik","Jungersen, Gregers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-341105"],"event":{"end":"2016-08-19","place":"Gold Coast, au","start":"2016-08-16","title":"11th International Veterinary Immunology Symposium","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institute of Virology and Immunoprophylaxis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"engineering a ctl tailored replicon rna vaccine against prrsv","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/127760136/Welner_et_al_IVIS_Abstract.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-341105","ids":["dtu-7a6c15e6-2659-4062-a69f-6b90ead6e591"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AC7969CF21C5AF6D5DD6F9560BF3E10F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/127760136/Welner_et_al_IVIS_Abstract.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"institute of virology and immunoprophylaxis","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Institute of Virology and Immunoprophylaxis","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon","key":"welnerpau","last":"Welner","locid":"82d69bec-9930-4587-86c5-e240ee2e4b11","name":"Welner, Simon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Simea","key":"werderpau","last":"Werder","name":"Werder, Simea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"70ba2d95-32b6-4c85-a05e-dfe3788bef7a","name":"Nielsen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-7885-4311","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"d2f5060c-0c9a-4875-820f-91180f3bb685","name":"Lund, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-1108-0491","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Markus","key":"gerberpau","last":"Gerber","name":"Gerber, Markus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"linigerpau","last":"Liniger","name":"Liniger, Matthias","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolas","key":"rugglipau","last":"Ruggli","name":"Ruggli, Nicolas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Artur","key":"summerfieldpau","last":"Summerfield","name":"Summerfield, Artur","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregers","key":"jungersenpau","last":"Jungersen","locid":"0ab77d4d-9a55-428c-9876-4a857d7e80f2","name":"Jungersen, Gregers","orcid":"0000-0003-3147-6960","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7a6c15e6-2659-4062-a69f-6b90ead6e591"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Engineering a CTL-Tailored Replicon RNA Vaccine against PRRSV","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-341105","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"We here describe a multimodality neuroimaging containing data from healthy volunteers and patients, acquired within the Lundbeck Foundation Center for Integrated Molecular Brain Imaging (Cimbi) in Copenhagen, Denmark. The data is of particular relevance for neurobiological research questions related to the serotonergic transmitter system with its normative data on the serotonergic subtype receptors 5-HT1A, 5-HT1B, 5-HT2A, and 5-HT4 and the 5-HT transporter (5-HTT), but can easily serve other purposes. The Cimbi database and Cimbi biobank were formally established in 2008 with the purpose to store the wealth of Cimbi-acquired data in a highly structured and standardized manner in accordance with the regulations issued by the Danish Data Protection Agency as well as to provide a quality-controlled resource for future hypothesis-generating and hypothesis-driven studies. The Cimbi database currently comprises a total of 1100 PET and 1000 structural and functional MRI scans and it holds a multitude of additional data, such as genetic and biochemical data, and scores from 17 self-reported questionnaires and from 11 neuropsychological paper/computer tests. The database associated Cimbi biobank currently contains blood and in some instances saliva samples from about 500 healthy volunteers and 300 patients with e.g., major depression, dementia, substance abuse, obesity, and impulsive aggression. Data continue to be added to the Cimbi database and biobank.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Knudsen, Gitte M.","Jensen, Peter S.","Erritzoe, David","Baaré, William F. C.","Ettrup, Anders","Fisher, Patrick M.","Gillings, Nic","Hansen, Hanne D.","Hansen, Lars Kai","Hasselbalch, Steen G","Henningsson, Susanne","Herth, Matthias M","Holst, Klaus K","Iversen, Pernille","Kessing, Lars V","Macoveanu, Julian","Madsen, Kathrine Skak","Mortensen, Erik L","Nielsen, Finn Årup","Paulson, Olaf B.","Siebner, Hartwig R.","Stenbæk, Dea S.","Svarer, Claus","Jernigan, Terry L.","Strother, Stephen C.","Frokjaer, Vibe G."],"cuid":["S02-094.44-037312"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Rotman Research Institute","University of California at San Diego"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the center for integrated molecular brain imaging cimbi database","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2015.04.025","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-094.44-037312","identifier":[{"id":"25891375","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84949323508","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d109702c-f124-41c9-84d2-2908941fe0b0","ku-a759ed49-2de2-49ee-8085-738ddf0ca853"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9670AA28E1F6206C0E709AAE81EA3808"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/118648465/1_s2.0_S1053811915003158_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2015.04.025","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"