{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Exposure to road traffic noise has been associated with adiposity and diabetes in adults. The suggested pathways have been through sleep disturbance and stress. Children may be particularly susceptible to noise induced sleep disturbance and stress and the effects hereof. OBJECTIVES: To examine the association between traffic noise exposure during pregnancy and early childhood and adiposity in children. METHODS: We identified 40,974 singletons from the Danish National Birth Cohort with parentally given questionnaire information on weight and height at 7-years of age. Road and railway traffic noise were modeled at all historical addresses and expressed as time-weighted means for two exposure periods (pregnancy and childhood). Adiposity was assessed using BMI z-scores and a dichotomous measure of childhood overweight based on age and sex specific cut-offs. Associations were analyzed using linear regression for BMI z-scores and logistic regression for risk of childhood overweight, adjusting for socioeconomic position, maternal BMI, maternal smoking, maternal age, parity and degree of urbanization. RESULTS: We found both pregnancy and childhood exposure to road traffic noise to be associated with a higher risk for childhood overweight (odds ratio (OR)=1.06 per 10dB, 95% confidence interval (CI): 1.00-1.12 for exposure during pregnancy and OR=1.06 per 10dB, 95% CI: 0.99-1.12 for childhood exposure). There were no associations between road traffic noise and BMI z-scores. We found no associations between railway noise and adiposity. CONCLUSIONS: We found suggestions of a positive association between road traffic noise and risk of overweight in 7-years old children.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christensen, Jeppe Schultz","Hjortebjerg, Dorrit","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Ketzel, Matthias","Sørensen, Thorkild I A","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-094.01-017849"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adolescence","BMI","Overweight","Traffic noise"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pregnancy and childhood exposure to residential traffic noise and overweight at 000000000007years of age","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84971673156","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.01-017849","identifier":[{"id":"27258658","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000382339000019","type":"wos"},{"id":"84971673156","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-4750f165-b0e8-4fb8-a694-7b6c32d165e8","ku-2dcda4ac-67b2-482e-b897-2238846faa2c"],"keyword":["Adolescence","BMI","Overweight","Traffic noise"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DF76C47F7F7B9EC8313CA14A34A0549B"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Human Genomics and Metagenomics in Metabolism","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe Schultz","key":"christensenjeppeschultzpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jeppe Schultz","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorrit","key":"hjortebjergdorritpau","last":"Hjortebjerg","name":"Hjortebjerg, Dorrit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenolepau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelmatthiaspau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thorkild I. A.","key":"sørensenthorkildiapau","last":"Sorensen","locid":"2cb8cf47-6b6b-4010-bdf6-9ec77c7deed3","name":"Sørensen, Thorkild I A","name_org":"Sorensen, Thorkild I. A.","orcid":"0000-0003-4821-430X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"sørensenmettepau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27258658"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envint.2016.05.016","issn":["01604120","18736750"],"issn_org":["01604120"],"journal":"Environment International","pages":"170-176","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Environment International","volume":"94"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84971673156"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4750f165-b0e8-4fb8-a694-7b6c32d165e8","ku-2dcda4ac-67b2-482e-b897-2238846faa2c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pregnancy and childhood exposure to residential traffic noise and overweight at 7years of age","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.01-017849","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: Exposure to traffic noise has been associated with adverse effects on neuropsychological outcomes in children, but findings with regard to behavioral problems are inconsistent. Objective: We investigated whether residential road traffic noise exposure is associated with behavioral problems in 7-year-old children. Methods: We identified 46,940 children from the Danish National Birth Cohort with complete information on behavioral problems at 7 years of age and complete address history from conception to 7 years of age. Road traffic noise (L den) was modeled at all present and historical addresses. Behavioral problems were assessed by the parent-reported Strengths and Difficulties Questionnaire (SDQ). Associations between pregnancy and childhood exposure to noise and behavioral problems were analyzed by multinomial or logistic regression and adjusted for potential confounders. Results: A 10-dB increase in average time-weighted road traffic noise exposure from birth to 7 years of age was associated with a 7% increase (95% CI: 1.00, 1.14) in abnormal versus normal total difficulties scores; 5% (95% CI: 1.00, 1.10) and 9% (95% CI: 1.03, 1.18) increases in borderline and abnormal hyperactivity/inattention subscale scores, respectively; and 5% (95% CI: 0.98, 1.14) and 6% (95% CI: 0.99, 1.12) increases in abnormal conduct problem and peer relationship problem subscale scores, respectively. Exposure to road traffic noise during pregnancy was not associated with child behavioral problems at 7 years of age. Conclusions: Residential road traffic noise in early childhood may be associated with behavioral problems, particularly hyperactivity/inattention symptoms.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hjortebjerg, Dorrit Irene","Andersen, Anne-Marie Nybo","Schultz Christensen, Jeppe","Ketzel, Matthias","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Sunyer, Jordi","Julvez, Jordi","Forns, Joan","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-094.44-028237"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian Institute of Public Health"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exposure to road traffic noise and behavioral problems in 000000000007 year old children a cohort study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/ehp.1409430","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.44-028237","identifier":[{"id":"26126294","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4749080","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84956667069","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d6d2a65c-030c-4d3a-9eb3-cb388d47563f","ku-a73569d0-39e1-4511-8226-1acbe2e0303d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E75235BD8ECA08688458A1189C41DC55"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/ehp.1409430","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"no","key":"norwegian institute of public health","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian Institute of Public Health","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorrit Irene","key":"hjortebjergpau","last":"Hjortebjerg","name":"Hjortebjerg, Dorrit Irene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne-Marie","key":"nyboandersenpau","last":"Nybo Andersen","locid":"249beb4b-1fec-4854-b57d-d2bf355767db","name":"Andersen, Anne-Marie Nybo","name_org":"Nybo Andersen, Anne-Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4296-8488","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe","key":"schultzchristensenpau","last":"Schultz Christensen","name":"Schultz Christensen, Jeppe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jeppe Schultz","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jeppe Schultz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jordi","key":"sunyerpau","last":"Sunyer","name":"Sunyer, Jordi","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jordi","key":"julvezpau","last":"Julvez","name":"Julvez, Jordi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Joan","key":"fornspau","last":"Forns","name":"Forns, Joan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26126294"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1289/ehp.1409430","issn":["00916765","15529924"],"issn_org":["00916765"],"issue":"2","journal":"Environmental Health Perspectives","pages":"1-33","publisher":"Public Health Services, US Dept of Health and Human Services","status":"p","title":"Environmental Health Perspectives","volume":"124"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84956667069"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d6d2a65c-030c-4d3a-9eb3-cb388d47563f","ku-a73569d0-39e1-4511-8226-1acbe2e0303d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exposure to Road Traffic Noise and Behavioral Problems in 7-Year-Old Children: A Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.44-028237","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a novel approach for estimating 2-D flow angles using a high-frame-rate ultrasound method. The angle estimator features high accuracy and low standard deviation (SD) over the full 360° range. The method is validated on Field II simulations and phantom measurements using the experimental ultrasound scanner SARUS and a flow rig before being tested in vivo. An 8-MHz linear array transducer is used with defocused beam emissions. In the simulations of a spinning disk phantom, a 360° uniform behavior on the angle estimation is observed with a median angle bias of 1.01° and a median angle SD of 1.8°. Similar results are obtained on a straight vessel for both simulations and measurements, where the obtained angle biases are below 1.5° with SDs around 1°. Estimated velocity magnitudes are also kept under 10% bias and 5% relative SD in both simulations and measurements. An in vivo measurement is performed on a carotid bifurcation of a healthy individual. A 3-s acquisition during three heart cycles is captured. A consistent and repetitive vortex is observed in the carotid bulb during systoles.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Villagómez Hoyos, Carlos Armando","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Lindskov Hansen, Kristoffer","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S02-095.19-034629"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Blood flow","Journal Article","Medical ultrasound","Synthetic aperture","Vector flow imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accurate angle estimator for high frame rate 000000000002 d vector flow imaging","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84973333174","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.19-034629","identifier":[{"id":"84973333174","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27093598","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-59d7f593-f749-4aba-8d60-9b4ff163b522","ku-214c054e-5dbe-4612-824b-0f793187bfcc"],"keyword":["Angle estimator","Blood flow","Journal Article","Medical ultrasound","Synthetic aperture","Vector Flow Imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8DFDEFBF50CE245972D23F4F81B8E8BB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carlos Armando","key":"villagómezhoyospau","last":"Villagómez Hoyos","locid":"dfb725c3-c502-44e8-80b9-ed3b63177248","name":"Villagómez Hoyos, Carlos Armando","orcid":"0000-0002-2157-5677","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carlos Armando","key":"villagomezhoyospau","last":"Villagomez Hoyos","name":"Villagomez Hoyos, Carlos Armando","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristoffer","key":"lindskovhansenpau","last":"Lindskov Hansen","name":"Lindskov Hansen, Kristoffer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristoffer Lindskov","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27093598"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tuffc.2016.2551689","issn":["08853010","15258955"],"issn_org":["08853010"],"issue":"6","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics and Frequency Control","pages":"842-853","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics and Frequency Control","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics and Frequency Control","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2