aspedh","last":"Heymann","name":"Heymann, Matthias","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","eisbn":["9781137596888"],"isbn":["9781137596871"],"pages":"195-216","place":"New York","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","subtitle":"Cold War Science and Technology on Ice","title":"Exploring Greenland"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-69ebfedb-9972-4987-b505-78e1b1366e4f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Camp Century - Cold War City Under the Ice","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-189795","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Air pollution causes lung cancer, but associations with other cancers have not been established. We investigated whether long-term exposure to traffic-related air pollution is associated with the risk of the general population for leukaemia. We identified 1,967 people in whom leukaemia was diagnosed in 1992-2010 from a nation-wide cancer registry and selected 3,381 control people at random, matched on sex and year of birth, from the entire Danish population. Residential addresses since 1971 were traced in a population registry, and outdoor concentrations of NOx and NO2, as indicators of traffic-related air pollution, were calculated at each address in a dispersion model. We used conditional logistic regression to estimate the risk for leukaemia after adjustment for income, educational level, cohabitation status and co-morbidity. In linear analyses, we found odds ratios for acute myeloid leukaemia of 1.20 (95% confidence interval: 1.04-1.38) per 20 μg/m3 increase in NOx and 1.31 (1.02-1.68) per 10 μg/m3 increase in NO2, calculated as time-weighted average exposure at all addresses since 1971. We found no association with chronic myeloid or lymphocytic leukaemia. This study indicates an association between long-term exposure to traffic-related air pollution and acute myeloid leukaemia in the general population, but not for other subtypes of leukaemia.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Ketzel, Matthias","Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-214787"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"keyword":["Acute myeloid leukaemia","Air pollution","Benzene","Leukaemia","Traffic"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"traffic related air pollution and risk for leukaemia of an adult population","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84955672603","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-214787","identifier":[{"id":"84955672603","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26415047","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-95f5ebe2-db3e-462f-b7e7-aba72a4081c8"],"keyword":["Acute myeloid leukaemia","Air pollution","Benzene","Leukaemia","Traffic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-932C216EA4603EEF90736DC52684C5E8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26415047"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ijc.29867","issn":["00207136"],"issue":"5","journal":"International Journal of Cancer","pages":"1111-1117","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cancer","volume":"138"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84955672603"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-95f5ebe2-db3e-462f-b7e7-aba72a4081c8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Traffic-related air pollution and risk for leukaemia of an adult population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-214787","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: Very little is currently known about air pollutants’ adverse effects on neurodegenerative diseases even though recent studies have linked particulate exposures to brain pathologies associated with Parkinson’s and Alzheimer’s disease. Objective: In the present study, we investigated long-term exposure to traffic-related air pollution and Parkinson’s disease. Methods: In a case–control study of 1,696 Parkinson’s disease (PD) patients identified from Danish hospital registries and diagnosed 1996–2009 and 1,800 population controls matched by sex and year of birth, we assessed long-term traffic-related air pollutant exposures (represented by nitrogen dioxide; NO 2) from a dispersion model, using residential addresses from 1971 to the date of diagnosis or first cardinal symptom for cases and the corresponding index date for their matched controls. Odds ratios (ORs) and 95% confidence intervals (CIs) were estimated with logistic regression, adjusting for matching factors and potential confounders. Results: We found ambient air pollution from traffic sources to be associated with risk of PD, with a 9% higher risk (95% CI: 3, 16.0%) per interquartile range increase (2.97 μg/m3) in modeled NO 2. For participants living for ≥ 20 years in the capital city, ORs were larger (OR = 1.21; 95% CI: 1.11, 1.31) than in provincial towns (OR = 1.10; 95% CI: 0.97, 1.26), whereas there was no association among rural residents. Conclusions: Our findings raise concerns about potential effects of air pollution from traffic and other sources on the risk of PD, particularly in populations with high or increasing exposures.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ritz, Beate","Lee, Pei-Chen","Hansen, Johnni","Funch Lassen, Christina","Ketzel, Matthias","Sørensen, Mette","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-218561"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Taiwan","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Taipei University of Nursing and Health Sciences","University of California at Los Angeles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"traffic related air pollution and parkinson s disease in denmark a case control study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84959264593","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-218561","identifier":[{"id":"26151951","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4786985","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84959264593","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9cabb38a-6d7c-4433-bf45-f553a5e19686"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-95CE1AF03BCC3C1A8F2E38603AB1054D"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of california at los angeles","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Los Angeles","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"tw","key":"national taipei university of nursing and health sciences","loc":["Taiwan","Asia, East"],"name":"National Taipei University of Nursing and Health Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Beate","key":"ritzpau","last":"Ritz","name":"Ritz, Beate","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pei-Chen","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Pei-Chen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Johnni","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Johnni","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"funchlassenpau","last":"Funch Lassen","name":"Funch Lassen, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26151951"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1289/ehp.1409313","issn":["00916765","15529924"],"issn_org":["00916765"],"issue":"3","journal":"Environmental Health Perspectives","pages":"351-356","publisher":"Public Health Services, US Dept of Health and Human Services","status":"p","title":"Environmental Health Perspectives","volume":"124"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84959264593"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9cabb38a-6d7c-4433-bf45-f553a5e19686"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Traffic-Related Air Pollution and Parkinson's Disease in Denmark : A Case-Control Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-218561","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Air pollution is an established lung carcinogen, and there is increasing evidence that air pollution also negatively affects the brain. We have previously reported an association between air pollution and risk of brain tumors in a cohort study based on only 95 cases. We set out to replicate that finding in a large nationwide case–control study. Methods: We identified all 4,183 adult brain tumor cases in Denmark in the years 2000–2009 and 8,018 risk set sampled population controls matched on gender and year of birth. We extracted residential address histories and estimated mean residential nitrogen oxides (NO x) concentrations since 1971 with a validated dispersion model. Categorical and linear odds ratios (OR) and confidence intervals (CI) were calculated with conditional logistic regression models. Results: The highest risk estimates for any brain cancer were observed among subjects with the highest average exposure levels (80–99 µg/m 3: OR 1.27, 95 % CI 0.82–1.96; ≥100 µg/m 3: 1.40, 95 % CI 0.87–2.26 as compared to <20 µg/m 3 NO x), but there was no increased OR at NO x levels below 80 µg/m 3 and when modeled linearly there was no significant association with risk of brain cancer (OR 1.11, 95 % CI 0.84–1.46 per 100 µg/m 3 NO x). In sub-analysis the OR associated with exposures ≥100 µg/m 3 was 2.30 (95 % CI 1.15–4.59) for non-glioma and 0.89 (95 % CI 0.44–1.77) for glioma. Conclusions: This study did not support the relatively strong linear association between air pollution and risk of brain tumors which was found in our previous study. The suggestion of an increased brain tumor risk at high exposures merits further attention as does the differing results according to tumor morphology.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Sørensen, Mette","Andersen, Zorana J","Ketzel, Matthias","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-099.29-021966"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Air pollution","Brain cancer","Epidemiology","Nitrous oxides"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"air pollution from traffic and risk for brain tumors a nationwide study in denmark","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84961247874","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.29-021966","identifier":[{"id":"26892605","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84961247874","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7f7bc813-e797-425f-9ea2-5f5ef2c43002","ku-5ef8b562-22e3-4899-84e7-08d702b64a02"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Brain cancer","Epidemiology","Nitrous oxides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3C57424853909216FD17A0211AB0E325"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Center of Epidemiology and Screening"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"7b6bb5c8-8f2f-4e42-b828-038fa5128e7c","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zorana J.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8bffc514-d71e-40ba-b979-910dfb03ec5e","name":"Andersen, Zorana Jovanovic","name_org":"Andersen, Zorana J.","orcid":"0000-0003-4138-9828","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26892605"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10552-016-0721-x","issn":["09575243","15737225"],"issn_org":["09575243"],"issue":"4","journal":"Cancer Causes & Control","pages":"473-480","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Cancer Causes & Control","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961247874"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7f7bc813-e797-425f-9ea2-5f5ef2c43002","ku-5ef8b562-22e3-4899-84e7-08d702b64a02"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Air pollution from traffic and risk for brain tumors : a nationwide study in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.29-021966","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"A method for vector velocity volume flow estimation is presented, along with an investigation of its sources of error and correction of actual volume flow measurements. Volume flow errors are quantified theoretically by numerical modeling, through flow phantom measurements, and studied in vivo. This paper investigates errors from estimating volumetric flow using a commercial ultrasound scanner and the common assumptions made in the literature. The theoretical model shows, e.g. that volume flow is underestimated by 15%, when the scan plane is off-axis with the vessel center by 28% of the vessel radius. The error sources were also studied in vivo under realistic clinical conditions, and the theoretical results were applied for correcting the volume flow errors. Twenty dialysis patients with arteriovenous fistulas were scanned to obtain vector flow maps of fistulas. When fitting an ellipsis to cross-sectional scans of the fistulas, the major axis was on average 10.2 mm, which is 8.6% larger than the minor axis. The ultrasound beam was on average 1.5 mm from the vessel center, corresponding to 28% of the semi-major axis in an average fistula. Estimating volume flow with an elliptical, rather than circular, vessel area and correcting the ultrasound beam for being off-axis, gave a significant (p = 0.008) reduction in error from 31.2% to 24.3%. The error is relative to the Ultrasound Dilution Technique, which is considered the gold standard for volume flow estimation for dialysis patients. The study shows the importance of correcting for volume flow errors, which are often made in clinical practice.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jensen, Jonas","Olesen, Jacob Bjerring","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Hansen, Peter Møller","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S02-099.67-036582"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Arteriovenous fistula","Error sources","Journal Article","Transverse oscillation","Volume flow"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vector velocity volume flow estimation sources of error and corrections applied for arteriovenous fistulas","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84965010996","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.67-036582","identifier":[{"id":"84965010996","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27164045","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-b00af986-819f-44a0-90ac-906b205cbcef","ku-b1fa534c-83ec-42ad-ac45-5b4bc022be9a"],"keyword":["Arteriovenous fistula","Error sources","Journal Article","Transverse oscillation","Volume flow"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-906E13B975362EF0DBA5FBDB95489290"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"jensenjonaspau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ce6e719b-4e0f-4795-a9ac-91265cc918a8","name":"Jensen, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0003-4456-0838","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Bjerring","key":"olesenjacobbjerringpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"024aaa55-d5a4-4763-8004-b2fb701dfd2b","name":"Olesen, Jacob Bjerring","orcid":"0000-0002-5169-1644","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartmatthiasbopau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Møller","key":"hansenpetermøllerpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Peter Møller","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenmichaelbachmannpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenjørgenarendtpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27164045"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ultras.2016.04.023","issn":["0041624X","18749968"],"issn_org":["0041624X"],"journal":"Ultrasonics","pages":"136-146","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Ultrasonics","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84965010996"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b00af986-819f-44a0-90ac-906b205cbcef","ku-b1fa534c-83ec-42ad-ac45-5b4bc022be9a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Vector velocity volume flow estimation: Sources of error and corrections applied for arteriovenous fistulas","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.67-036582","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG) is the standard treatment for revascularisation in patients with left main coronary artery disease, but use of percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) for this indication is increasing. We aimed to compare PCI and CABG for treatment of left main coronary artery disease. METHODS: In this prospective, randomised, open-label, non-inferiority trial, patients with left main coronary artery disease were enrolled in 36 centres in northern Europe and randomised 1:1 to treatment with PCI or CABG. Eligible patients had stable angina pectoris, unstable angina pectoris, or non-ST-elevation myocardial infarction. Exclusion criteria were ST-elevation myocardial infarction within 24 h, being considered too high risk for CABG or PCI, or expected survival of less than 1 year. The primary endpoint was major adverse cardiac or cerebrovascular events (MACCE), a composite of all-cause mortality, non-procedural myocardial infarction, any repeat coronary revascularisation, and stroke. Non-inferiority of PCI to CABG required the lower end of the 95% CI not to exceed a hazard ratio (HR) of 1·35 after up to 5 years of follow-up. The intention-to-treat principle was used in the analysis if not specified otherwise. This trial is registered with ClinicalTrials.gov identifier, number NCT01496651. FINDINGS: Between Dec 9, 2008, and Jan 21, 2015, 1201 patients were randomly assigned, 598 to PCI and 603 to CABG, and 592 in each group entered analysis by intention to treat. Kaplan-Meier 5 year estimates of MACCE were 29% for PCI (121 events) and 19% for CABG (81 events), HR 1·48 (95% CI 1·11-1·96), exceeding the limit for non-inferiority, and CABG was significantly better than PCI (p=0·0066). As-treated estimates were 28% versus 19% (1·55, 1·18-2·04, p=0·0015). Comparing PCI with CABG, 5 year estimates were 12% versus 9% (1·07, 0·67-1·72, p=0·77) for all-cause mortality, 7% versus 2% (2·88, 1·40-5·90, p=0·0040) for non-procedural myocardial infarction, 16% versus 10% (1·50, 1·04-2·17, p=0·032) for any revascularisation, and 5% versus 2% (2·25, 0·93-5·48, p=0·073) for stroke. INTERPRETATION: The findings of this study suggest that CABG might be better than PCI for treatment of left main stem coronary artery disease. FUNDING: Biosensors, Aarhus University Hospital, and participating sites.","author_count":45,"contributors":["Mäkikallio, Timo","Holm, Niels Ramsing","Lindsay, Mitchell","Spence, Mark S","Erglis, Andrejs","Menown, Ian B A","Trovik, Thor","Eskola, Markku","Romppanen, Hannu","Kellerth, Thomas","Ravkilde, Jan","Jensen, Lisette O","Kalinauskas, Gintaras","Linder, Rikard B A","Pentikainen, Markku","Hervold, Anders","Banning, Adrian","Zaman, Azfar","Cotton, Jamen","Eriksen, Erlend","Margus, Sulev","Sørensen, Henrik T","Nielsen, Per Hostrup","Niemelä, Matti","Kervinen, Kari","Lassen, Jens F","Maeng, Michael","Oldroyd, Keith","Berg, Geoff","Walsh, Simon J","Hanratty, Colm G","Kumsars, Indulis","Stradins, Peteris","Steigen, Terje K","Fröbert, Ole","Graham, Alastair N J","Endresen, Petter C","Corbascio, Matthias","Kajander, Olli","Trivedi, Uday","Hartikainen, Juha","Anttila, Vesa","Hildick-Smith, David","Thuesen, Leif","Christiansen, Evald Høj"],"cuid":["S02-099.72-011691"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["NOBLE study investigators"],"country":["Estonia","Finland","Latvia","Lithuania","Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brighton and Sussex University Hospitals NHS Trust","East Tallinn Central Hospital","Golden Jubilee National Hospital","Helsinki University Central Hospital","Karolinska Institutet","Karolinska University Hospital","Kuopio University Hospital","Newcastle upon Tyne Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Riga Stradins University","Tampere University","UiT The Arctic University of Norway","Univ