volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84952636777"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a3e8ab4d-3b7a-407b-8cac-c9e01eaefb8c","sdu-972429ea-5786-4144-8770-53a5e547cf25"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"MFAP4 Promotes Vascular Smooth Muscle Migration, Proliferation and Accelerates Neointima Formation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-024672","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Introduction In terms of effects on mortality fine particulate matter (PM2.5) is considered the most important component of air polllution. Several international studies have investigated the effect size. It is estimated that overall mortality increases 6% per 10µg/m3 increase in annual PM2.5 and that PM2.5 affects global mortality signficantly (Hoek, 2013). The first attempt to describe the size of the effects of PM2.5 in Denmark were published in 2002 (Raaschou-Nielsen, 2002). At that time only PM10 data were available and only with a great deal of uncertainty. Since then the knowledge of PM2.5 concentration and distribution in Denmark (and elsewhere) has increased tremendously and new calculations of its’ health effects have been reported. Since 2002 not only the air pollution data and the models have changed, so has the demography of the population and the baseline mortality rates. It is not clear to what extent the changes in estimates of mortality from PM2.5 exposure over the years is due to changes in population and in pollution and to what extent they are due to improved models. Methods Several methods of calculation were compared for the year 2012. First the method used in 2002 in which the annual mean in PM10 in different areas of Denmark was estimated by expert judgments and then multiplied by a relative risk of 1.043/10 µg/m3 of PM10 and the mortality rate. Second a model system integrating chemistry transport, urban background models, and population density in a 1 x 1 km grid (the EVA model) was applied using a relative risk of 1.06/10 µg/m3 of PM2.5. Third, a life table analysis using the age distribution of the population in Denmark in 2012 and the average PM2.5 exposure of the entire population and the relative risk from the EVA model. Fourth, the life table analysis was repeated with the same data but under the assumption of a log-linear relationship between PM2.5 and mortality rather than a linear relationship. Annual urban background PM10 in Copenhagen changed from 25 µg/m3 in 2002 to 17 in 2012. In 2012 PM2.5 was 11 µg/m3 at the Copenhagen urban background and 15 µg/m3 at the Copenhagen street level (http://envs.au.dk/en/knowledge/air/monitoring/). Results from the different methods of calculation of effects on mortality will be presented and discussed. Conclusions Estimation of health effects from long term PM exposure has developed tremendously over the past decade. Rigouros comparisons of how these different methods perform has rarely been done. This study compare methods using Denmark as an example, and gives an update on mortality caused by fine particulate matter air pollution. This work was funded by the DCE – National Centre for Environment and Energy project ”Health impacts and external costs from air pollution in Denmark over 25 years” and by NordForsk under the Nordic Programme on Health and Welfare project “Understanding the link between air pollution and distribution of related health impacts and welfare in the Nordic countries (NordicWelfAir)”. Hoek G, Krishnan RM, Beelen R, Peters A, Ostro B, Brunekreef B, et al. (2013). Long-term air pollution exposure and cardio- respiratory mortality: a review. Environ Health, 12, 43. Raaschou-Nielsen O, Palmgren F, Jensen S, Wåhlin P, Berkowicz R, Hertel O, et al. (2002). Helbredseffekter af partikulær luftforurening i Danmark - et forsøg på kvantificering. Ugeskrift for Læger, 164, 3959–63.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bønløkke, Jakob Hjort","Andersen, Mikael Skou","Brandt, Jørgen","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Geels, Camilla","Hansen, Kaj Mantzius","Hertel, Ole","Im, Ulas","Jensen, Steen Solvang","Ketzel, Matthias","Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","Sigsgaard, Torben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-155225"],"event":{"end":"2016-04-04","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2016-04-04","title":"NOSA 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an update on mortality in denmark caused by fine particulate matter air pollution","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/110210479/Poster_NOSA.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-155225","ids":["au-2d4519a8-0b77-4278-acba-1d5a535b9614"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-38A0ECCCA6D5A55CCFB51A894D5A1DA1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/110210479/Poster_NOSA.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Institute of Environmental and Occupational Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Hjort","key":"bønløkkepau","last":"Bønløkke","locid":"70b350dc-20d7-416b-a44f-71fbc646fc00","name":"Bønløkke, Jakob Hjort","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikael Skou","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"d6eb07fd-3020-4801-9beb-04c0cc0f0914","name":"Andersen, Mikael Skou","orcid":"0000-0003-2299-8134","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaj Mantzius","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"85f79280-93e9-4d5f-aaec-c245958a6b24","name":"Hansen, Kaj Mantzius","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hertelpau","last":"Hertel","locid":"6a33f2b3-9140-4f59-a55e-e68a73c9fa32","name":"Hertel, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-0972-7735","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulas","key":"impau","last":"Im","locid":"e2356d82-8e7b-49c9-b660-76e719a4058e","name":"Im, Ulas","orcid":"0000-0001-5177-5306","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Solvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"0d52f91a-4eaa-46f9-ab5f-d7fd3c31440d","name":"Jensen, Steen Solvang","orcid":"0000-0001-5923-8441","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole-Kenneth","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"17ec76bb-7916-4024-867b-3aca60ca0c40","name":"Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","orcid":"0000-0003-4350-0956","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marlene Schmidt","key":"plejdruppau","last":"Plejdrup","locid":"9dede80b-ff3e-4171-9504-bf8547fec74d","name":"Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"sigsgaardpau","last":"Sigsgaard","locid":"5d7f5dc8-00ea-48ba-9467-a93703b015b7","name":"Sigsgaard, Torben","orcid":"0000-0002-2043-7571","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2d4519a8-0b77-4278-acba-1d5a535b9614"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"An update on mortality in Denmark caused by fine particulate matter air pollution","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-155225","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Most real-world optimization problems are of a multi-objective nature, involving objectives which are conflicting and incomparable. Solving a multi-objective optimization problem requires a method which can generate the set of rational compromises between the objectives. In this paper, we propose two distinct bound set based branch-and-cut algorithms for bi-objective combinatorial optimization problems, based on implicitly and explicitly stated lower bound sets, respectively. The algorithm based on explicitly given lower bound sets computes for each branching node a lower bound set and compares it to an upper bound set. The implicit bound set based algorithm, on the other hand, fathoms branching nodes by generating a single point on the lower bound set for each local nadir point. We outline several approaches for fathoming branching nodes and we propose an updating scheme for the lower bound sets that prevents us from solving the bi-objective LP-relaxation of each branching node. To strengthen the lower bound sets, we propose a bi-objective cutting plane algorithm that dynamically adjusts the weights of the objective functions such that different parts of the feasible set are strengthened by cutting planes. In addition, we suggest an extension of the branching strategy \"Pareto branching''. Extensive computational results obtained for the bi-objective single source capacitated facility location problem prove the effectiveness of the algorithms.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Gadegaard, Sune Lauth","Ehrgott, Matthias","Nielsen, Lars Relund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-259111"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lancaster University"],"keyword":["Bi objective optimization","Branch and cut","Combinatorial optimization","bi objective branch and cut"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bi objective branch and cut algorithms applications to the single source capacitated facility location problem","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.optimization-online.org/DB_HTML/2016/04/5402.html","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-259111","ids":["au-e35445b7-f840-402e-bb48-c361968530cb"],"keyword":["bi-objective branc-and-cut","bi-objective branch-and-cut","bi-objective optimization","branch-and-cut","combinatorial optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-158C84299CED2FE1D149BB404D0A1212"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.optimization-online.org/DB_HTML/2016/04/5402.html","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Economics and Business Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"lancaster university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Lancaster University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sune Lauth","key":"gadegaardpau","last":"Gadegaard","locid":"7ea17dde-2cf6-4a20-bea7-25434eeb984d","name":"Gadegaard, Sune Lauth","orcid":"0000-0001-8989-6015","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"ehrgottpau","last":"Ehrgott","name":"Ehrgott, Matthias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Relund","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5