8-4be4-a1d8-433cd15873f5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Residential exposure to traffic noise and risk of incident atrial fibrillation : A cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.88-004707","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Recent developments in information and communication technology have advanced the connectivity of cities, both in terms of scope and efficiency. The connected nature of a city is one of the key characteristics of the concept of a smart city; a modern city whose urban growth is fueled by technology, infrastructure, and an emphasis on social and educational capital. Such growth affects the physical and social landscape of a city, and both the tangible and intangible heritage of a city is threatened by these changing landscapes. At the same time, new technology brings with it potential new methods for the preservation of a city’s threatened heritage. The present paper aims to place a city’s heritage in the context of a smart city, and how it is affected by such urban development. Using Aalborg in Denmark as a case study, this paper presents a potential way to use recent technological advancements to transfer the preservation of a city’s heritage from its museums to the urban environment.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Damgård, Mathias","Nielsen, Emil","van Heijster, Seth","Rodil, Kasper","Rehm, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-053458"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-19","place":"Kyoto, jp","start":"2015-10-17","title":"International Conference on Culture and Computing 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Intangible Cultural Heritage","Mobile learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preserving heritage through technology in a city undergoing change","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://ai.soc.i.kyoto-u.ac.jp/culture2015/paper.html","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-053458","identifier":[{"id":"84964917396","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0bb6f7ae-8efd-4b26-b4e5-8e022b22d339"],"keyword":["Intangible Cultural Heritage","mobile learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-11363CB2927F5342B84FEB05683BE1AA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathias","key":"damgårdpau","last":"Damgård","locid":"b84fda35-5dfb-4a8e-9bfc-b401016bbe5e","name":"Damgård, Mathias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Emil","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e55db751-2e47-4bbd-b3c9-604de5875b04","name":"Nielsen, Emil","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Seth","key":"vanheijsterpau","last":"van Heijster","locid":"8dbddca3-0341-4dfa-b119-f2d3effb6ffe","name":"van Heijster, Seth","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"rodilpau","last":"Rodil","locid":"43295420-1fb5-48c4-b8cb-e6fb3c72503f","name":"Rodil, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-6737-7342","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"rehmpau","last":"Rehm","locid":"04553c36-2327-4e8d-8d3c-701b04cb2d77","name":"Rehm, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-6264-1688","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/culture.and.computing.2015.34","isbn":["9781467382328"],"pages":"183-186","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society Press","status":"p","title":"Culture and Computing 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964917396"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0bb6f7ae-8efd-4b26-b4e5-8e022b22d339"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Preserving Heritage Through Technology in a City Undergoing Change","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-053458","year":"2015","yearsub":"2016"}
