{"abstract":"Intrinsically disordered proteins can phase separate from the soluble intracellular space, and tend to aggregate under pathological conditions. The physiological functions and molecular triggers of liquid demixing by phase separation are not well understood. Here we show in vitro and in vivo that the nucleic acid-mimicking biopolymer poly(ADP-ribose) (PAR) nucleates intracellular liquid demixing. PAR levels are markedly induced at sites of DNA damage, and we provide evidence that PAR-seeded liquid demixing results in rapid, yet transient and fully reversible assembly of various intrinsically disordered proteins at DNA break sites. Demixing, which relies on electrostatic interactions between positively charged RGG repeats and negatively charged PAR, is amplified by aggregation-prone prion-like domains, and orchestrates the earliest cellular responses to DNA breakage. We propose that PAR-seeded liquid demixing is a general mechanism to dynamically reorganize the soluble nuclear space with implications for pathological protein aggregation caused by derailed phase separation.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Altmeyer, Matthias","Neelsen, Kai John","Teloni, Federico","Pozdnyakova, Irina","Pellegrino, Stefania","Grøfte, Merete","Rask, Maj-Britt Druedahl","Streicher, Werner","Jungmichel, Stephanie","Nielsen, Michael L.","Lukas, Jiri"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-511919"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"liquid demixing of intrinsically disordered proteins is seeded by poly adp ribose","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms9088","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-511919","identifier":[{"id":"84939825873","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26286827","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4560800","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-c67d2b99-00a0-4649-ad0b-7bb616910b6f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-39B6737365C7213DD8014B222BADD09C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms9088","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Protein Signaling Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"altmeyerpau","last":"Altmeyer","locid":"5ce7801d-8725-4cbc-a842-c42504725ed0","name":"Altmeyer, Matthias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kai J","key":"neelsenpau","last":"Neelsen","locid":"c028a7e4-aa87-438f-a872-5a17f11eb450","name":"Neelsen, Kai John","name_org":"Neelsen, Kai J","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Federico","key":"telonipau","last":"Teloni","name":"Teloni, Federico","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Irina","key":"pozdnyakovapau","last":"Pozdnyakova","locid":"5aed9639-c923-486b-9c4e-24f28fc1850c","name":"Pozdnyakova, Irina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefania","key":"pellegrinopau","last":"Pellegrino","name":"Pellegrino, Stefania","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Merete","key":"grøftepau","last":"Grøfte","name":"Grøfte, Merete","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maj-Britt Druedahl","key":"raskpau","last":"Rask","name":"Rask, Maj-Britt Druedahl","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Werner","key":"streicherpau","last":"Streicher","locid":"be9be2b9-30e1-4eac-9ec4-20eafa6ee3d2","name":"Streicher, Werner","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stephanie","key":"jungmichelpau","last":"Jungmichel","locid":"555451a4-8ef2-41bd-aab4-e24fad88a9c1","name":"Jungmichel, Stephanie","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Lund","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b72d98f7-79fa-43a7-8066-783ed8034146","name":"Nielsen, Michael L.","name_org":"Nielsen, Michael Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-0067-9039","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jiri","key":"lukaspau","last":"Lukas","locid":"d13249de-fd5d-4494-a642-4f416727a417","name":"Lukas, Jiri","orcid":"0000-0001-9087-506X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26286827"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ncomms9088","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","pages":"1-12","paperid":"8088","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84939825873"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c67d2b99-00a0-4649-ad0b-7bb616910b6f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Liquid demixing of intrinsically disordered proteins is seeded by poly(ADP-ribose)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-511919","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a novel approach AffinityViz to visualize live and aggregated consumption data from multistory buildings. The objective of the approach is to provide a generic but high affinity relation between real buildings' spatial layouts and the consumption data visualizations. Current approaches come short on maintaining such affinity. This implies an avoidable cognitive load on users such as energy managers and facility managers who need to monitor consumption and make decisions from consumption data. To alleviate this we have transformed three conventional types of visualizations into highly affine visualizations lowering the cognitive load for users. The contributions are: 1) Development of the AffinityViz techniques featuring three generic designs of highly affine visualizations of consumption data. 2) Comparison of the affine visualizations with the conventional visualizations. 3) Initial evaluation of the AffinityViz designs by expert users on real world data. Finally, the design challenges of AffinityViz are discussed, including prospects for AffinityViz as a future tool for visual analysis of data from buildings.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Matthias","Grønbæk, Kaj"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-221066"],"event":{"acronym":"IVAPP","end":"2015-03-14","place":"Berlin, de","start":"2015-03-11","title":"International Conference on Information Visualization Theory and Applications","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards highly affine visualizations of consumption data from buildings","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84938797384","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-221066","identifier":[{"id":"84938797384","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a0fe224c-e39a-44b8-b0c5-955f3e38f6dc"],"keyword":["Energy management support","Interactive visual analytics","Spatial visualizations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5EEA301BA5634784BCC8BF202D0BAA5D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"790b96d1-cd52-41e3-84ae-cd5a795fb3dc","name":"Nielsen, Matthias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaj","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"c7b908c7-ad69-4b60-bfb2-f6d7f490bb4f","name":"Grønbæk, Kaj","orcid":"0000-0002-3752-6714","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789897580888"],"pages":"247-255","publisher":"SCITEPRESS Digital Library","status":"p","title":"IVAPP 2015 - 6th International Conference on Information Visualization Theory and Applications; VISIGRAPP, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84938797384"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a0fe224c-e39a-44b8-b0c5-955f3e38f6dc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Towards highly affine visualizations of consumption data from buildings","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-221066","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Exposure to traffic noise may result in stress and sleep disturbances, which may impair the immune system. People with weakened immune systems are known to have a higher risk for non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL). We aimed to determine whether traffic noise was associated with risk for NHL. We identified 2,753 cases aged 30-84 years with a primary diagnosis of NHL in Denmark between 1992 and 2010. For each case we selected two random population controls, matched on sex and year of birth. Road traffic noise was calculated for all present and historical residential addresses of cases and controls from 1987 to 2010. Associations between traffic noise and risk for NHL were estimated using conditional logistic regression, adjusted for socioeconomic position. We found a 5-year time-weighted mean of road traffic noise above 65 dB to be associated with an 18% higher risk for NHL (95% confidence interval (CI) 1.01-1.37) when compared to road traffic noise below 55 dB, whereas for exposure between 55 and 65 dB no association was found. In analyses of NHL subtypes, we found no association between road traffic noise and risk for T-cell lymphoma, whereas increased risks for B-cell lymphoma and unspecified lymphomas were observed at exposures above 65 dB. In conclusion, our nationwide study may indicate that high exposure to traffic noise is associated with higher risk for NHL.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sørensen, Mette","Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Ketzel, Matthias","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","Friis, Søren","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-227714"],"event":{"end":"2015-06-03","place":"Maastricht, nl","start":"2015-06-01","title":"10th European Congress and Exposition on Noise Control Engineering, Euronoise 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"road traffic noise and risk for non hodgkin lymphoma among adults","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85076203650","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-227714","identifier":[{"id":"85076203650","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ac8a72de-4fb5-4866-a064-17f44ddfd98a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E09F84A3E0BD40E7C3103D037F46AD97"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne Oksbjerg","key":"daltonpau","last":"Dalton","name":"Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","name":"Friis, Søren","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"99-104","status":"p","title":"Euronoise 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ac8a72de-4fb5-4866-a064-17f44ddfd98a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Road traffic noise and risk for non-Hodgkin lymphoma among adults","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-227714","year":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Previous studies have suggested that polymorphisms in CASP8 on chromosome 2 are associated with breast cancer risk. To clarify the role of CASP8 in breast cancer susceptibility, we carried out dense genotyping of this region in the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC). Single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) spanning a 1 Mb region around CASP8 were genotyped in 46 450 breast cancer cases and 42 600 controls of European origin from 41 studies participating in the BCAC as part of a custom genotyping array experiment (iCOGS). Missing genotypes and SNPs were imputed and, after quality exclusions, 501 typed and 1232 imputed SNPs were included in logistic regression models adjusting for study and ancestry principal components. The SNPs retained in the final model were investigated further in data from nine genome-wide association studies (GWAS) comprising in total 10 052 case and 12 575 control subjects. The most significant association signal observed in European subjects was for the imputed intronic SNP rs1830298 in ALS2CR12 (telomeric to CASP8), with per allele odds ratio and 95% confidence interval [OR (95% confidence interval, CI)] for the minor allele of 1.05 (1.03-1.07), P = 1 × 10(-5). Three additional independent signals from intronic SNPs were identified, in CASP8 (rs36043647), ALS2CR11 (rs59278883) and CFLAR (rs7558475). The association with rs1830298 was replicated in the imputed results from the combined GWAS (P = 3 × 10(-6)), yielding a combined OR (95% CI) of 1.06 (1.04-1.08), P = 1 × 10(-9). Analyses of gene expression associations in peripheral blood and normal breast tissue indicate that CASP8 might be the target gene, suggesting a mechanism involving apoptosis.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Lin, Wei-Yu","Camp, Nicola J","Ghoussaini, Maya","Beesley, Jonathan","Michailidou, Kyriaki","Hopper, John L","Apicella, Carmel","Southey, Melissa C","Stone, Jennifer","Schmidt, Marjanka K","Broeks, Annegien","Van't Veer, Laura J","Th Rutgers, Emiel J","Muir, Kenneth","Lophatananon, Artitaya","Stewart-Brown, Sarah","Siriwanarangsan, Pornthep","Fasching, Peter A","Haeberle, Lothar","Ekici, Arif B","Beckmann, Matthias W","Peto, Julian","Dos-Santos-Silva, Isabel","Fletcher, Olivia","Johnson, Nichola","Bolla, Manjeet K","Wang, Qin","Dennis, Joe","Sawyer, Elinor J","Cheng, Timothy","Tomlinson, Ian","Kerin, Michael J","Miller, Nicola","Marmé, Frederik","Surowy, Harald M","Burwinkel, Barbara","Guénel, Pascal","Truong, Thérèse","Menegaux, Florence","Mulot, Claire","Bojesen, Stig E","Nordestgaard, Børge G","Nielsen, Sune F","Flyger, Henrik","Benitez, Javier","Zamora, M Pilar","Arias Perez, Jose Ignacio","Menéndez, Primitiva","González-Neira, Anna","Pita, Guillermo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-526487"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["GENICA Network"],"keyword":["Breast Neoplasms","CASP8 and FADD Like Apoptosis Regulating Protein","Case Control Studies","Caspase 8","Chromosomes Human Pair 2","European Continental Ancestry Group","Female","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome Wide Association Study","Genotyping Techniques","Humans","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","Proteins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification and characterization of novel associations in the i casp000000000008 als000000000002cr000000000012 i region on chromosome 000000000002 with breast cancer risk","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-526487","identifier":[{"id":"25168388","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84927610980","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4334820","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-debb9e8e-00bc-4cc3-ba1f-93a591c6583b"],"keyword":["Breast Neoplasms","CASP8 and FADD-Like Apoptosis Regulating Protein","Case-Control Studies","Caspa