{"abstract":"Chromosome breakage elicits transient silencing of ribosomal RNA synthesis, but the mechanisms involved remained elusive. Here we discover an in trans signalling mechanism that triggers pan-nuclear silencing of rRNA transcription in response to DNA damage. This is associated with transient recruitment of the Nijmegen breakage syndrome protein 1 (NBS1), a central regulator of DNA damage responses, into the nucleoli. We further identify TCOF1 (also known as Treacle), a nucleolar factor implicated in ribosome biogenesis and mutated in Treacher Collins syndrome, as an interaction partner of NBS1, and demonstrate that NBS1 translocation and accumulation in the nucleoli is Treacle dependent. Finally, we provide evidence that Treacle-mediated NBS1 recruitment into the nucleoli regulates rRNA silencing in trans in the presence of distant chromosome breaks.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Larsen, Dorthe Helena","Hari, Flurina","Clapperton, Julie A","Gwerder, Myriam","Gutsche, Katrin","Altmeyer, Matthias","Jungmichel, Stephanie","Toledo, Luis","Fink, Daniel","Rask, Maj-Britt","Grøfte, Merete","Lukas, Claudia","Nielsen, Michael L.","Smerdon, Stephen J","Lukas, Jiri","Stucki, Manuel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-422590"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Zurich"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["MRC National Institute of Medical Research, Division of Protein Structure, The Ridgeway, Mill Hill, London NW7 1AA, UK."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the nbs000000000001 treacle complex controls ribosomal rna transcription in response to dna damage","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb3007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-422590","identifier":[{"id":"84905510594","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4962910","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"25064736","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-30ef3b15-0a81-4d66-8b9d-7698c914c206"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E387BE6895C7760A31A765180C86B8B3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb3007","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Protein Signaling Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"university of zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Zurich","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["MRC National Institute of Medical Research, Division of Protein Structure, The Ridgeway, Mill Hill, London NW7 1AA, UK."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Dorthe H","key":"larsendorthehelenapau","last":"Larsen","locid":"827e7754-61b7-4fa3-a93b-b86bbcb982d1","name":"Larsen, Dorthe Helena","name_org":"Larsen, Dorthe H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Flurina","key":"hariflurinapau","last":"Hari","name":"Hari, Flurina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Julie A","key":"clappertonjulieapau","last":"Clapperton","name":"Clapperton, Julie A","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Myriam","key":"gwerdermyriampau","last":"Gwerder","name":"Gwerder, Myriam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Katrin","key":"gutschekatrinpau","last":"Gutsche","name":"Gutsche, Katrin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"altmeyermatthiaspau","last":"Altmeyer","locid":"5ce7801d-8725-4cbc-a842-c42504725ed0","name":"Altmeyer, Matthias","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stephanie","key":"jungmichelstephaniepau","last":"Jungmichel","locid":"555451a4-8ef2-41bd-aab4-e24fad88a9c1","name":"Jungmichel, Stephanie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Luis Ignacio","key":"toledoluispau","last":"Toledo Lazaro","locid":"ddeb1448-348d-4549-a723-4ede5a4f7057","name":"Toledo, Luis","name_org":"Toledo Lazaro, Luis Ignacio","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Daniel","key":"finkdanielpau","last":"Fink","name":"Fink, Daniel","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maj-Britt","key":"raskmajbrittpau","last":"Rask","name":"Rask, Maj-Britt","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Merete","key":"grøftemeretepau","last":"Grøfte","name":"Grøfte, Merete","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claudia","key":"lukasclaudiapau","last":"Lukas","locid":"4b038f1c-a5dc-46d1-95bc-486c0872225e","name":"Lukas, Claudia","orcid":"0000-0001-7169-6883","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael L","key":"nielsenmichaellpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b72d98f7-79fa-43a7-8066-783ed8034146","name":"Nielsen, Michael L.","name_org":"Nielsen, Michael L","orcid":"0000-0002-0067-9039","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Stephen J","key":"smerdonstephenjpau","last":"Smerdon","name":"Smerdon, Stephen J","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jiri","key":"lukasjiripau","last":"Lukas","locid":"d13249de-fd5d-4494-a642-4f416727a417","name":"Lukas, Jiri","orcid":"0000-0001-9087-506X","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Manuel","key":"stuckimanuelpau","last":"Stucki","name":"Stucki, Manuel","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25064736"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ncb3007","issn":["14657392","14764679"],"issn_org":["14657392"],"issue":"8","journal":"Nature Cell Biology","pages":"792-803","status":"p","title":"Nature Cell Biology","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905510594"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-30ef3b15-0a81-4d66-8b9d-7698c914c206"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The NBS1-Treacle complex controls ribosomal RNA transcription in response to DNA damage","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-422590","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"A comparison of synthetic aperture imaging using spherical and plane waves with low number of emission events is presented. For both wave types, a 90 degree sector is insonified using 15 emission events giving a frame rate of 200 frames per second. Field II simulations of point targets show similar resolution of approximately one wavelength radially and one degree angularly for both wave types. The use of spherical waves is found to have higher signal strength and better cystic resolution than plane waves. Measurements on wires in water yield similar results to simulations with similar resolution between the two wave types but better cystic resolution for spherical waves. Mea- surements on tissue mimicking phantoms show that both wave types penetrate down to 11 cm. Intensity measurements show an I spta: 3 of 18.4 mW/cm 2 for spherical waves and 22.7 mW/cm 2 for plane waves. The derated MI is 0.43 for spherical and 0.70 for plane waves. All measures are well within FDA limits for cardiac imaging. In-vivo images of the heart of a healthy 28-year old volunteer are shown.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Stuart, Matthias Bo","Jensen, Jonas","Brandt, Andreas Hjelm","Nikolov, Svetoslav","Nielsen, Michael Bachman","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S02-086.94-035081"],"event":{"end":"2014-09-06","place":"Chicago, us","start":"2014-09-03","title":"2014 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium, IUS 2014","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in vivo synthetic aperture and plane wave high frame rate cardiac imaging","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/99355802/mbs_et_al_2014_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-086.94-035081","identifier":[{"id":"84910092495","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6c6c6b8b-a910-4ff8-9a64-a5e3a766ad4d","ku-e73831e9-f7d2-4854-9791-34fe454d4a20"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-214D59C0230C23935A875DF03A332EE3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/99355802/mbs_et_al_2014_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ULTSYM.2014.0298","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["BK Medical ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartmatthiasbopau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"jensenjonaspau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ce6e719b-4e0f-4795-a9ac-91265cc918a8","name":"Jensen, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0003-4456-0838","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Hjelm","key":"brandtandreashjelmpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Andreas Hjelm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Svetoslav","key":"nikolovsvetoslavpau","last":"Nikolov","name":"Nikolov, Svetoslav","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Svetoslav Ivanov","key":"nikolovsvetoslavivanovpau","last":"Nikolov","name":"Nikolov, Svetoslav Ivanov","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenmichaelbachmannpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Bachman","key":"nielsenmichaelbachmanpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachman","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenjørgenarendtpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ultsym.2014.0298","eisbn":["9781479970490"],"isbn":["978170490"],"issn":["19485719"],"pages":"1209-1212","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society Press","series":"IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium, IUS","status":"p","title":"IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium, IUS"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84910092495"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","bk medical","bk medical aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6c6c6b8b-a910-4ff8-9a64-a5e3a766ad4d","ku-e73831e9-f7d2-4854-9791-34fe454d4a20"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"In-Vivo Synthetic Aperture and Plane Wave High Frame Rate Cardiac Imaging","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.94-035081","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Exposure to traffic noise may result in stress and sleep disturbances. Studies on self-reported sleep duration and breast cancer risk have found inconsistent results. In a population-based Danish cohort of 29,875 women aged 50-64 years at enrolment in 1993-1997, we identified 1219 incident, postmenopausal breast cancer cases during follow-up through 2010. Mean follow-up time was 12.3 years. Road traffic and railway noise was calculated for all present and historical residential addresses from 1987 to 2010. We used Cox proportional hazard model for analyses and adjusted for hormone replacement therapy use, parity, alcohol consumption and other potential confounders. We found no overall association between residential road traffic or railway noise and breast cancer risk. Among women with estrogen receptor negative breast cancer, a 10-dB higher level of road traffic noise (continuous scale) during the previous 1, 5 and 10 years were associated with 28% (95% CI: 1.04-1.56), 23% (95% CI: 1.00-1.51) and 20% (95% CI: 0.97-1.48) higher risks of estrogen receptor negative breast cancer, respectively, in fully adjusted models. Similarly, a 10-dB increase in railway noise (1-year mean at diagnosis address) increased risk for estrogen receptor negative breast cancer by 38% (95% CI: 1.01-1.89). There was no association between road traffic or railway noise and estrogen receptor positive breast cancer. In conclusion, these results suggest that residential road traffic and railway noise may increase risk of estrogen receptor negative breast cancer. As the first study on traffic noise and breast cancer results should be treated with caution.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Sørensen, Mette","Ketzel, Matthias","Overvad, Kim","Tjønneland, Anne","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-182127"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exposure to road traffic and railway noise and postmenopausal breast cancer a cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.28592","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-182127","identifier":[{"id":"24338235","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84896394547","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5c87dc23-9227-4acf-aaa3-cef8f69d88e7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7004284AF68B04B882BE5173C5CE5EC9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.28592","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","