{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Heymann, Matthias","Nielsen, Kristian Hvidtfelt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-264893"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fæstning grønland videnskab og teknologi under den kolde krig","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://online.fliphtml5.com/xsvh/eaqy/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-264893","ids":["au-ed8a4b1a-2f52-4ca9-8b33-734016ee370c"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-838353AA3ED9B3CB383F3148BE5FFEC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://online.fliphtml5.com/xsvh/eaqy/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Mathematics, Department of Mathematics - Science Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"heymannpau","last":"Heymann","locid":"debefba8-67c0-46e8-aebe-17efb00c6254","name":"Heymann, Matthias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian Hvidtfelt","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b3e227f2-dc63-4a9b-b77f-efdc7798c83f","name":"Nielsen, Kristian Hvidtfelt","orcid":"0000-0002-6192-400X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["13957961"],"journal":"Carlsbergfondet. Aarsskrift","pages":"46-49","status":"p","title":"Carlsbergfondet. Aarsskrift"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ed8a4b1a-2f52-4ca9-8b33-734016ee370c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Fæstning Grønland : Videnskab og teknologi under den kolde krig","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-264893","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Over 40 susceptibility loci have been identified for type 1 diabetes (T1D). Little is known about how these variants modify disease risk and progression. Here, we combined in vitro and in vivo experiments with clinical studies to determine how genetic variation of the candidate gene cathepsin H (CTSH) affects disease mechanisms and progression in T1D. The T allele of rs3825932 was associated with lower CTSH expression in human lymphoblastoid cell lines and pancreatic tissue. Proinflammatory cytokines decreased the expression of CTSH in human islets and primary rat β-cells, and overexpression of CTSH protected insulin-secreting cells against cytokine-induced apoptosis. Mechanistic studies indicated that CTSH exerts its antiapoptotic effects through decreased JNK and p38 signaling and reduced expression of the proapoptotic factors Bim, DP5, and c-Myc. CTSH overexpression also up-regulated Ins2 expression and increased insulin secretion. Additionally, islets from Ctsh(-/-) mice contained less insulin than islets from WT mice. Importantly, the TT genotype was associated with higher daily insulin dose and faster disease progression in newly diagnosed T1D patients, indicating agreement between the experimental and clinical data. In line with these observations, healthy human subjects carrying the T allele have lower β-cell function, which was evaluated by glucose tolerance testing. The data provide strong evidence that CTSH is an important regulator of β-cell function during progression of T1D and reinforce the concept that candidate genes for T1D may affect disease progression by modulating survival and function of pancreatic β-cells, the target cells of the autoimmune assault.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Fløyel, Tina","Brorsson, Caroline","Nielsen, Lotte B","Miani, Michela","Bang-Berthelsen, Claus Heiner","Friedrichsen, Martin","Overgaard, Anne Julie","Berchtold, Lukas Adrian","Wiberg, Anna","Poulsen, Pernille","Hansen, Lars","Rosinger, Silke","Boehm, Bernhard O","Ram, Ramesh","Nguyen, Quang","Mehta, Munish","Morahan, Grant","Concannon, Patrick","Bergholdt, Regine","Nielsen, Jens Høiriis","Reinheckel, Thomas","von Herrath, Matthias","Vaag, Allan","Eizirik, Decio Laks","Mortensen, Henrik B","Størling, Joachim","Pociot, Flemming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-544088"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Free University of Brussels","Imperial College London","Ulm University","University of California at San Diego","University of Florida","University of Freiburg","University of Western Australia"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ctsh regulates β cell function and disease progression in newly diagnosed type 000000000001 diabetes patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1402571111","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-544088","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4104872","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24982147","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84904353328","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-fc5f11cb-d7e1-4129-acff-547f874f8cd9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-28277D81F34BE797191D6A3C8DB5AFE9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1402571111","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yea