{"abstract":"Poly(ADP-ribos)ylation (PARylation) is a reversible posttranslational modification found in higher eukaryotes. However, little is known about PARylation acceptor proteins. Here, we describe a sensitive proteomics approach based on high-accuracy quantitative mass spectrometry for the identification of PARylated proteins induced under different cellular stress conditions. While confirming the majority of known PARylated substrates, our screen identifies numerous additional PARylation targets. In vivo and in vitro validation of acceptor proteins confirms that our methodology targets covalent PARylation. Nuclear proteins encompassing nucleic acid binding properties are prominently PARylated upon genotoxic stress, consistent with the nuclear localization of ARTD1/PARP1 and ARTD2/PARP2. Distinct differences in proteins becoming PARylated upon various genotoxic insults are observed, exemplified by the PARylation of RNA-processing factors THRAP3 and TAF15 under oxidative stress. High-content imaging reveals that PARylation affects the nuclear relocalization of THRAP3 and TAF15, demonstrating the potential of our approach to uncover hitherto unappreciated processes being controlled by specific genotoxic-stress-induced PARylation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jungmichel, Stephanie","Rosenthal, F.","Altmeyer, Matthias","Lukas, Jiri","Hottiger, M.O.","Nielsen, Michael L."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-500398"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Zurich"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proteome wide identification of poly adp ribosyl ation targets in different genotoxic stress responses","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molcel.2013.08.026","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-500398","identifier":[{"id":"84886246082","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24055347","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b3174c7d-fdcc-47e9-b18c-d91d3dfcc39b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1F11176071853461891BC29D37EA0F57"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molcel.2013.08.026","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Proteomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"university of zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Zurich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"S.","key":"jungmichelpau","last":"Jungmichel","locid":"555451a4-8ef2-41bd-aab4-e24fad88a9c1","name":"Jungmichel, Stephanie","name_org":"Jungmichel, S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"F.","key":"rosenthalpau","last":"Rosenthal","name":"Rosenthal, F.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"M.","key":"altmeyerpau","last":"Altmeyer","locid":"5ce7801d-8725-4cbc-a842-c42504725ed0","name":"Altmeyer, Matthias","name_org":"Altmeyer, M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J.","key":"lukaspau","last":"Lukas","locid":"d13249de-fd5d-4494-a642-4f416727a417","name":"Lukas, Jiri","name_org":"Lukas, J.","orcid":"0000-0001-9087-506X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"M.O.","key":"hottigerpau","last":"Hottiger","name":"Hottiger, M.O.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"M.L.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b72d98f7-79fa-43a7-8066-783ed8034146","name":"Nielsen, Michael L.","name_org":"Nielsen, M.L.","orcid":"0000-0002-0067-9039","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24055347"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.molcel.2013.08.026","issn":["10972765","10974164"],"issn_org":["10972765"],"issue":"2","journal":"Molecular Cell","pages":"272-285","status":"p","title":"Molecular Cell","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84886246082"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b3174c7d-fdcc-47e9-b18c-d91d3dfcc39b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Proteome-wide Identification of Poly(ADP-Ribosyl)ation Targets in Different Genotoxic Stress Responses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-500398","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We lack an understanding of human values, motivations and behavior in regards to new means for changing people’s behavior towards more sustainable choices in their everyday life. Previous anthropological and sociological studies have identified these objects of study to be quite complex and to require new methods to be unfolded further. Especially behavior within the privacy of people’s homes has proven challenging to uncover through the use of traditional qualitative and quantitative social scientific methods (e.g. interviews, participatory observations and questionnaires). Furthermore, many research experiments are attempting to motivate environmental improvements through feedback via, e.g., room displays, web pages or smart phones, based on (smart) metering of energy usage, or for saving energy by automatic control of, e.g., heating, lighting or appliances. However, existing evaluation methods are primarily unilateral by opting for either a quantitative or a qualitative method or for a simple combination—and therefore do not provide detailed insight into the potentials and impacts of such solutions. This paper therefore proposes a combined quantitative and qualitative collective sensing and anthropologic investigation methodology we term Computational Environmental Ethnography, which provides quantitative sensing data that document behavior while facilitating qualitative investigations to link the data to explanations and ideas for further sensing. We propose this methodology to include the establishment of base lines, comparative experimental feedback, traceable sensor data with respect for different privacy levels, visualization of sensor data, qualitative explanations of recurrent and exceptional patterns in sensor data, taking place as part of an innovative process and in an iterative interplay among complementing disciplines, potentially including also partners from industry. Experiences from using the methodology in a zero-emission home setting, as well as an ongoing case investigating transportation habits are discussed.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Blunck, Henrik","Bouvin, Niels Olof","Entwistle, Johanne Mose","Grønbæk, Kaj","Kjærgaard, Mikkel Baun","Nielsen, Matthias","Petersen, Marianne Graves","Rasmussen, Majken Kirkegård","Wüstenberg, Markus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-189234"],"event":{"acronym":"e-Energy","end":"2013-05-24","place":"us","start":"2013-05-22","title":"International Conference onFuture Energy Systems","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computational environmental ethnography combining collective sensing and ethnographic inquiries to advance means for reducing environmental footprints","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/60271476/p8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-189234","identifier":[{"id":"84878663739","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-68e421ec-8646-4f4c-bc49-8a66b3f6295a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BDB57FD09A8E9B88C044D4BDBEFE4B45"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=2487176","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/60271476/p8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2487166.2487176","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"blunckpau","last":"Blunck","locid":"f35b0c0b-39c5-46f9-b6e8-05c3ae8a11b9","name":"Blunck, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Olof","key":"bouvinpau","last":"Bouvin","locid":"a100614b-adba-4dfe-9ada-8df77bfed841","name":"Bouvin, Niels Olof","orcid":"0000-0001-8421-4951","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Johanne Mose","key":"entwistlepau","last":"Entwistle","locid":"13b5e0cb-16c5-4679-b422-66e34dbe190f","name":"Entwistle, Johanne Mose","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaj","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"c7b908c7-ad69-4b60-bfb2-f6d7f490bb4f","name":"Grønbæk, Kaj","orcid":"0000-0002-3752-6714","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Baun","key":"kjærgaardpau","last":"Kjærgaard","locid":"70d0ef0a-bd07-45e6-a496-6654d8565606","name":"Kjærgaard, Mikkel Baun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"790b96d1-cd52-41e3-84ae-cd5a795fb3dc","name":"Nielsen, Matthias","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne Graves","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"da3161f7-ece7-471a-af07-f05e91059d3a","name":"Petersen, Marianne Graves","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Majken","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","loc