rnal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-209788","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The three-dimensional (3-D) Transverse Oscillation (TO) method is used to obtain 3-D velocity vector estimates in two orthogonal planes. The method is suitable for a real-time implementation. Data are acquired using a Vermon 3.0 MHz 32x32 element 2-D phased array and the experimental ultrasound scanner SARUS. Measurements are conducted on a carotid artery flow phantom from Danish Phantom Design, and 20 frames are acquired with a constant flow rate of 16.7±0.17 mL/s provided by a Shelley Medical Imaging Technologies CompuFlow 1000 system. The peak velocity magnitude in the vessel is found to be 52.3±8.1 m/s compared to an expected peak velocity of 53.6±0.54 cm/s. Based on the out-of-plane velocity component in the crosssectional plane, the estimated volumetric flow rates are 17.1±1.4 mL/s. The coefficient of variation is 8.3%, and the bias is 2.2%. An in vivo measurement of 3-D M-mode velocities is conducted over five heart beats. The peak systolic and end-diastolic velocities are 69±5.4 cm/s and 7.9±5.5 cm/s at the center of the vessel. For comparison, a commercial BK Medical ultrasound scanner using the spectral estimator yields 71.2 cm/s and 7.70 cm/s, respectively. The results demonstrate that the 3-D TO method can estimate 3-D velocities in two crossed planes, volumetric flow rates, and 3-D velocities in vivo.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Pihl, Michael Johannes","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev","Hansen, Peter Møller","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-372266"],"event":{"end":"2013-07-25","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2013-07-21","title":"2013 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in vivo three dimensional velocity vector imaging and volumetric flow rate measurements","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/56779262/prod21374325086079.pihl_et_al_ieee_ius_2013_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-372266","identifier":[{"id":"84894376558","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e27fccb1-392a-4ec0-9442-c98959eeb2af"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DADC9664406BA7F53281B95555639304"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/56779262/prod21374325086079.pihl_et_al_ieee_ius_2013_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Johannes","key":"pihlpau","last":"Pihl","locid":"efb04be2-6e73-4643-94c3-5b37126d55b0","name":"Pihl, Michael Johannes","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias Bo",