{"abstract":"Perioperative optimization of spatially resolved near-infrared spectroscopy determined cerebral frontal lobe oxygenation (scO2) may reduce postoperative morbidity. Norepinephrine is routinely administered to maintain cerebral perfusion pressure and, thereby, cerebral blood flow, but norepinephrine reduces the scO2. We hypothesized that norepinephrine-induced reduction in scO2 is influenced by cutaneous vasoconstriction.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Holm-Sørensen, Henrik","Secher, Niels H.","Siebenmann, Christoph","Nielsen, Henning M Bay","Kohl-Bareis, Matthias","Lundby, Carsten","Rasmussen, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-507084"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Zurich"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cutaneous vasoconstriction affects near infrared spectroscopy determined cerebral oxygen saturation during administration of norepinephrine","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-507084","identifier":[{"id":"22739762","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84864279167","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-be70162f-0823-4349-94ea-2dcde2231506"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C7D24C8EFD24B56B34D35129D02D2B5E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"university of zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Zurich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"holmsørensenpau","last":"Holm-Sørensen","name":"Holm-Sørensen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Niels H.","key":"secherpau","last":"Secher","locid":"fc54cecb-0c67-47bd-b27f-1e0127af0e4d","name":"Secher, Niels H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christoph","key":"siebenmannpau","last":"Siebenmann","name":"Siebenmann, Christoph","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henning M Bay","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Henning M Bay","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Matthias","key":"kohlbareispau","last":"Kohl-Bareis","name":"Kohl-Bareis, Matthias","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Carsten","key":"lundbypau","last":"Lundby","name":"Lundby, Carsten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22739762"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/aln.0b013e3182605afe","issn":["00033022","15281175"],"issn_org":["00033022"],"issue":"2","journal":"Anesthesiology","pages":"263-270","status":"p","title":"Anesthesiology","volume":"117"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84864279167"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-be70162f-0823-4349-94ea-2dcde2231506"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cutaneous vasoconstriction affects near-infrared spectroscopy determined cerebral oxygen saturation during administration of norepinephrine","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-507084","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Staphylococcus aureus is a serious human pathogen that employs a number of virulence factors as part of its pathogenesis. The purpose of the present study was to explore marine bacteria as a source of compounds that modulate virulence gene expression in S. aureus. During the global marine Galathea 3 expedition, a strain collection was established comprising bacteria that express antimicrobial activity against Vibrio anguillarum and/or Staphylococcus aureus. Within this collection we searched colony material, culture supernatants, and cell extracts for virulence modulating activity showing that 68 out of 83 marine bacteria (affiliated with the Vibrionaceae and Pseudoalteromonas sp.) influenced expression of S. aureus hla encoding α-hemolysin toxin and/or spa encoding Protein A. The isolate that upon initial screening showed the highest degree of interference (crude ethyl acetate extract) was a Vibrio nigripulchritudo. Extraction, purification and structural elucidation revealed a novel siderophore, designated nigribactin, which induces spa transcription. The effect of nigribactin on spa expression is likely to be independent from its siderophore activity, as another potent siderophore, enterobactin, failed to influence S. aureus virulence gene expression. This study shows that marine microorganisms produce compounds with potential use in therapeutic strategies targeting virulence rather than viability of human pathogens.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Anita","Månsson, Maria","Wietz, Matthias","Varming, Anders N.","Phipps, Richard Kerry","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","Gram, Lone","Ingmer, Hanne"],"cuid":["S02-096.49-035191"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biology and Life Sciences","Health sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nigribactin a novel siderophore from em vibrio nigripulchritudo em modulates em staphylococcus aureus em virulence gene expression","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/35965052/1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.49-035191","identifier":[{"id":"23203279","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84870044179","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3509537","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-71b23243-cb2c-4480-80ee-d1e15f0fc9e8","ku-de66333f-4319-452f-a6da-285c9ae35d57"],"keyword":["Biology and Life Sciences","Health Sciences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7CF48339DDD4935436F4BDEC0DC1A903"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/35965052/1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/md10112584","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Anita","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"96d76fb7-da68-4592-a02f-dd0e980bfef1","name":"Nielsen, Anita","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria","key":"månssonpau","last":"Månsson","locid":"b544bec6-c495-4e6d-8b22-b1a749699479","name":"Månsson, Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"wietzpau","last":"Wietz","locid":"f8928597-cfad-401a-84d2-07faf1cbbda3","name":"Wietz, Matthias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Nissen","key":"varmingpau","last":"Varming","locid":"e0705a41-239f-47ec-9a75-5d21a1793f55","name":"Varming, Anders Nissen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard Kerry","key":"phippspau","last":"Phipps","locid":"0b506225-97e7-4d90-98bd-204a50c0cb91","name":"Phipps, Richard Kerry","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Ostenfeld","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"bd958d52-71b6-4720-b30a-cc9305633b43","name":"Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3362-5707","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lone","key":"grampau","last":"Gram","locid":"9fabd1ae-e28f-4a5d-8456-7a075b4aa34e","name":"Gram, Lone","orcid":"0000-0002-1076-5723","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne","key":"ingmerpau","last":"Ingmer","locid":"abe2cd31-84e7-4f06-81a3-33e08bf93b8f","name":"Ingmer, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0002-8350-5631","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23203279"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/md10112584","issn":["16603397"],"issue":"11","journal":"Marine Drugs","pages":"2584-2595","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Marine Drugs","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84870044179"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-71b23243-cb2c-4480-80ee-d1e15f0fc9e8","ku-de66333f-4319-452f-a6da-285c9ae35d57"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nigribactin, a Novel Siderophore from Vibrio nigripulchritudo, Modulates Staphylococcus aureus Virulence Gene Expression","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.49-035191","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Although there has been much success in identifying genetic variants associated with common diseases using genome-wide association studies (GWAS), it has been difficult to demonstrate which variants are causal and what role they have in disease. Moreover, the modest contribution that these variants make to disease risk has raised questions regarding their medical relevance. Here we have investigated a single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) in the TNFRSF1A gene, that encodes tumour necrosis factor receptor 1 (TNFR1), which was discovered through GWAS to be associated with multiple sclerosis (MS), but not with other autoimmune conditions such as rheumatoid arthritis, psoriasis and Crohn’s disease. By analysing MS GWAS data in conjunction with the 1000 Genomes Project data we provide genetic evidence that strongly implicates this SNP, rs1800693, as the causal variant in the TNFRSF1A region. We further substantiate this through functional studies showing that the MS risk allele directs expression of a novel, soluble form of TNFR1 that can block TNF. Importantly, TNF-blocking drugs can promote onset or exacerbation of MS, but they have proven highly efficacious in the treatment of autoimmune diseases for which there is no association with rs1800693. This indicates that the clinical experience with these drugs parallels the disease association of rs1800693, and that the MS-associated TNFR1 variant mimics the effect of TNF-blocking drugs. Hence, our study demonstrates that clinical practice can be informed by comparing GWAS across common autoimmune diseases and by investigating the functional consequences of the disease-associated genetic variation.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Gregory, Adam P","Dendrou, Calliope A","Attfield, Kathrine E","Haghikia, Aiden","Xifara, Dionysia K","Butter, Falk","Poschmann, Gereon","Kaur, Gurman","Lambert, Lydia","Leach, Oliver A","Prömel, Simone","Punwani, Divya","Felce, James H","Davis, Simon J","Gold, Ralf","Nielsen, Finn C","Siegel, Richard M","Mann, Matthias","Bell, John I","McVean, Gil","Fugger, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-028057"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Alleles","Exons","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome Human","Genome Wide Association Study","Genomics","Genotype","Great Britain","Humans","Multiple sclerosis","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","RNA Splicing","Receptors Tumor Necrosis Factor Type I","Solubility","Tumor Necrosis Factor alpha"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tnf receptor 000000000001 genetic risk mirrors outcome of anti tnf therapy in multiple sclerosis","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11307","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-028057","identifier":[{"id":"22801493","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4268493","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84865261493","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d4ae8393-7eeb-4dc5-afa6-100c7efcfd01","ku-eb006576-269c-402d-966b-0ef6d70b3203"],"keyword":["Alleles","Exons","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome, Human","Genome-Wide Association Study","Genomics","Genotype","Great Britain","Humans","Multiple Sclerosis","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","RNA Splicing","Receptors, Tumor Necrosis Factor, Type I","Solubility","Tumor Necrosis Factor-alpha"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FF2B9DB6F7C7533A6D83317EFDC75F33"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11307","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Mis