{"abstract":"Over the past two decades, continuous flow analysis (CFA) systems have been refined and widely used to measure aerosol constituents in polar and alpine ice cores in very high-depth resolution. Here we present a newly designed system consisting of sodium, ammonium, dust particles, and electrolytic meltwater conductivity detection modules. The system is optimized for high- resolution determination of transient signals in thin layers of deep polar ice cores. Based on standard measurements and by comparing sections of early Holocene and glacial ice from Greenland, we find that the new system features a depth resolution in the ice of a few millimeters which is considerably better than other CFA systems. Thus, the new system can resolve ice strata down to 10 mm thickness and has the potential of identifying annual layers in both Greenland and Antarctic ice cores throughout the last glacial cycle.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bigler, Matthias","Svensson, Anders","Kettner, Ernesto","Vallelonga, Paul","Nielsen, Maibritt","Steffensen, Jørgen Peder"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-537030"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimization of high resolution continuous flow analysis for transient climate signals in ice cores","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/es200118j","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-537030","identifier":[{"id":"79952136924","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21504155","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f0a4ac2c-70a1-4a6f-8bb3-eec3e5441c60"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FA87318C19A85B11EBDFB389AE03E2DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/es200118j","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/es200118j","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Physics of Ice, Climate and Earth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Matthias","key":"biglerpau","last":"Bigler","locid":"2714d296-3b40-421f-b5b1-a3a783f462e0","name":"Bigler, Matthias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"e0501b84-a817-417e-9c70-9601c6b26cb8","name":"Svensson, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-4364-6085","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ernesto","key":"kettnerpau","last":"Kettner","locid":"03a9f668-a59c-4385-9601-d5566b9ccac0","name":"Kettner, Ernesto","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Paul Travis","key":"vallelongapau","last":"Vallelonga","locid":"51df0666-60ac-46fe-8fdd-ae4ab41f3fef","name":"Vallelonga, Paul","name_org":"Vallelonga, Paul Travis","orcid":"0000-0003-1055-7235","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maibritt","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Maibritt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen Peder","key":"steffensenpau","last":"Steffensen","locid":"688738da-b41f-4ff3-bb45-9870e6db5c7e","name":"Steffensen, Jørgen Peder","orcid":"0000-0002-5516-1093","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21504155"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/es200118j","issn":["0013936X","15205851"],"issn_org":["0013936X"],"issue":"10","journal":"Environmental Science & Technology","pages":"4483-4489","status":"p","title":"Environmental Science & Technology","title_org":"Environmental Science & Technology (Washington)","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79952136924"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f0a4ac2c-70a1-4a6f-8bb3-eec3e5441c60"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Optimization of High-Resolution Continuous Flow Analysis for Transient Climate Signals in Ice Cores","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-537030","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The Greenland NGRIP ice core continuously covers the period from present day back to 123 ka before present, which includes several thousand years of ice from the previous interglacial period, MIS 5e or the Eemian. In the glacial part of the core, annual layers can be identified from impurity records and visual stratigraphy, and stratigraphic layer counting has been performed back to 60 ka. In the deepest part of the core, however, the ice is close to the pressure melting point, the visual stratigraphy is dominated by crystal boundaries, and annual layering is not visible to the naked eye. In this study, we apply a newly developed setup for high-resolution ice core impurity analysis to produce continuous records of dust, sodium and ammonium concentrations as well as conductivity of melt water. We analyzed three 2.2m sections of ice from the Eemian and the glacial inception. In all of the analyzed ice, annual layers can clearly be recognized, most prominently in the dust and conductivity profiles. Part of the samples is, however, contaminated in dust, most likely from drill liquid. It is interesting that the annual layering is preserved despite a very active crystal growth and grain boundary migration in the deep and warm NGRIP ice. Based on annual layer counting of the new records, we determine a mean annual layer thickness close to 11mm for all three sections, which, to first order, confirms the modeled NGRIP time scale (ss09sea). The counting does, however, suggest a longer duration of the climatically warmest part of the NGRIP record (MIS5e) of up to 1 ka as compared to the model estimate. Our results suggest that stratigraphic layer counting is possible basically throughout the entire NGRIP ice core, provided sufficiently highly-resolved profiles become available.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Svensson, Anders","Bigler, Matthias","Kettner, Ernesto","Dahl-Jensen, Dorthe","Johnsen, Sigfus Johann","Kipfstuhl, Sepp","Nielsen, Maibritt","Steffensen, Jørgen Peder"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-539625"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["Alfred-Wegener-Institut, Wattenmeerstation Sylt","All Global Affiliations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"annual layering in the ngrip ice core during the eemian","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-539625","identifier":[{"id":"84255187182","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f4ecd0ad-2d98-4614-94e1-dc9d1ba1d801"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24F417C0BC3848A951475604D1DEADB0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Physics of Ice, Climate and Earth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"alfred wegener institut wattenmeerstation sylt","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Alfred-Wegener-Institut, Wattenmeerstation Sylt","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"e0501b84-a817-417e-9c70-9601c6b26cb8","name":"Svensson, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-4364-6085","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"biglerpau","last":"Bigler","locid":"2714d296-3b40-421f-b5b1-a3a783f462e0","name":"Bigler, Matthias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ernesto","key":"kettnerpau","last":"Kettner","locid":"03a9f668-a59c-4385-9601-d5566b9ccac0","name":"Kettner, Ernesto"