{"abstract":"In most European countries the ethnic minority migrant populations are currently reaching an age where dementia becomes an increasingly important issue. There is no European consensus on good clinical practice with these patient groups, who often have special needs and expectations with regard to dementia services.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, T Rune","Vogel, Asmus","Riepe, Matthias W","de Mendonça, Alexandre","Rodriguez, Guido","Nobili, Flavio","Gade, Anders","Waldemar, Gunhild"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-469890"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessment of dementia in ethnic minority patients in europe a european alzheimer s disease consortium survey","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S1041610210000955","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-469890","identifier":[{"id":"20602861","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79951671985","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7fb46078-0162-4095-bddd-04c80fa5d123"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-E72C9F62CE7170E87B51B1DA027F7B83"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S1041610210000955","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Neurology, Psychiatry and Sensory Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"T Rune","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, T Rune","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Asmus","key":"vogelpau","last":"Vogel","locid":"91459149-dc91-4c80-bab6-6d843284ca57","name":"Vogel, Asmus","orcid":"0000-0002-3401-1061","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthias W","key":"riepepau","last":"Riepe","name":"Riepe, Matthias W","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexandre","key":"demendonçapau","last":"de Mendonça","name":"de Mendonça, Alexandre","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Guido","key":"rodriguezpau","last":"Rodriguez","name":"Rodriguez, Guido","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Flavio","key":"nobilipau","last":"Nobili","name":"Nobili, Flavio","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"gadepau","last":"Gade","locid":"d275da50-7603-4fc3-90c8-01f34197d626","name":"Gade, Anders","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gunhild","key":"waldemarpau","last":"Waldemar","locid":"becd5a62-33b3-405e-8c6e-36a9578512d6","name":"Waldemar, Gunhild","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["20602861"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s1041610210000955","issn":["10416102","1741203X"],"issn_org":["10416102"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Psychogeriatrics","pages":"86-95","status":"p","title":"International Psychogeriatrics","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79951671985"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7fb46078-0162-4095-bddd-04c80fa5d123"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Assessment of dementia in ethnic minority patients in Europe: a European Alzheimer's Disease Consortium survey","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-469890","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"RATIONALE: Short-term exposure to air pollution has been associated with exacerbation of chronic obstructive respiratory disease (COPD) whereas the role of long-term exposures on the development of COPD is not yet fully understood. OBJECTIVES: We assessed the effect of exposure to traffic-related air pollution over 35 years on the incidence of COPD in a prospective cohort study. MEASUREMENTS: We followed 57 053 participants in the Danish Diet, Cancer and Health cohort in the Hospital Discharge Register for their first hospital admission for COPD between 1993 and 2006. We estimated the annual mean levels of nitrogen dioxide (NO2) and nitrogen oxides (NOx) at all residential addresses of the cohort participants since 1971 to an event or 2006 and used indicators of traffic near the residential address at recruitment. We assessed the association between exposure to air pollution and COPD incidence by Cox regression analyses for the full cohort, and for participants with and without co-morbid conditions including asthma, diabetes, or cardiovascular disease. MAIN RESULTS: A first hospital admission for COPD was recorded for 1 786 (3.4%) of 52 799 eligible subjects between recruitment (1993-1997) and 2006. COPD incidence was associated with the 35-year mean NO2 level (hazard ratio 1.08; 95% confidence interval 1.02-1.14, per interquartile range of 5.8 µg/m(3)), with stronger associations in subjects with diabetes (1.29; 1.05-1.60) and asthma (1.19; 1.03-1.38). CONCLUSIONS: Long-term exposure to traffic related air pollution may contribute to the development of COPD with possibly enhanced susceptibility in people with diabetes and asthma.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Andersen, Zorana J","Hvidberg, Martin","Jensen, Steen Solvang","Ketzel, Matthias","Loft, Steffen","Sørensen, Mette","Tjønneland, Anne","Overvad, Kim","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-091.28-024774"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Air Pollutants","Air pollution","Asthma","Causality","Cohort Studies","Comorbidity","Denmark","Diabetes mellitus","Environmental Exposure","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Incidence","Male","Middle Aged","Nitrogen dioxide","Nitrogen oxides","Prospective Studies","Pulmonary Disease Chronic Obstructive","Risk Factors","Vehicle Emissions"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and long term exposure to traffic related air pollution a cohort study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1164/rccm.201006-0937OC","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-091.28-024774","identifier":[{"id":"79951820583","type":"scopus"},{"id":"20870755","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-a5802790-cbb6-11df-8cb9-000ea68e967b","ku-c8eb5ead-3d83-4adc-a10b-f0d0f37721bc"],"keyword":["Air Pollutants","Air Pollution","Asthma","Causality","Cohort Studies","Comorbidity","Denmark","Diabetes Mellitus","Environmental Exposure","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Incidence","Male","Middle Aged","Nitrogen Dioxide","Nitrogen Oxides","Prospective Studies","Pulmonary Disease, Chronic Obstructive","Risk Factors","Vehicle Emissions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-183B3AED00BF0CACFD1FEEFAD50A14C0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1164/rccm.201006-0937OC","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Environmental Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Kardiovaskulært Forskningscenter, Aalborg Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Zorana J","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Zorana J","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"hvidbergpau","last":"Hvidberg","locid":"caad0d45-bf3a-4a5f-ae85-b78a367b5186","name":"Hvidberg, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen S","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"0d52f91a-4eaa-46f9-ab5f-d7fd3c31440d","name":"Jensen, Steen Solvang","name_org":"Jensen, Steen S","orcid":"0000-0001-5923-8441","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Steffen","key":"loftpau","last":"Loft","locid":"cc94a7fc-b397-47b4-94a5-bde078bb4fb6","name":"Loft, Steffen","o