{"abstract":"During a global research expedition, more than five hundred marine bacterial strains capable of inhibiting the growth of pathogenic bacteria were collected. The purpose of the present study was to determine if these marine bacteria are also a source of compounds that interfere with the agr quorum sensing system that controls virulence gene expression in Staphylococcus aureus. Using a gene reporter fusion bioassay, we recorded agr interference as enhanced expression of spa, encoding Protein A, concomitantly with reduced expression of hla, encoding α-hemolysin, and rnaIII encoding RNAIII, the effector molecule of agr. A marine Photobacterium produced compounds interfering with agr in S. aureus strain 8325-4, and bioassay-guided fractionation of crude extracts led to the isolation of two novel cyclodepsipeptides, designated solonamide A and B. Northern blot analysis confirmed the agr interfering activity of pure solonamides in both S. aureus strain 8325-4 and the highly virulent, community-acquired strain USA300 (CA-MRSA). To our knowledge, this is the first report of inhibitors of the agr system by a marine bacterium.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Månsson, Maria","Nielsen, Anita","Kjærulff, Louise","Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","Wietz, Matthias","Ingmer, Hanne","Gram, Lone","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-036542"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inhibition of virulence gene expression in em staphylococcus aureus em by novel depsipeptides from a marine em photobacterium em","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6309618/prod21323336324627.M_nsson-etal_2011MarDrugs_solonamide.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-036542","identifier":[{"id":"80053311236","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22363239","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3280567","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-ae662566-35c2-490a-b412-bd4556642c39","ku-77cc6718-1d43-49df-8639-e51a05af533c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B17C3862917F14C022473AA2A1E60CD6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/md9122537","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6309618/prod21323336324627.M_nsson-etal_2011MarDrugs_solonamide.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Microbiology